window.EM_TR = {"battle-of-gonzales":{"es":{"The Battle of Gonzales":"La batalla de Gonzales","Decide whether a small skirmish over a cannon — the 'Come and Take It' fight of October 2, 1835 — was truly the turning point that began the Texas Revolution.":"Decide si una pequeña escaramuza por un cañón —la lucha de 'Come and Take It' ('Ven y tómalo') del 2 de octubre de 1835— fue realmente el punto de inflexión que inició la Revolución de Texas.","On October 2, 1835, Texian colonists at Gonzales refused to hand a small cannon back to Mexican soldiers and fired on them instead, under a homemade flag reading 'Come and Take It.' Almost no one was hurt — so why do historians call this the turning point that began the Texas Revolution? Map what led up to it and what changed afterward.":"El 2 de octubre de 1835, los colonos texianos de Gonzales se negaron a devolver un pequeño cañón a los soldados mexicanos y en su lugar dispararon contra ellos, bajo una bandera casera que decía 'Come and Take It' ('Ven y tómalo'). Casi nadie resultó herido, entonces ¿por qué los historiadores llaman a esto el punto de inflexión que inició la Revolución de Texas? Traza lo que condujo a este suceso y lo que cambió después.","Battle of Gonzales ('Come and Take It')":"Batalla de Gonzales ('Come and Take It' / 'Ven y tómalo')","Gonzales, Texas":"Gonzales, Texas","Compare your before-and-after with a partner. Did you agree on what changed most?":"Compara tu antes y después con un compañero. ¿Estuvieron de acuerdo en lo que más cambió?","Which pressure do you think mattered most in pushing events toward a fight?":"¿Cuál presión crees que fue la más importante para empujar los acontecimientos hacia un enfrentamiento?","Was the Battle of Gonzales truly a turning point? Use evidence from at least two sources to argue what changed after it that could not be undone.":"¿Fue la batalla de Gonzales realmente un punto de inflexión? Usa evidencia de al menos dos fuentes para argumentar qué cambió después de ella que no pudo deshacerse.","Explain what happened at Gonzales and why the colonists refused to return the cannon.":"Explica qué sucedió en Gonzales y por qué los colonos se negaron a devolver el cañón.","Connect Santa Anna's shift to centralism to the colonists' decision to fight.":"Relaciona el giro de Santa Anna hacia el centralismo con la decisión de los colonos de luchar.","Apply the idea of a small event with big consequences to another moment in history.":"Aplica la idea de un pequeño acontecimiento con grandes consecuencias a otro momento de la historia.","Gonzales, Battle of — Handbook of Texas Online (TSHA)":"Gonzales, batalla de — Handbook of Texas Online (TSHA)","The Texas State Historical Association's entry on the opening battle of the Revolution.":"La entrada de la Texas State Historical Association sobre la batalla que abrió la Revolución.","What was the dispute really about?":"¿De qué se trataba realmente la disputa?","Why was it important even though few were hurt?":"¿Por qué fue importante aunque pocos resultaron heridos?","Gonzales 'Come and Take It' Cannon — Handbook of Texas Online (TSHA)":"El cañón de Gonzales 'Come and Take It' ('Ven y tómalo') — Handbook of Texas Online (TSHA)","The story of the loaned cannon and the 'Come and Take It' flag made by the women of Gonzales.":"La historia del cañón prestado y de la bandera 'Come and Take It' ('Ven y tómalo') hecha por las mujeres de Gonzales.","Why did the colonists care so much about one small cannon?":"¿Por qué les importaba tanto a los colonos un solo cañón pequeño?","What did the flag's message mean?":"¿Qué significaba el mensaje de la bandera?","First shots of the Texas Revolution fired in the Battle of Gonzales (HISTORY)":"Los primeros disparos de la Revolución de Texas se hicieron en la batalla de Gonzales (HISTORY)","A short account of the skirmish and its minimal casualties.":"Un breve relato de la escaramuza y sus mínimas bajas.","How many people were hurt in the fight?":"¿Cuántas personas resultaron heridas en la lucha?","How can an event be important without being big?":"¿Cómo puede un acontecimiento ser importante sin ser grande?","Anglo colonists and Tejanos lived fairly autonomously in Mexican Texas under the 1824 federal constitution; Gonzales kept a small cannon, loaned in 1831, for defense against raids.":"Los colonos angloamericanos y los tejanos vivían con bastante autonomía en el Texas mexicano bajo la constitución federal de 1824; Gonzales conservaba un pequeño cañón, prestado en 1831, para defenderse de las incursiones.","Santa Anna shifted Mexico toward centralism, dismantling the 1824 federal system and alarming Texans; Colonel Ugartechea demanded the loaned Gonzales cannon back, and the colonists refused.":"Santa Anna llevó a México hacia el centralismo, desmantelando el sistema federal de 1824 y alarmando a los texanos; el coronel Ugartechea exigió la devolución del cañón prestado de Gonzales, y los colonos se negaron.","Texian militia crossed the Guadalupe River at dawn and fired on Lt. Castañeda's dragoons rather than surrender the cannon — the first shots of the Texas Revolution.":"La milicia texiana cruzó el río Guadalupe al amanecer y disparó contra los dragones del teniente Castañeda en lugar de entregar el cañón: los primeros disparos de la Revolución de Texas.","Castañeda withdrew toward San Antonio de Béxar empty-handed; 'Come and Take It' became a rallying cry; volunteers streamed to Gonzales.":"Castañeda se retiró hacia San Antonio de Béxar con las manos vacías; 'Come and Take It' ('Ven y tómalo') se convirtió en un grito de guerra; los voluntarios acudieron en masa a Gonzales.","The gathering force marched on Béxar (captured December 1835); delegates convened the Consultation, moving Texas toward the 1836 declaration of independence.":"La fuerza que se reunía marchó sobre Béxar (capturada en diciembre de 1835); los delegados convocaron la Consulta (Consultation), llevando a Texas hacia la declaración de independencia de 1836.","Gonzales colonists and DeWitt-colony militia (the 'Old Eighteen' and John Henry Moore), determined to keep the cannon.":"Los colonos de Gonzales y la milicia de la colonia DeWitt (los 'Old Eighteen' / 'Viejos Dieciocho' y John Henry Moore), decididos a conservar el cañón.","Mexican centralist authorities — Colonel Ugartechea and Lt. Castañeda, ordered to recover the cannon.":"Las autoridades centralistas mexicanas: el coronel Ugartechea y el teniente Castañeda, con la orden de recuperar el cañón.","Castañeda was ordered to avoid a fight; had he pressed the attack, or had colonists complied, revolution might have been delayed or sparked elsewhere.":"A Castañeda se le ordenó evitar un enfrentamiento; si hubiera insistido en el ataque, o si los colonos hubieran cedido, la revolución podría haberse retrasado o haber estallado en otro lugar.","Why do historians call a small skirmish with almost no casualties the 'turning point' that began the Texas Revolution? What changed after Gonzales that could not be undone?":"¿Por qué los historiadores llaman a una pequeña escaramuza con casi ninguna baja el 'punto de inflexión' que inició la Revolución de Texas? ¿Qué cambió después de Gonzales que no pudo deshacerse?"},"vi":{"The Battle of Gonzales":"Trận Gonzales","Decide whether a small skirmish over a cannon — the 'Come and Take It' fight of October 2, 1835 — was truly the turning point that began the Texas Revolution.":"Hãy quyết định xem một cuộc giao tranh nhỏ vì một khẩu đại bác — trận 'Come and Take It' ('Đến mà lấy đi') ngày 2 tháng 10 năm 1835 — có thực sự là bước ngoặt khởi đầu cuộc Cách mạng Texas hay không.","On October 2, 1835, Texian colonists at Gonzales refused to hand a small cannon back to Mexican soldiers and fired on them instead, under a homemade flag reading 'Come and Take It.' Almost no one was hurt — so why do historians call this the turning point that began the Texas Revolution? Map what led up to it and what changed afterward.":"Ngày 2 tháng 10 năm 1835, những người khai hoang Texian ở Gonzales từ chối trả lại một khẩu đại bác nhỏ cho lính Mexico và thay vào đó đã nổ súng vào họ, dưới một lá cờ tự làm ghi dòng chữ 'Come and Take It' ('Đến mà lấy đi'). Hầu như không ai bị thương — vậy tại sao các nhà sử học lại gọi đây là bước ngoặt khởi đầu cuộc Cách mạng Texas? Hãy phác họa những gì dẫn đến sự kiện này và những gì đã thay đổi sau đó.","Battle of Gonzales ('Come and Take It')":"Trận Gonzales ('Come and Take It' / 'Đến mà lấy đi')","Gonzales, Texas":"Gonzales, Texas","Compare your before-and-after with a partner. Did you agree on what changed most?":"So sánh phần trước-và-sau của em với một bạn. Các em có đồng ý với nhau về điều gì đã thay đổi nhiều nhất không?","Which pressure do you think mattered most in pushing events toward a fight?":"Em nghĩ áp lực nào là quan trọng nhất trong việc đẩy các sự kiện tiến tới một cuộc chiến?","Was the Battle of Gonzales truly a turning point? Use evidence from at least two sources to argue what changed after it that could not be undone.":"Trận Gonzales có thực sự là một bước ngoặt không? Hãy dùng bằng chứng từ ít nhất hai nguồn để lập luận điều gì đã thay đổi sau đó mà không thể đảo ngược được.","Explain what happened at Gonzales and why the colonists refused to return the cannon.":"Hãy giải thích điều gì đã xảy ra ở Gonzales và tại sao những người khai hoang từ chối trả lại khẩu đại bác.","Connect Santa Anna's shift to centralism to the colonists' decision to fight.":"Hãy liên hệ việc Santa Anna chuyển sang chế độ tập quyền trung ương với quyết định chiến đấu của những người khai hoang.","Apply the idea of a small event with big consequences to another moment in history.":"Hãy áp dụng ý tưởng về một sự kiện nhỏ nhưng có hậu quả lớn vào một thời khắc khác trong lịch sử.","Gonzales, Battle of — Handbook of Texas Online (TSHA)":"Gonzales, Trận — Handbook of Texas Online (TSHA)","The Texas State Historical Association's entry on the opening battle of the Revolution.":"Mục từ của Texas State Historical Association về trận đánh mở màn cuộc Cách mạng.","What was the dispute really about?":"Cuộc tranh chấp thực sự là về điều gì?","Why was it important even though few were hurt?":"Tại sao nó lại quan trọng dù rất ít người bị thương?","Gonzales 'Come and Take It' Cannon — Handbook of Texas Online (TSHA)":"Khẩu đại bác 'Come and Take It' ('Đến mà lấy đi') ở Gonzales — Handbook of Texas Online (TSHA)","The story of the loaned cannon and the 'Come and Take It' flag made by the women of Gonzales.":"Câu chuyện về khẩu đại bác được cho mượn và lá cờ 'Come and Take It' ('Đến mà lấy đi') do những người phụ nữ ở Gonzales làm ra.","Why did the colonists care so much about one small cannon?":"Tại sao những người khai hoang lại coi trọng một khẩu đại bác nhỏ đến vậy?","What did the flag's message mean?":"Thông điệp trên lá cờ có ý nghĩa gì?","First shots of the Texas Revolution fired in the Battle of Gonzales (HISTORY)":"Những phát súng đầu tiên của cuộc Cách mạng Texas được bắn ra trong Trận Gonzales (HISTORY)","A short account of the skirmish and its minimal casualties.":"Một bản tường thuật ngắn gọn về cuộc giao tranh và số thương vong tối thiểu của nó.","How many people were hurt in the fight?":"Có bao nhiêu người bị thương trong cuộc chiến?","How can an event be important without being big?":"Làm thế nào một sự kiện có thể quan trọng mà không cần phải to lớn?","Anglo colonists and Tejanos lived fairly autonomously in Mexican Texas under the 1824 federal constitution; Gonzales kept a small cannon, loaned in 1831, for defense against raids.":"Những người khai hoang gốc Anh và người Tejano sống khá tự trị ở vùng Texas thuộc Mexico theo hiến pháp liên bang năm 1824; Gonzales giữ một khẩu đại bác nhỏ, được cho mượn năm 1831, để phòng thủ chống lại các cuộc đột kích.","Santa Anna shifted Mexico toward centralism, dismantling the 1824 federal system and alarming Texans; Colonel Ugartechea demanded the loaned Gonzales cannon back, and the colonists refused.":"Santa Anna đưa Mexico chuyển sang chế độ tập quyền trung ương, phá bỏ hệ thống liên bang năm 1824 và khiến người Texas lo ngại; Đại tá Ugartechea đòi trả lại khẩu đại bác đã cho Gonzales mượn, và những người khai hoang từ chối.","Texian militia crossed the Guadalupe River at dawn and fired on Lt. Castañeda's dragoons rather than surrender the cannon — the first shots of the Texas Revolution.":"Dân quân Texian vượt sông Guadalupe vào lúc bình minh và nổ súng vào đội kỵ binh của Trung úy Castañeda thay vì giao nộp khẩu đại bác — những phát súng đầu tiên của cuộc Cách mạng Texas.","Castañeda withdrew toward San Antonio de Béxar empty-handed; 'Come and Take It' became a rallying cry; volunteers streamed to Gonzales.":"Castañeda rút lui về San Antonio de Béxar tay không; 'Come and Take It' ('Đến mà lấy đi') trở thành khẩu hiệu tập hợp; các tình nguyện viên đổ về Gonzales.","The gathering force marched on Béxar (captured December 1835); delegates convened the Consultation, moving Texas toward the 1836 declaration of independence.":"Lực lượng đang tập hợp tiến quân về Béxar (bị chiếm vào tháng 12 năm 1835); các đại biểu triệu tập Hội nghị Tham vấn (Consultation), đưa Texas tiến tới tuyên ngôn độc lập năm 1836.","Gonzales colonists and DeWitt-colony militia (the 'Old Eighteen' and John Henry Moore), determined to keep the cannon.":"Những người khai hoang ở Gonzales và dân quân của khu định cư DeWitt (nhóm 'Old Eighteen' / 'Mười tám người cũ' và John Henry Moore), quyết tâm giữ lại khẩu đại bác.","Mexican centralist authorities — Colonel Ugartechea and Lt. Castañeda, ordered to recover the cannon.":"Chính quyền tập quyền Mexico — Đại tá Ugartechea và Trung úy Castañeda, được lệnh thu hồi khẩu đại bác.","Castañeda was ordered to avoid a fight; had he pressed the attack, or had colonists complied, revolution might have been delayed or sparked elsewhere.":"Castañeda được lệnh tránh giao chiến; nếu ông ta cứ tiếp tục tấn công, hoặc nếu những người khai hoang chịu tuân theo, thì cuộc cách mạng có thể đã bị trì hoãn hoặc bùng nổ ở nơi khác.","Why do historians call a small skirmish with almost no casualties the 'turning point' that began the Texas Revolution? What changed after Gonzales that could not be undone?":"Tại sao các nhà sử học lại gọi một cuộc giao tranh nhỏ với hầu như không có thương vong là 'bước ngoặt' khởi đầu cuộc Cách mạng Texas? Điều gì đã thay đổi sau Gonzales mà không thể đảo ngược được?"},"ar":{"The Battle of Gonzales":"معركة غونزاليس","Decide whether a small skirmish over a cannon — the 'Come and Take It' fight of October 2, 1835 — was truly the turning point that began the Texas Revolution.":"قرّر ما إذا كانت مناوشة صغيرة حول مدفع — معركة 'Come and Take It' ('تعالَ وخذه') في 2 أكتوبر 1835 — كانت حقًا نقطة التحول التي بدأت ثورة تكساس.","On October 2, 1835, Texian colonists at Gonzales refused to hand a small cannon back to Mexican soldiers and fired on them instead, under a homemade flag reading 'Come and Take It.' Almost no one was hurt — so why do historians call this the turning point that began the Texas Revolution? Map what led up to it and what changed afterward.":"في 2 أكتوبر 1835، رفض المستوطنون التكسيون في غونزاليس إعادة مدفع صغير إلى الجنود المكسيكيين وأطلقوا النار عليهم بدلًا من ذلك، تحت راية مصنوعة يدويًا كُتب عليها 'Come and Take It' ('تعالَ وخذه'). لم يُصَب أحد تقريبًا — فلماذا يسمّي المؤرخون هذا نقطة التحول التي بدأت ثورة تكساس؟ ارسم خريطة لما أدى إليه وما تغيّر بعده.","Battle of Gonzales ('Come and Take It')":"معركة غونزاليس ('Come and Take It' / 'تعالَ وخذه')","Gonzales, Texas":"غونزاليس، تكساس","Compare your before-and-after with a partner. Did you agree on what changed most?":"قارن ما قبل وما بعد الخاص بك مع زميل. هل اتفقتما على ما تغيّر أكثر؟","Which pressure do you think mattered most in pushing events toward a fight?":"أيّ ضغط تعتقد أنه كان الأهم في دفع الأحداث نحو القتال؟","Was the Battle of Gonzales truly a turning point? Use evidence from at least two sources to argue what changed after it that could not be undone.":"هل كانت معركة غونزاليس نقطة تحول حقًا؟ استخدم أدلة من مصدرين على الأقل لتبرهن ما الذي تغيّر بعدها ولم يكن بالإمكان التراجع عنه.","Explain what happened at Gonzales and why the colonists refused to return the cannon.":"اشرح ما الذي حدث في غونزاليس ولماذا رفض المستوطنون إعادة المدفع.","Connect Santa Anna's shift to centralism to the colonists' decision to fight.":"اربط تحوّل سانتا آنا نحو المركزية بقرار المستوطنين بالقتال.","Apply the idea of a small event with big consequences to another moment in history.":"طبّق فكرة حدث صغير ذي عواقب كبيرة على لحظة أخرى في التاريخ.","Gonzales, Battle of — Handbook of Texas Online (TSHA)":"غونزاليس، معركة — Handbook of Texas Online (TSHA)","The Texas State Historical Association's entry on the opening battle of the Revolution.":"مدخل جمعية تكساس التاريخية (Texas State Historical Association) حول المعركة الافتتاحية للثورة.","What was the dispute really about?":"حول ماذا كان النزاع في حقيقته؟","Why was it important even though few were hurt?":"لماذا كان مهمًا رغم أن قلة قليلة أُصيبت؟","Gonzales 'Come and Take It' Cannon — Handbook of Texas Online (TSHA)":"مدفع غونزاليس 'Come and Take It' ('تعالَ وخذه') — Handbook of Texas Online (TSHA)","The story of the loaned cannon and the 'Come and Take It' flag made by the women of Gonzales.":"قصة المدفع المُعار وراية 'Come and Take It' ('تعالَ وخذه') التي صنعتها نساء غونزاليس.","Why did the colonists care so much about one small cannon?":"لماذا اهتم المستوطنون كثيرًا بمدفع صغير واحد؟","What did the flag's message mean?":"ماذا كانت تعني رسالة الراية؟","First shots of the Texas Revolution fired in the Battle of Gonzales (HISTORY)":"أُطلقت أولى طلقات ثورة تكساس في معركة غونزاليس (HISTORY)","A short account of the skirmish and its minimal casualties.":"سرد موجز للمناوشة وخسائرها البشرية الضئيلة.","How many people were hurt in the fight?":"كم عدد الأشخاص الذين أُصيبوا في القتال؟","How can an event be important without being big?":"كيف يمكن أن يكون حدثٌ مهمًا دون أن يكون كبيرًا؟","Anglo colonists and Tejanos lived fairly autonomously in Mexican Texas under the 1824 federal constitution; Gonzales kept a small cannon, loaned in 1831, for defense against raids.":"عاش المستوطنون الأنجلو والتيخانو باستقلالية نسبية في تكساس المكسيكية في ظل الدستور الفيدرالي لعام 1824؛ واحتفظت غونزاليس بمدفع صغير، أُعير في عام 1831، للدفاع ضد الغارات.","Santa Anna shifted Mexico toward centralism, dismantling the 1824 federal system and alarming Texans; Colonel Ugartechea demanded the loaned Gonzales cannon back, and the colonists refused.":"دفع سانتا آنا المكسيك نحو المركزية، مفككًا النظام الفيدرالي لعام 1824 ومثيرًا قلق التكسيين؛ وطالب الكولونيل أوغارتيتشيا بإعادة مدفع غونزاليس المُعار، فرفض المستوطنون.","Texian militia crossed the Guadalupe River at dawn and fired on Lt. Castañeda's dragoons rather than surrender the cannon — the first shots of the Texas Revolution.":"عبرت الميليشيا التكسية نهر غوادالوبي عند الفجر وأطلقت النار على فرسان الملازم كاستانيدا بدلًا من تسليم المدفع — أولى طلقات ثورة تكساس.","Castañeda withdrew toward San Antonio de Béxar empty-handed; 'Come and Take It' became a rallying cry; volunteers streamed to Gonzales.":"انسحب كاستانيدا نحو سان أنطونيو دي بيخار خالي الوفاض؛ وأصبحت 'Come and Take It' ('تعالَ وخذه') صيحة حشد؛ وتدفّق المتطوعون إلى غونزاليس.","The gathering force marched on Béxar (captured December 1835); delegates convened the Consultation, moving Texas toward the 1836 declaration of independence.":"زحفت القوة المتجمّعة على بيخار (التي سُيطر عليها في ديسمبر 1835)؛ وعقد المندوبون 'المشاورة' (Consultation)، ما دفع تكساس نحو إعلان الاستقلال عام 1836.","Gonzales colonists and DeWitt-colony militia (the 'Old Eighteen' and John Henry Moore), determined to keep the cannon.":"مستوطنو غونزاليس وميليشيا مستعمرة ديويت (الـ 'Old Eighteen' / 'الثمانية عشر القدامى' وجون هنري مور)، وقد عقدوا العزم على الاحتفاظ بالمدفع.","Mexican centralist authorities — Colonel Ugartechea and Lt. Castañeda, ordered to recover the cannon.":"السلطات المركزية المكسيكية — الكولونيل أوغارتيتشيا والملازم كاستانيدا، اللذان صدرت إليهما الأوامر باستعادة المدفع.","Castañeda was ordered to avoid a fight; had he pressed the attack, or had colonists complied, revolution might have been delayed or sparked elsewhere.":"أُمر كاستانيدا بتجنّب القتال؛ فلو أنه مضى في الهجوم، أو لو أن المستوطنين امتثلوا، لربما تأخرت الثورة أو اندلعت في مكان آخر.","Why do historians call a small skirmish with almost no casualties the 'turning point' that began the Texas Revolution? What changed after Gonzales that could not be undone?":"لماذا يسمّي المؤرخون مناوشة صغيرة بلا خسائر بشرية تقريبًا 'نقطة التحول' التي بدأت ثورة تكساس؟ وما الذي تغيّر بعد غونزاليس ولم يكن بالإمكان التراجع عنه؟"},"zh":{"The Battle of Gonzales":"冈萨雷斯之战","Decide whether a small skirmish over a cannon — the 'Come and Take It' fight of October 2, 1835 — was truly the turning point that began the Texas Revolution.":"判断一场为争夺一门大炮而起的小规模冲突——1835 年 10 月 2 日的'Come and Take It'('有本事就来拿')之战——是否真正是引发得克萨斯革命的转折点。","On October 2, 1835, Texian colonists at Gonzales refused to hand a small cannon back to Mexican soldiers and fired on them instead, under a homemade flag reading 'Come and Take It.' Almost no one was hurt — so why do historians call this the turning point that began the Texas Revolution? Map what led up to it and what changed afterward.":"1835 年 10 月 2 日,冈萨雷斯的得克萨斯移民拒绝把一门小型大炮交还给墨西哥士兵,反而向他们开火,头顶一面自制的、写着'Come and Take It'('有本事就来拿')的旗帜。几乎无人受伤——那么历史学家为什么把这称为引发得克萨斯革命的转折点?请梳理导致此事发生的原因以及此后发生的变化。","Battle of Gonzales ('Come and Take It')":"冈萨雷斯之战('Come and Take It' / '有本事就来拿')","Gonzales, Texas":"得克萨斯州冈萨雷斯","Compare your before-and-after with a partner. Did you agree on what changed most?":"与同伴比较你们各自梳理的'之前和之后'。你们对什么变化最大意见一致吗?","Which pressure do you think mattered most in pushing events toward a fight?":"你认为哪种压力在把事态推向冲突方面最为关键?","Was the Battle of Gonzales truly a turning point? Use evidence from at least two sources to argue what changed after it that could not be undone.":"冈萨雷斯之战真的是一个转折点吗?请使用至少两个来源的证据,论证它之后发生了哪些无法逆转的变化。","Explain what happened at Gonzales and why the colonists refused to return the cannon.":"解释在冈萨雷斯发生了什么,以及移民为什么拒绝归还大炮。","Connect Santa Anna's shift to centralism to the colonists' decision to fight.":"把圣安纳转向中央集权与移民决定开战联系起来。","Apply the idea of a small event with big consequences to another moment in history.":"把'小事件带来大后果'这一概念应用到历史上的另一个时刻。","Gonzales, Battle of — Handbook of Texas Online (TSHA)":"冈萨雷斯之战 — Handbook of Texas Online(TSHA)","The Texas State Historical Association's entry on the opening battle of the Revolution.":"得克萨斯州历史协会关于这场革命开局之战的条目。","What was the dispute really about?":"这场争端真正的核心是什么?","Why was it important even though few were hurt?":"尽管受伤者寥寥无几,它为什么依然重要?","Gonzales 'Come and Take It' Cannon — Handbook of Texas Online (TSHA)":"冈萨雷斯'Come and Take It'('有本事就来拿')大炮 — Handbook of Texas Online(TSHA)","The story of the loaned cannon and the 'Come and Take It' flag made by the women of Gonzales.":"关于那门借来的大炮,以及由冈萨雷斯的妇女们制作的'Come and Take It'('有本事就来拿')旗帜的故事。","Why did the colonists care so much about one small cannon?":"移民为什么如此在意一门小小的大炮?","What did the flag's message mean?":"旗帜上的这句话是什么意思?","First shots of the Texas Revolution fired in the Battle of Gonzales (HISTORY)":"得克萨斯革命的第一枪在冈萨雷斯之战中打响(HISTORY)","A short account of the skirmish and its minimal casualties.":"对这场小规模冲突及其极少伤亡的简短叙述。","How many people were hurt in the fight?":"这场战斗中有多少人受伤?","How can an event be important without being big?":"一个事件怎么能不'大'却依然重要?","Anglo colonists and Tejanos lived fairly autonomously in Mexican Texas under the 1824 federal constitution; Gonzales kept a small cannon, loaned in 1831, for defense against raids.":"在 1824 年联邦宪法下,盎格鲁移民和特哈诺人在墨西哥治下的得克萨斯生活得相当自治;冈萨雷斯保留了一门 1831 年借来的小型大炮,用于抵御袭击。","Santa Anna shifted Mexico toward centralism, dismantling the 1824 federal system and alarming Texans; Colonel Ugartechea demanded the loaned Gonzales cannon back, and the colonists refused.":"圣安纳推动墨西哥转向中央集权,拆解了 1824 年的联邦制度,令得克萨斯人警觉;乌加特切亚上校要求归还借给冈萨雷斯的大炮,移民则予以拒绝。","Texian militia crossed the Guadalupe River at dawn and fired on Lt. Castañeda's dragoons rather than surrender the cannon — the first shots of the Texas Revolution.":"得克萨斯民兵在黎明时分渡过瓜达卢佩河,向卡斯塔涅达中尉的龙骑兵开火,而不是交出大炮——这便是得克萨斯革命的第一枪。","Castañeda withdrew toward San Antonio de Béxar empty-handed; 'Come and Take It' became a rallying cry; volunteers streamed to Gonzales.":"卡斯塔涅达空手退向圣安东尼奥-德贝哈尔;'Come and Take It'('有本事就来拿')成了号召口号;志愿者纷纷涌向冈萨雷斯。","The gathering force marched on Béxar (captured December 1835); delegates convened the Consultation, moving Texas toward the 1836 declaration of independence.":"集结起来的队伍向贝哈尔进军(于 1835 年 12 月被攻占);代表们召开了'协商会议'(Consultation),推动得克萨斯迈向 1836 年的独立宣言。","Gonzales colonists and DeWitt-colony militia (the 'Old Eighteen' and John Henry Moore), determined to keep the cannon.":"冈萨雷斯的移民和德威特殖民地的民兵('Old Eighteen'/'元老十八人'以及约翰·亨利·摩尔),决心留住这门大炮。","Mexican centralist authorities — Colonel Ugartechea and Lt. Castañeda, ordered to recover the cannon.":"墨西哥中央集权当局——乌加特切亚上校和卡斯塔涅达中尉,奉命夺回大炮。","Castañeda was ordered to avoid a fight; had he pressed the attack, or had colonists complied, revolution might have been delayed or sparked elsewhere.":"卡斯塔涅达奉命避免交战;倘若他坚持进攻,或者移民选择服从,革命也许会被推迟,或在别处引爆。","Why do historians call a small skirmish with almost no casualties the 'turning point' that began the Texas Revolution? What changed after Gonzales that could not be undone?":"历史学家为什么把一场几乎零伤亡的小规模冲突称为引发得克萨斯革命的'转折点'?冈萨雷斯之后发生了哪些无法逆转的变化?"},"ur":{"The Battle of Gonzales":"گونزالیس کی لڑائی","Decide whether a small skirmish over a cannon — the 'Come and Take It' fight of October 2, 1835 — was truly the turning point that began the Texas Revolution.":"فیصلہ کریں کہ ایک توپ پر ہونے والی چھوٹی سی جھڑپ — 2 اکتوبر 1835 کی 'Come and Take It' ('آؤ اور اسے لے لو') کی لڑائی — واقعی وہ موڑ تھی جس نے ٹیکساس انقلاب کا آغاز کیا؟","On October 2, 1835, Texian colonists at Gonzales refused to hand a small cannon back to Mexican soldiers and fired on them instead, under a homemade flag reading 'Come and Take It.' Almost no one was hurt — so why do historians call this the turning point that began the Texas Revolution? Map what led up to it and what changed afterward.":"2 اکتوبر 1835 کو گونزالیس کے ٹیکسیئن آبادکاروں نے ایک چھوٹی توپ میکسیکن سپاہیوں کو واپس کرنے سے انکار کر دیا اور اس کے بجائے اُن پر فائرنگ کر دی، ایک گھر کے بنے جھنڈے کے نیچے جس پر لکھا تھا 'Come and Take It' ('آؤ اور اسے لے لو')۔ تقریباً کوئی زخمی نہ ہوا — تو پھر مؤرخین اسے وہ موڑ کیوں کہتے ہیں جس نے ٹیکساس انقلاب کا آغاز کیا؟ جو کچھ اس سے پہلے ہوا اور اس کے بعد جو کچھ بدلا، اس کا نقشہ بنائیں۔","Battle of Gonzales ('Come and Take It')":"گونزالیس کی لڑائی ('Come and Take It' / 'آؤ اور اسے لے لو')","Gonzales, Texas":"گونزالیس، ٹیکساس","Compare your before-and-after with a partner. Did you agree on what changed most?":"اپنے 'پہلے اور بعد' کا موازنہ کسی ساتھی کے ساتھ کریں۔ کیا آپ دونوں اس بات پر متفق ہوئے کہ سب سے زیادہ کیا بدلا؟","Which pressure do you think mattered most in pushing events toward a fight?":"آپ کے خیال میں کون سا دباؤ واقعات کو لڑائی کی طرف دھکیلنے میں سب سے اہم تھا؟","Was the Battle of Gonzales truly a turning point? Use evidence from at least two sources to argue what changed after it that could not be undone.":"کیا گونزالیس کی لڑائی واقعی ایک موڑ تھی؟ کم از کم دو ذرائع سے شواہد استعمال کرتے ہوئے دلیل دیں کہ اس کے بعد کیا بدلا جسے واپس نہیں کیا جا سکتا تھا۔","Explain what happened at Gonzales and why the colonists refused to return the cannon.":"وضاحت کریں کہ گونزالیس میں کیا ہوا اور آبادکاروں نے توپ واپس کرنے سے انکار کیوں کیا۔","Connect Santa Anna's shift to centralism to the colonists' decision to fight.":"سانتا آنا کے مرکزیت کی طرف رجحان کو آبادکاروں کے لڑنے کے فیصلے سے جوڑیں۔","Apply the idea of a small event with big consequences to another moment in history.":"چھوٹے واقعے کے بڑے نتائج کے تصور کو تاریخ کے کسی اور لمحے پر لاگو کریں۔","Gonzales, Battle of — Handbook of Texas Online (TSHA)":"گونزالیس، کی لڑائی — Handbook of Texas Online (TSHA)","The Texas State Historical Association's entry on the opening battle of the Revolution.":"انقلاب کی افتتاحی لڑائی پر ٹیکساس اسٹیٹ ہسٹاریکل ایسوسی ایشن کا اندراج۔","What was the dispute really about?":"یہ تنازع دراصل کس بارے میں تھا؟","Why was it important even though few were hurt?":"بہت کم لوگ زخمی ہونے کے باوجود یہ اہم کیوں تھا؟","Gonzales 'Come and Take It' Cannon — Handbook of Texas Online (TSHA)":"گونزالیس کی 'Come and Take It' ('آؤ اور اسے لے لو') توپ — Handbook of Texas Online (TSHA)","The story of the loaned cannon and the 'Come and Take It' flag made by the women of Gonzales.":"اُدھار دی گئی توپ اور گونزالیس کی خواتین کے بنائے ہوئے 'Come and Take It' ('آؤ اور اسے لے لو') جھنڈے کی کہانی۔","Why did the colonists care so much about one small cannon?":"آبادکاروں کو ایک چھوٹی سی توپ کی اتنی پروا کیوں تھی؟","What did the flag's message mean?":"جھنڈے کے پیغام کا کیا مطلب تھا؟","First shots of the Texas Revolution fired in the Battle of Gonzales (HISTORY)":"ٹیکساس انقلاب کی پہلی گولیاں گونزالیس کی لڑائی میں چلائی گئیں (HISTORY)","A short account of the skirmish and its minimal casualties.":"جھڑپ اور اس میں ہونے والے معمولی جانی نقصان کا مختصر بیان۔","How many people were hurt in the fight?":"لڑائی میں کتنے لوگ زخمی ہوئے؟","How can an event be important without being big?":"کوئی واقعہ بڑا ہوئے بغیر اہم کیسے ہو سکتا ہے؟","Anglo colonists and Tejanos lived fairly autonomously in Mexican Texas under the 1824 federal constitution; Gonzales kept a small cannon, loaned in 1831, for defense against raids.":"1824 کے وفاقی آئین کے تحت میکسیکن ٹیکساس میں اینگلو آبادکار اور تیخانو کافی حد تک خودمختاری سے رہتے تھے؛ گونزالیس نے حملوں سے بچاؤ کے لیے 1831 میں اُدھار لی گئی ایک چھوٹی توپ رکھی ہوئی تھی۔","Santa Anna shifted Mexico toward centralism, dismantling the 1824 federal system and alarming Texans; Colonel Ugartechea demanded the loaned Gonzales cannon back, and the colonists refused.":"سانتا آنا نے میکسیکو کو مرکزیت کی طرف موڑا، 1824 کے وفاقی نظام کو ختم کیا اور ٹیکسان باشندوں کو پریشان کیا؛ کرنل اوگارتیچیا نے گونزالیس کو اُدھار دی گئی توپ واپس مانگی، اور آبادکاروں نے انکار کر دیا۔","Texian militia crossed the Guadalupe River at dawn and fired on Lt. Castañeda's dragoons rather than surrender the cannon — the first shots of the Texas Revolution.":"ٹیکسیئن ملیشیا نے صبح سویرے دریائے گواڈالوپے عبور کیا اور توپ حوالے کرنے کے بجائے لیفٹیننٹ کاستانیڈا کے گھڑسواروں پر فائرنگ کی — ٹیکساس انقلاب کی پہلی گولیاں۔","Castañeda withdrew toward San Antonio de Béxar empty-handed; 'Come and Take It' became a rallying cry; volunteers streamed to Gonzales.":"کاستانیڈا خالی ہاتھ سان انتونیو دی بیخار کی طرف پیچھے ہٹ گیا؛ 'Come and Take It' ('آؤ اور اسے لے لو') ایک نعرۂ اجتماع بن گیا؛ رضاکار جوق در جوق گونزالیس پہنچنے لگے۔","The gathering force marched on Béxar (captured December 1835); delegates convened the Consultation, moving Texas toward the 1836 declaration of independence.":"جمع ہونے والی فوج نے بیخار پر چڑھائی کی (دسمبر 1835 میں فتح ہوا)؛ مندوبین نے 'مشاورت' (Consultation) کا اجلاس بلایا، جس نے ٹیکساس کو 1836 کے اعلانِ آزادی کی طرف بڑھایا۔","Gonzales colonists and DeWitt-colony militia (the 'Old Eighteen' and John Henry Moore), determined to keep the cannon.":"گونزالیس کے آبادکار اور ڈی وِٹ کالونی کی ملیشیا ('Old Eighteen' / 'قدیم اٹھارہ' اور جون ہنری مور)، جو توپ اپنے پاس رکھنے پر مصمم تھے۔","Mexican centralist authorities — Colonel Ugartechea and Lt. Castañeda, ordered to recover the cannon.":"میکسیکن مرکزیت پسند حکام — کرنل اوگارتیچیا اور لیفٹیننٹ کاستانیڈا، جنہیں توپ واپس لانے کا حکم دیا گیا تھا۔","Castañeda was ordered to avoid a fight; had he pressed the attack, or had colonists complied, revolution might have been delayed or sparked elsewhere.":"کاستانیڈا کو لڑائی سے بچنے کا حکم تھا؛ اگر وہ حملہ جاری رکھتا، یا آبادکار مان جاتے، تو انقلاب میں تاخیر ہو سکتی تھی یا وہ کہیں اور بھڑک اٹھتا۔","Why do historians call a small skirmish with almost no casualties the 'turning point' that began the Texas Revolution? What changed after Gonzales that could not be undone?":"مؤرخین تقریباً بغیر کسی جانی نقصان والی ایک چھوٹی جھڑپ کو وہ 'موڑ' کیوں کہتے ہیں جس نے ٹیکساس انقلاب کا آغاز کیا؟ گونزالیس کے بعد ایسا کیا بدلا جسے واپس نہیں کیا جا سکتا تھا؟"},"hi":{"The Battle of Gonzales":"गोंज़ालेस की लड़ाई","Decide whether a small skirmish over a cannon — the 'Come and Take It' fight of October 2, 1835 — was truly the turning point that began the Texas Revolution.":"तय करें कि एक तोप को लेकर हुई छोटी सी झड़प — 2 अक्टूबर 1835 की 'Come and Take It' ('आओ और इसे ले लो') की लड़ाई — क्या सचमुच वह मोड़ थी जिसने टेक्सास क्रांति की शुरुआत की।","On October 2, 1835, Texian colonists at Gonzales refused to hand a small cannon back to Mexican soldiers and fired on them instead, under a homemade flag reading 'Come and Take It.' Almost no one was hurt — so why do historians call this the turning point that began the Texas Revolution? Map what led up to it and what changed afterward.":"2 अक्टूबर 1835 को गोंज़ालेस के टेक्सियन उपनिवेशवासियों ने एक छोटी तोप मैक्सिकन सैनिकों को लौटाने से इनकार कर दिया और उनके बजाय उन पर गोली चला दी, एक घर में बने झंडे के नीचे जिस पर लिखा था 'Come and Take It' ('आओ और इसे ले लो')। लगभग कोई घायल नहीं हुआ — तो फिर इतिहासकार इसे वह मोड़ क्यों कहते हैं जिसने टेक्सास क्रांति की शुरुआत की? इससे पहले जो हुआ और बाद में जो बदला, उसका खाका बनाएं।","Battle of Gonzales ('Come and Take It')":"गोंज़ालेस की लड़ाई ('Come and Take It' / 'आओ और इसे ले लो')","Gonzales, Texas":"गोंज़ालेस, टेक्सास","Compare your before-and-after with a partner. Did you agree on what changed most?":"अपने 'पहले और बाद' की तुलना किसी साथी के साथ करें। क्या आप इस बात पर सहमत हुए कि सबसे ज़्यादा क्या बदला?","Which pressure do you think mattered most in pushing events toward a fight?":"आपके विचार में कौन-सा दबाव घटनाओं को टकराव की ओर धकेलने में सबसे अहम था?","Was the Battle of Gonzales truly a turning point? Use evidence from at least two sources to argue what changed after it that could not be undone.":"क्या गोंज़ालेस की लड़ाई सचमुच एक मोड़ थी? कम से कम दो स्रोतों के प्रमाणों का उपयोग करके तर्क दें कि इसके बाद क्या बदला जिसे पलटा नहीं जा सकता था।","Explain what happened at Gonzales and why the colonists refused to return the cannon.":"समझाएं कि गोंज़ालेस में क्या हुआ और उपनिवेशवासियों ने तोप लौटाने से इनकार क्यों किया।","Connect Santa Anna's shift to centralism to the colonists' decision to fight.":"सांता आना के केंद्रीयवाद की ओर झुकाव को उपनिवेशवासियों के लड़ने के निर्णय से जोड़ें।","Apply the idea of a small event with big consequences to another moment in history.":"'बड़े परिणामों वाली छोटी घटना' के विचार को इतिहास के किसी अन्य क्षण पर लागू करें।","Gonzales, Battle of — Handbook of Texas Online (TSHA)":"गोंज़ालेस की लड़ाई — Handbook of Texas Online (TSHA)","The Texas State Historical Association's entry on the opening battle of the Revolution.":"क्रांति की शुरुआती लड़ाई पर टेक्सास स्टेट हिस्टोरिकल एसोसिएशन की प्रविष्टि।","What was the dispute really about?":"यह विवाद वास्तव में किस बारे में था?","Why was it important even though few were hurt?":"बहुत कम लोग घायल होने के बावजूद यह महत्वपूर्ण क्यों था?","Gonzales 'Come and Take It' Cannon — Handbook of Texas Online (TSHA)":"गोंज़ालेस की 'Come and Take It' ('आओ और इसे ले लो') तोप — Handbook of Texas Online (TSHA)","The story of the loaned cannon and the 'Come and Take It' flag made by the women of Gonzales.":"उधार दी गई तोप और गोंज़ालेस की महिलाओं द्वारा बनाए गए 'Come and Take It' ('आओ और इसे ले लो') झंडे की कहानी।","Why did the colonists care so much about one small cannon?":"उपनिवेशवासियों को एक छोटी सी तोप की इतनी परवाह क्यों थी?","What did the flag's message mean?":"झंडे के संदेश का क्या अर्थ था?","First shots of the Texas Revolution fired in the Battle of Gonzales (HISTORY)":"टेक्सास क्रांति की पहली गोलियां गोंज़ालेस की लड़ाई में चलाई गईं (HISTORY)","A short account of the skirmish and its minimal casualties.":"इस झड़प और इसमें हुए न्यूनतम हताहतों का संक्षिप्त विवरण।","How many people were hurt in the fight?":"लड़ाई में कितने लोग घायल हुए?","How can an event be important without being big?":"कोई घटना बड़ी हुए बिना महत्वपूर्ण कैसे हो सकती है?","Anglo colonists and Tejanos lived fairly autonomously in Mexican Texas under the 1824 federal constitution; Gonzales kept a small cannon, loaned in 1831, for defense against raids.":"1824 के संघीय संविधान के तहत मैक्सिकन टेक्सास में एंग्लो उपनिवेशवासी और तेहानो काफी हद तक स्वायत्त रूप से रहते थे; गोंज़ालेस ने हमलों से बचाव के लिए 1831 में उधार ली गई एक छोटी तोप रखी हुई थी।","Santa Anna shifted Mexico toward centralism, dismantling the 1824 federal system and alarming Texans; Colonel Ugartechea demanded the loaned Gonzales cannon back, and the colonists refused.":"सांता आना ने मैक्सिको को केंद्रीयवाद की ओर मोड़ा, 1824 की संघीय व्यवस्था को नष्ट किया और टेक्सासवासियों को चिंतित कर दिया; कर्नल उगार्तेचिया ने गोंज़ालेस को उधार दी गई तोप वापस मांगी, और उपनिवेशवासियों ने इनकार कर दिया।","Texian militia crossed the Guadalupe River at dawn and fired on Lt. Castañeda's dragoons rather than surrender the cannon — the first shots of the Texas Revolution.":"टेक्सियन मिलिशिया ने भोर के समय ग्वादालूपे नदी पार की और तोप सौंपने के बजाय लेफ्टिनेंट कास्तानेदा के घुड़सवारों पर गोली चला दी — टेक्सास क्रांति की पहली गोलियां।","Castañeda withdrew toward San Antonio de Béxar empty-handed; 'Come and Take It' became a rallying cry; volunteers streamed to Gonzales.":"कास्तानेदा खाली हाथ सान अंतोनियो दे बेहार की ओर पीछे हट गया; 'Come and Take It' ('आओ और इसे ले लो') एक जयघोष बन गया; स्वयंसेवक गोंज़ालेस की ओर उमड़ पड़े।","The gathering force marched on Béxar (captured December 1835); delegates convened the Consultation, moving Texas toward the 1836 declaration of independence.":"एकत्रित होती सेना ने बेहार पर चढ़ाई की (दिसंबर 1835 में कब्ज़ा हुआ); प्रतिनिधियों ने 'परामर्श सभा' (Consultation) बुलाई, जिसने टेक्सास को 1836 की स्वतंत्रता की घोषणा की ओर बढ़ाया।","Gonzales colonists and DeWitt-colony militia (the 'Old Eighteen' and John Henry Moore), determined to keep the cannon.":"गोंज़ालेस के उपनिवेशवासी और डेविट-कॉलोनी की मिलिशिया ('Old Eighteen' / 'पुराने अठारह' और जॉन हेनरी मूर), जो तोप को अपने पास रखने के लिए दृढ़ थे।","Mexican centralist authorities — Colonel Ugartechea and Lt. Castañeda, ordered to recover the cannon.":"मैक्सिकन केंद्रीयवादी अधिकारी — कर्नल उगार्तेचिया और लेफ्टिनेंट कास्तानेदा, जिन्हें तोप वापस लाने का आदेश दिया गया था।","Castañeda was ordered to avoid a fight; had he pressed the attack, or had colonists complied, revolution might have been delayed or sparked elsewhere.":"कास्तानेदा को लड़ाई टालने का आदेश दिया गया था; यदि उसने हमला जारी रखा होता, या उपनिवेशवासी मान गए होते, तो क्रांति में देरी हो सकती थी या वह कहीं और भड़क उठती।","Why do historians call a small skirmish with almost no casualties the 'turning point' that began the Texas Revolution? What changed after Gonzales that could not be undone?":"इतिहासकार लगभग शून्य हताहतों वाली एक छोटी झड़प को वह 'मोड़' क्यों कहते हैं जिसने टेक्सास क्रांति की शुरुआत की? गोंज़ालेस के बाद ऐसा क्या बदला जिसे पलटा नहीं जा सकता था?"}},"boston-tea-party":{"es":{"Boston Tea Party":"Motín del té de Boston","Examine how Patriots, British officials, tea merchants, and other colonists viewed taxation, resistance, and British authority in the events surrounding the destruction of the tea.":"Examina cómo los patriotas, los funcionarios británicos, los comerciantes de té y otros colonos vieron los impuestos, la resistencia y la autoridad británica en los hechos que rodearon la destrucción del té."},"vi":{"Boston Tea Party":"Tiệc trà Boston","Examine how Patriots, British officials, tea merchants, and other colonists viewed taxation, resistance, and British authority in the events surrounding the destruction of the tea.":"Tìm hiểu cách những người Ái quốc, quan chức Anh, thương nhân trà và các dân thuộc địa khác nhìn nhận về thuế, sự phản kháng và quyền lực của Anh trong các sự kiện xoay quanh việc phá hủy trà."},"ar":{"Boston Tea Party":"حفلة شاي بوسطن","Examine how Patriots, British officials, tea merchants, and other colonists viewed taxation, resistance, and British authority in the events surrounding the destruction of the tea.":"افحص كيف نظر الوطنيون والمسؤولون البريطانيون وتجار الشاي وبقية المستعمِرين إلى الضرائب والمقاومة والسلطة البريطانية في الأحداث المحيطة بإتلاف الشاي."},"zh":{"Boston Tea Party":"波士顿倾茶事件","Examine how Patriots, British officials, tea merchants, and other colonists viewed taxation, resistance, and British authority in the events surrounding the destruction of the tea.":"考察爱国者、英国官员、茶叶商人和其他殖民地居民如何看待围绕倾倒茶叶事件中的税收、反抗与英国权威。"},"ur":{"Boston Tea Party":"بوسٹن ٹی پارٹی","Examine how Patriots, British officials, tea merchants, and other colonists viewed taxation, resistance, and British authority in the events surrounding the destruction of the tea.":"جائزہ لیں کہ محبِّینِ وطن، برطانوی عہدیداروں، چائے کے تاجروں اور دیگر نوآبادکاروں نے چائے کی تباہی کے گرد پیش آنے والے واقعات میں ٹیکس، مزاحمت اور برطانوی اختیار کو کیسے دیکھا۔"},"hi":{"Boston Tea Party":"बोस्टन टी पार्टी","Examine how Patriots, British officials, tea merchants, and other colonists viewed taxation, resistance, and British authority in the events surrounding the destruction of the tea.":"जाँचें कि देशभक्तों, ब्रिटिश अधिकारियों, चाय व्यापारियों और अन्य उपनिवेशवासियों ने चाय के विनाश से जुड़ी घटनाओं में कर, प्रतिरोध और ब्रिटिश सत्ता को कैसे देखा।"}},"civil-rights-movement":{"es":{"The Civil Rights Movement":"El Movimiento por los Derechos Civiles","Weigh what changed, what changed slowly, and what stayed the same across the Civil Rights Movement (1954–1968), and judge whether it was a true turning point.":"Sopesa qué cambió, qué cambió lentamente y qué permaneció igual a lo largo del Movimiento por los Derechos Civiles (1954–1968), y determina si fue un verdadero punto de inflexión.","Between 1954 and 1968, courts, laws, and mass movements dismantled the legal framework of segregation. But law on paper and life on the ground are not the same thing. Compare before, during, and after — then judge: was this era a genuine turning point in U.S. history, or the acceleration of a longer struggle?":"Entre 1954 y 1968, los tribunales, las leyes y los movimientos de masas desmantelaron el marco legal de la segregación. Pero la ley sobre el papel y la vida real no son lo mismo. Compara el antes, el durante y el después, y luego decide: ¿fue esta época un verdadero punto de inflexión en la historia de EE. UU., o la aceleración de una lucha más larga?","The United States":"Los Estados Unidos","Compare your ledgers with a partner. Did you sort the same items into 'changed' vs. 'stayed the same'?":"Compara tus registros con un compañero. ¿Clasificaron los mismos elementos como 'cambió' frente a 'permaneció igual'?","Where did you disagree about whether something changed a lot, a little, or not at all?":"¿En qué puntos no estuvieron de acuerdo sobre si algo cambió mucho, poco o nada?","Was 1954–1968 a genuine turning point, or the acceleration of a longer struggle? Use evidence from at least two sources, cite specific laws or events, and address at least one way change was incomplete.":"¿Fue 1954–1968 un verdadero punto de inflexión, o la aceleración de una lucha más larga? Usa evidencia de al menos dos fuentes, cita leyes o acontecimientos específicos y aborda al menos una forma en que el cambio fue incompleto.","Explain the difference between de jure and de facto change using one example.":"Explica la diferencia entre el cambio de jure (por ley) y de facto (en la práctica) usando un ejemplo.","Connect a protest or event 'during' the movement to a law that came 'after' it.":"Conecta una protesta o acontecimiento 'durante' el movimiento con una ley que surgió 'después'.","Apply the continuity-and-change lens to a rights movement happening today. What has changed, and what has not?":"Aplica el enfoque de continuidad y cambio a un movimiento por los derechos que ocurre hoy. ¿Qué ha cambiado y qué no?","Civil Rights Act (1964) — National Archives":"Ley de Derechos Civiles (Civil Rights Act, 1964) — Archivos Nacionales","The 1964 law banning discrimination and outlawing segregation in public accommodations and employment.":"La ley de 1964 que prohibió la discriminación y proscribió la segregación en los establecimientos públicos y el empleo.","What did the Civil Rights Act make illegal?":"¿Qué hizo ilegal la Ley de Derechos Civiles?","What might a law like this not be able to change by itself?":"¿Qué podría no lograr cambiar por sí sola una ley como esta?","Voting Rights Act (1965) — National Archives":"Ley de Derecho al Voto (Voting Rights Act, 1965) — Archivos Nacionales","The 1965 law outlawing literacy tests and authorizing federal oversight of voter registration.":"La ley de 1965 que proscribió las pruebas de alfabetización y autorizó la supervisión federal del registro de votantes.","How did this law try to protect the right to vote?":"¿Cómo intentó esta ley proteger el derecho al voto?","Why might voting rights need federal enforcement?":"¿Por qué el derecho al voto podría necesitar aplicación federal?","Little Rock Central High School National Historic Site — National Park Service":"Sitio Histórico Nacional de la Escuela Secundaria Central de Little Rock — Servicio de Parques Nacionales","How nine Black students integrated a school in 1957 and why federal troops were sent.":"Cómo nueve estudiantes negros integraron una escuela en 1957 y por qué se enviaron tropas federales.","What did it take to enforce the court's desegregation order?":"¿Qué hizo falta para hacer cumplir la orden de desegregación del tribunal?","What does this show about the gap between law and practice?":"¿Qué revela esto sobre la brecha entre la ley y la práctica?","Jim Crow laws and legally enforced segregation across the South":"Las leyes Jim Crow y la segregación impuesta legalmente en todo el Sur","Plessy v. Ferguson (1896) 'separate but equal' doctrine":"La doctrina de 'separados pero iguales' de Plessy v. Ferguson (1896)","Systematic Black disenfranchisement — poll taxes, literacy tests, white primaries, intimidation":"La privación sistemática del derecho al voto de los negros: impuestos electorales, pruebas de alfabetización, primarias solo para blancos e intimidación","Legal strategy in the courts (NAACP Legal Defense Fund; Brown v. Board, 1954)":"La estrategia legal en los tribunales (Fondo de Defensa Legal de la NAACP; Brown v. Board, 1954)","Nonviolent direct action — boycotts, sit-ins, Freedom Rides, marches":"La acción directa no violenta: boicots, sentadas, Viajes de la Libertad (Freedom Rides) y marchas","Grassroots organizing (SCLC, SNCC, CORE, NAACP) and youth leadership":"La organización de base (SCLC, SNCC, CORE, NAACP) y el liderazgo juvenil","Federal intervention prompted by protest and violence (Little Rock; Selma → Voting Rights Act)":"La intervención federal impulsada por la protesta y la violencia (Little Rock; Selma → Ley de Derecho al Voto)","Landmark federal law: Civil Rights Act (1964), Voting Rights Act (1965), Fair Housing Act (1968)":"Leyes federales históricas: Ley de Derechos Civiles (1964), Ley de Derecho al Voto (1965), Ley de Vivienda Justa (Fair Housing Act, 1968)","A sharp rise in Black voter registration and officeholding, especially in the South":"Un fuerte aumento en el registro de votantes negros y en la ocupación de cargos públicos, especialmente en el Sur","Persistent limits: de facto segregation, economic inequality, and later rollbacks (Shelby County v. Holder, 2013)":"Límites persistentes: la segregación de facto (en la práctica), la desigualdad económica y los retrocesos posteriores (Shelby County v. Holder, 2013)","The legal status of segregation and voting: federal law made de jure segregation and discriminatory voting tests illegal.":"El estatus legal de la segregación y del voto: la ley federal declaró ilegales la segregación de jure (por ley) y las pruebas electorales discriminatorias.","Actual desegregation of schools and public life, and the growth of Black political participation — over years, not overnight.":"La desegregación efectiva de las escuelas y de la vida pública, y el crecimiento de la participación política de los negros: a lo largo de años, no de la noche a la mañana.","De facto segregation and deep economic disparities in housing, wealth, and schooling persisted despite legal change.":"La segregación de facto (en la práctica) y las profundas disparidades económicas en la vivienda, la riqueza y la educación persistieron a pesar del cambio legal.","Why did some conditions change quickly (the law on paper) while others changed slowly or barely at all (everyday economic and residential realities)? What is the difference between de jure and de facto change?":"¿Por qué algunas condiciones cambiaron rápidamente (la ley sobre el papel) mientras que otras cambiaron lentamente o apenas cambiaron (las realidades económicas y residenciales cotidianas)? ¿Cuál es la diferencia entre el cambio de jure (por ley) y de facto (en la práctica)?"},"vi":{"The Civil Rights Movement":"Phong trào Dân quyền","Weigh what changed, what changed slowly, and what stayed the same across the Civil Rights Movement (1954–1968), and judge whether it was a true turning point.":"Cân nhắc điều gì đã thay đổi, điều gì thay đổi chậm và điều gì vẫn như cũ trong suốt Phong trào Dân quyền (1954–1968), và đánh giá xem đó có phải là một bước ngoặt thực sự hay không.","Between 1954 and 1968, courts, laws, and mass movements dismantled the legal framework of segregation. But law on paper and life on the ground are not the same thing. Compare before, during, and after — then judge: was this era a genuine turning point in U.S. history, or the acceleration of a longer struggle?":"Từ năm 1954 đến 1968, tòa án, luật pháp và các phong trào quần chúng đã phá bỏ khuôn khổ pháp lý của sự phân biệt chủng tộc. Nhưng luật trên giấy và cuộc sống thực tế không phải là một. Hãy so sánh trước, trong và sau — rồi đánh giá: liệu thời kỳ này có phải là một bước ngoặt thực sự trong lịch sử Hoa Kỳ, hay là sự tăng tốc của một cuộc đấu tranh dài hơn?","The United States":"Hoa Kỳ","Compare your ledgers with a partner. Did you sort the same items into 'changed' vs. 'stayed the same'?":"So sánh bảng ghi của bạn với một người bạn. Hai bạn có sắp xếp cùng những mục vào nhóm 'đã thay đổi' và 'vẫn như cũ' không?","Where did you disagree about whether something changed a lot, a little, or not at all?":"Ở đâu hai bạn bất đồng về việc một điều gì đó đã thay đổi nhiều, một chút, hay hoàn toàn không thay đổi?","Was 1954–1968 a genuine turning point, or the acceleration of a longer struggle? Use evidence from at least two sources, cite specific laws or events, and address at least one way change was incomplete.":"Giai đoạn 1954–1968 có phải là một bước ngoặt thực sự, hay là sự tăng tốc của một cuộc đấu tranh dài hơn? Sử dụng bằng chứng từ ít nhất hai nguồn, trích dẫn các luật hoặc sự kiện cụ thể, và nêu ít nhất một cách mà sự thay đổi còn dang dở.","Explain the difference between de jure and de facto change using one example.":"Giải thích sự khác biệt giữa thay đổi de jure (theo luật pháp) và de facto (trên thực tế) bằng một ví dụ.","Connect a protest or event 'during' the movement to a law that came 'after' it.":"Kết nối một cuộc biểu tình hoặc sự kiện 'trong' phong trào với một đạo luật ra đời 'sau' nó.","Apply the continuity-and-change lens to a rights movement happening today. What has changed, and what has not?":"Áp dụng góc nhìn tính liên tục và sự thay đổi vào một phong trào đòi quyền lợi đang diễn ra ngày nay. Điều gì đã thay đổi và điều gì thì không?","Civil Rights Act (1964) — National Archives":"Đạo luật Dân quyền (Civil Rights Act, 1964) — Cục Lưu trữ Quốc gia","The 1964 law banning discrimination and outlawing segregation in public accommodations and employment.":"Đạo luật năm 1964 cấm phân biệt đối xử và đặt sự phân biệt chủng tộc trong các cơ sở công cộng và việc làm ra ngoài vòng pháp luật.","What did the Civil Rights Act make illegal?":"Đạo luật Dân quyền đã khiến điều gì trở thành bất hợp pháp?","What might a law like this not be able to change by itself?":"Một đạo luật như thế này có thể không tự mình thay đổi được điều gì?","Voting Rights Act (1965) — National Archives":"Đạo luật Quyền Bầu cử (Voting Rights Act, 1965) — Cục Lưu trữ Quốc gia","The 1965 law outlawing literacy tests and authorizing federal oversight of voter registration.":"Đạo luật năm 1965 đặt các bài kiểm tra biết chữ ra ngoài vòng pháp luật và cho phép chính quyền liên bang giám sát việc đăng ký cử tri.","How did this law try to protect the right to vote?":"Đạo luật này đã cố gắng bảo vệ quyền bầu cử như thế nào?","Why might voting rights need federal enforcement?":"Vì sao quyền bầu cử có thể cần đến sự thực thi của chính quyền liên bang?","Little Rock Central High School National Historic Site — National Park Service":"Di tích Lịch sử Quốc gia Trường Trung học Central ở Little Rock — Cục Công viên Quốc gia","How nine Black students integrated a school in 1957 and why federal troops were sent.":"Chín học sinh da đen đã hòa nhập vào một trường học năm 1957 như thế nào và vì sao quân đội liên bang được điều đến.","What did it take to enforce the court's desegregation order?":"Cần những gì để thực thi lệnh xóa bỏ phân biệt chủng tộc của tòa án?","What does this show about the gap between law and practice?":"Điều này cho thấy gì về khoảng cách giữa luật pháp và thực tiễn?","Jim Crow laws and legally enforced segregation across the South":"Các đạo luật Jim Crow và sự phân biệt chủng tộc được thực thi hợp pháp khắp miền Nam","Plessy v. Ferguson (1896) 'separate but equal' doctrine":"Học thuyết 'tách biệt nhưng bình đẳng' trong vụ Plessy v. Ferguson (1896)","Systematic Black disenfranchisement — poll taxes, literacy tests, white primaries, intimidation":"Việc tước quyền bầu cử một cách có hệ thống đối với người da đen — thuế thân cử tri, bài kiểm tra biết chữ, bầu cử sơ bộ dành riêng cho người da trắng, và sự đe dọa","Legal strategy in the courts (NAACP Legal Defense Fund; Brown v. Board, 1954)":"Chiến lược pháp lý tại tòa án (Quỹ Bảo vệ Pháp lý NAACP; Brown v. Board, 1954)","Nonviolent direct action — boycotts, sit-ins, Freedom Rides, marches":"Hành động trực tiếp bất bạo động — tẩy chay, biểu tình ngồi, Những Chuyến đi vì Tự do (Freedom Rides), và tuần hành","Grassroots organizing (SCLC, SNCC, CORE, NAACP) and youth leadership":"Tổ chức phong trào từ cơ sở (SCLC, SNCC, CORE, NAACP) và vai trò lãnh đạo của thanh niên","Federal intervention prompted by protest and violence (Little Rock; Selma → Voting Rights Act)":"Sự can thiệp của liên bang do biểu tình và bạo lực thúc đẩy (Little Rock; Selma → Đạo luật Quyền Bầu cử)","Landmark federal law: Civil Rights Act (1964), Voting Rights Act (1965), Fair Housing Act (1968)":"Các đạo luật liên bang mang tính bước ngoặt: Đạo luật Dân quyền (1964), Đạo luật Quyền Bầu cử (1965), Đạo luật Nhà ở Công bằng (Fair Housing Act, 1968)","A sharp rise in Black voter registration and officeholding, especially in the South":"Sự gia tăng mạnh mẽ trong việc đăng ký cử tri da đen và giữ chức vụ công, đặc biệt ở miền Nam","Persistent limits: de facto segregation, economic inequality, and later rollbacks (Shelby County v. Holder, 2013)":"Những giới hạn dai dẳng: sự phân biệt chủng tộc de facto (trên thực tế), bất bình đẳng kinh tế, và những bước thụt lùi về sau (Shelby County v. Holder, 2013)","The legal status of segregation and voting: federal law made de jure segregation and discriminatory voting tests illegal.":"Địa vị pháp lý của sự phân biệt chủng tộc và quyền bầu cử: luật liên bang đã khiến sự phân biệt chủng tộc de jure (theo luật pháp) và các bài kiểm tra bầu cử phân biệt đối xử trở thành bất hợp pháp.","Actual desegregation of schools and public life, and the growth of Black political participation — over years, not overnight.":"Sự xóa bỏ phân biệt chủng tộc thực sự trong trường học và đời sống công cộng, cùng sự gia tăng tham gia chính trị của người da đen — qua nhiều năm, chứ không phải chỉ sau một đêm.","De facto segregation and deep economic disparities in housing, wealth, and schooling persisted despite legal change.":"Sự phân biệt chủng tộc de facto (trên thực tế) và những chênh lệch kinh tế sâu sắc về nhà ở, của cải và giáo dục vẫn dai dẳng bất chấp thay đổi về mặt pháp lý.","Why did some conditions change quickly (the law on paper) while others changed slowly or barely at all (everyday economic and residential realities)? What is the difference between de jure and de facto change?":"Vì sao một số điều kiện thay đổi nhanh chóng (luật trên giấy) trong khi những điều khác thay đổi chậm hoặc hầu như không thay đổi (thực tế kinh tế và cư trú hằng ngày)? Sự khác biệt giữa thay đổi de jure (theo luật pháp) và de facto (trên thực tế) là gì?"},"ar":{"The Civil Rights Movement":"حركة الحقوق المدنية","Weigh what changed, what changed slowly, and what stayed the same across the Civil Rights Movement (1954–1968), and judge whether it was a true turning point.":"قيّم ما تغيّر، وما تغيّر ببطء، وما ظل على حاله خلال حركة الحقوق المدنية (1954–1968)، واحكم على ما إذا كانت نقطة تحوّل حقيقية.","Between 1954 and 1968, courts, laws, and mass movements dismantled the legal framework of segregation. But law on paper and life on the ground are not the same thing. Compare before, during, and after — then judge: was this era a genuine turning point in U.S. history, or the acceleration of a longer struggle?":"بين عامي 1954 و1968، فكّكت المحاكم والقوانين والحركات الجماهيرية الإطار القانوني للفصل العنصري. لكن القانون على الورق والحياة على أرض الواقع ليسا شيئًا واحدًا. قارن بين ما قبل، وأثناء، وما بعد — ثم احكم: هل كان هذا العصر نقطة تحوّل حقيقية في تاريخ الولايات المتحدة، أم تسريعًا لنضال أطول؟","The United States":"الولايات المتحدة","Compare your ledgers with a partner. Did you sort the same items into 'changed' vs. 'stayed the same'?":"قارن سجلاتك مع زميل. هل صنّفتما العناصر نفسها ضمن 'تغيّر' مقابل 'ظل على حاله'؟","Where did you disagree about whether something changed a lot, a little, or not at all?":"أين اختلفتما حول ما إذا كان شيء ما قد تغيّر كثيرًا، أو قليلًا، أو لم يتغيّر على الإطلاق؟","Was 1954–1968 a genuine turning point, or the acceleration of a longer struggle? Use evidence from at least two sources, cite specific laws or events, and address at least one way change was incomplete.":"هل كانت الفترة 1954–1968 نقطة تحوّل حقيقية، أم تسريعًا لنضال أطول؟ استخدم أدلة من مصدرين على الأقل، واستشهد بقوانين أو أحداث محددة، وتناول طريقة واحدة على الأقل ظل بها التغيير غير مكتمل.","Explain the difference between de jure and de facto change using one example.":"اشرح الفرق بين التغيير de jure (بحكم القانون) و de facto (بحكم الأمر الواقع) باستخدام مثال واحد.","Connect a protest or event 'during' the movement to a law that came 'after' it.":"اربط احتجاجًا أو حدثًا وقع 'أثناء' الحركة بقانون صدر 'بعدها'.","Apply the continuity-and-change lens to a rights movement happening today. What has changed, and what has not?":"طبّق منظور الاستمرارية والتغيير على حركة حقوق تجري اليوم. ما الذي تغيّر وما الذي لم يتغيّر؟","Civil Rights Act (1964) — National Archives":"قانون الحقوق المدنية (Civil Rights Act، 1964) — الأرشيف الوطني","The 1964 law banning discrimination and outlawing segregation in public accommodations and employment.":"قانون عام 1964 الذي حظر التمييز وجرّم الفصل العنصري في المرافق العامة والتوظيف.","What did the Civil Rights Act make illegal?":"ما الذي جعله قانون الحقوق المدنية غير قانوني؟","What might a law like this not be able to change by itself?":"ما الذي قد لا يستطيع قانون كهذا تغييره بمفرده؟","Voting Rights Act (1965) — National Archives":"قانون حق التصويت (Voting Rights Act، 1965) — الأرشيف الوطني","The 1965 law outlawing literacy tests and authorizing federal oversight of voter registration.":"قانون عام 1965 الذي حظر اختبارات القراءة والكتابة وأجاز الإشراف الفيدرالي على تسجيل الناخبين.","How did this law try to protect the right to vote?":"كيف حاول هذا القانون حماية حق التصويت؟","Why might voting rights need federal enforcement?":"لماذا قد تحتاج حقوق التصويت إلى إنفاذ فيدرالي؟","Little Rock Central High School National Historic Site — National Park Service":"الموقع التاريخي الوطني لمدرسة ليتل روك سنترال الثانوية — هيئة المتنزهات الوطنية","How nine Black students integrated a school in 1957 and why federal troops were sent.":"كيف التحق تسعة طلاب سود بمدرسة عام 1957 ولماذا أُرسلت القوات الفيدرالية.","What did it take to enforce the court's desegregation order?":"ما الذي تطلّبه إنفاذ أمر المحكمة بإنهاء الفصل العنصري؟","What does this show about the gap between law and practice?":"ماذا يُظهر هذا عن الفجوة بين القانون والممارسة؟","Jim Crow laws and legally enforced segregation across the South":"قوانين جيم كرو والفصل العنصري المفروض قانونيًا في جميع أنحاء الجنوب","Plessy v. Ferguson (1896) 'separate but equal' doctrine":"مبدأ 'منفصلون لكن متساوون' في قضية Plessy v. Ferguson (1896)","Systematic Black disenfranchisement — poll taxes, literacy tests, white primaries, intimidation":"الحرمان الممنهج للسود من حق التصويت — ضرائب الاقتراع، اختبارات القراءة والكتابة، الانتخابات التمهيدية المقتصرة على البيض، والترهيب","Legal strategy in the courts (NAACP Legal Defense Fund; Brown v. Board, 1954)":"الاستراتيجية القانونية في المحاكم (صندوق الدفاع القانوني التابع لـ NAACP؛ Brown v. Board، 1954)","Nonviolent direct action — boycotts, sit-ins, Freedom Rides, marches":"العمل المباشر اللاعنفي — المقاطعات، والاعتصامات، ورحلات الحرية (Freedom Rides)، والمسيرات","Grassroots organizing (SCLC, SNCC, CORE, NAACP) and youth leadership":"التنظيم الشعبي القاعدي (SCLC، SNCC، CORE، NAACP) وقيادة الشباب","Federal intervention prompted by protest and violence (Little Rock; Selma → Voting Rights Act)":"التدخل الفيدرالي الذي دفع إليه الاحتجاج والعنف (ليتل روك؛ سلمى → قانون حق التصويت)","Landmark federal law: Civil Rights Act (1964), Voting Rights Act (1965), Fair Housing Act (1968)":"قوانين فيدرالية بارزة: قانون الحقوق المدنية (1964)، قانون حق التصويت (1965)، قانون الإسكان العادل (Fair Housing Act، 1968)","A sharp rise in Black voter registration and officeholding, especially in the South":"ارتفاع حاد في تسجيل الناخبين السود وتوليهم المناصب، خصوصًا في الجنوب","Persistent limits: de facto segregation, economic inequality, and later rollbacks (Shelby County v. Holder, 2013)":"قيود مستمرة: الفصل العنصري de facto (بحكم الأمر الواقع)، وعدم المساواة الاقتصادية، والتراجعات اللاحقة (Shelby County v. Holder، 2013)","The legal status of segregation and voting: federal law made de jure segregation and discriminatory voting tests illegal.":"الوضع القانوني للفصل العنصري والتصويت: جعل القانون الفيدرالي الفصل العنصري de jure (بحكم القانون) واختبارات التصويت التمييزية غير قانونية.","Actual desegregation of schools and public life, and the growth of Black political participation — over years, not overnight.":"الإنهاء الفعلي للفصل العنصري في المدارس والحياة العامة، ونمو المشاركة السياسية للسود — على مدى سنوات، وليس بين عشية وضحاها.","De facto segregation and deep economic disparities in housing, wealth, and schooling persisted despite legal change.":"استمر الفصل العنصري de facto (بحكم الأمر الواقع) والتفاوتات الاقتصادية العميقة في السكن والثروة والتعليم رغم التغيير القانوني.","Why did some conditions change quickly (the law on paper) while others changed slowly or barely at all (everyday economic and residential realities)? What is the difference between de jure and de facto change?":"لماذا تغيّرت بعض الأوضاع بسرعة (القانون على الورق) بينما تغيّرت أخرى ببطء أو لم تتغيّر تقريبًا (الحقائق الاقتصادية والسكنية اليومية)؟ ما الفرق بين التغيير de jure (بحكم القانون) و de facto (بحكم الأمر الواقع)؟"},"zh":{"The Civil Rights Movement":"民权运动","Weigh what changed, what changed slowly, and what stayed the same across the Civil Rights Movement (1954–1968), and judge whether it was a true turning point.":"权衡在民权运动（1954–1968）期间哪些发生了变化、哪些变化缓慢、哪些保持不变，并判断它是否是一个真正的转折点。","Between 1954 and 1968, courts, laws, and mass movements dismantled the legal framework of segregation. But law on paper and life on the ground are not the same thing. Compare before, during, and after — then judge: was this era a genuine turning point in U.S. history, or the acceleration of a longer struggle?":"在1954年至1968年间，法院、法律和群众运动瓦解了种族隔离的法律框架。但纸面上的法律与现实中的生活并不是一回事。比较之前、期间和之后——然后判断：这个时代是美国历史上一个真正的转折点，还是一场更长斗争的加速？","The United States":"美国","Compare your ledgers with a partner. Did you sort the same items into 'changed' vs. 'stayed the same'?":"与同伴比较你们的记录表。你们是否把相同的项目归入'发生变化'和'保持不变'？","Where did you disagree about whether something changed a lot, a little, or not at all?":"在某件事是变化很大、变化很小还是完全没有变化的问题上，你们在哪里产生了分歧？","Was 1954–1968 a genuine turning point, or the acceleration of a longer struggle? Use evidence from at least two sources, cite specific laws or events, and address at least one way change was incomplete.":"1954–1968年是一个真正的转折点，还是一场更长斗争的加速？请使用至少两个来源的证据，引用具体的法律或事件，并说明至少一种变化不完整的方式。","Explain the difference between de jure and de facto change using one example.":"用一个例子解释 de jure（法律上的）与 de facto（事实上的）变化之间的区别。","Connect a protest or event 'during' the movement to a law that came 'after' it.":"将运动'期间'的一次抗议或事件与'之后'出台的一项法律联系起来。","Apply the continuity-and-change lens to a rights movement happening today. What has changed, and what has not?":"将连续性与变化的视角应用于当今正在发生的某个权利运动。什么改变了，什么没有改变？","Civil Rights Act (1964) — National Archives":"《民权法案》（Civil Rights Act，1964）——美国国家档案馆","The 1964 law banning discrimination and outlawing segregation in public accommodations and employment.":"1964年的法律，禁止歧视，并将公共场所和就业中的种族隔离定为非法。","What did the Civil Rights Act make illegal?":"《民权法案》将什么定为非法？","What might a law like this not be able to change by itself?":"像这样的一部法律本身可能无法改变什么？","Voting Rights Act (1965) — National Archives":"《投票权法案》（Voting Rights Act，1965）——美国国家档案馆","The 1965 law outlawing literacy tests and authorizing federal oversight of voter registration.":"1965年的法律，取缔识字测试，并授权联邦政府监督选民登记。","How did this law try to protect the right to vote?":"这部法律是如何尝试保护投票权的？","Why might voting rights need federal enforcement?":"为什么投票权可能需要联邦的强制执行？","Little Rock Central High School National Historic Site — National Park Service":"小石城中央高中国家历史遗址——美国国家公园管理局","How nine Black students integrated a school in 1957 and why federal troops were sent.":"九名黑人学生如何在1957年融入一所学校，以及为何派遣了联邦军队。","What did it take to enforce the court's desegregation order?":"执行法院的废除种族隔离命令需要付出什么？","What does this show about the gap between law and practice?":"这说明了法律与实践之间的差距有何问题？","Jim Crow laws and legally enforced segregation across the South":"吉姆·克劳法以及南方各地依法强制实施的种族隔离","Plessy v. Ferguson (1896) 'separate but equal' doctrine":"普莱西诉弗格森案（Plessy v. Ferguson，1896）的'隔离但平等'原则","Systematic Black disenfranchisement — poll taxes, literacy tests, white primaries, intimidation":"对黑人有系统的选举权剥夺——人头税、识字测试、白人初选、恐吓","Legal strategy in the courts (NAACP Legal Defense Fund; Brown v. Board, 1954)":"在法庭上的法律策略（全国有色人种协进会法律辩护基金；布朗诉教育委员会案 Brown v. Board，1954）","Nonviolent direct action — boycotts, sit-ins, Freedom Rides, marches":"非暴力直接行动——抵制、静坐、自由乘车运动（Freedom Rides）、游行","Grassroots organizing (SCLC, SNCC, CORE, NAACP) and youth leadership":"基层组织（SCLC、SNCC、CORE、NAACP）与青年领导","Federal intervention prompted by protest and violence (Little Rock; Selma → Voting Rights Act)":"由抗议和暴力促成的联邦干预（小石城；塞尔玛 Selma → 《投票权法案》）","Landmark federal law: Civil Rights Act (1964), Voting Rights Act (1965), Fair Housing Act (1968)":"具有里程碑意义的联邦法律：《民权法案》（1964）、《投票权法案》（1965）、《公平住房法案》（Fair Housing Act，1968）","A sharp rise in Black voter registration and officeholding, especially in the South":"黑人选民登记和担任公职人数的急剧上升，尤其是在南方","Persistent limits: de facto segregation, economic inequality, and later rollbacks (Shelby County v. Holder, 2013)":"持续存在的局限：de facto（事实上的）种族隔离、经济不平等，以及后来的倒退（谢尔比县诉霍尔德案 Shelby County v. Holder，2013）","The legal status of segregation and voting: federal law made de jure segregation and discriminatory voting tests illegal.":"种族隔离与投票的法律地位：联邦法律将 de jure（法律上的）种族隔离和歧视性的投票测试定为非法。","Actual desegregation of schools and public life, and the growth of Black political participation — over years, not overnight.":"学校和公共生活中真正的废除种族隔离，以及黑人政治参与的增长——历经数年，而非一夜之间。","De facto segregation and deep economic disparities in housing, wealth, and schooling persisted despite legal change.":"尽管法律发生了变化，de facto（事实上的）种族隔离以及住房、财富和教育方面的深刻经济差距依然存在。","Why did some conditions change quickly (the law on paper) while others changed slowly or barely at all (everyday economic and residential realities)? What is the difference between de jure and de facto change?":"为什么有些状况变化迅速（纸面上的法律），而另一些却变化缓慢甚至几乎没有变化（日常的经济和居住现实）？de jure（法律上的）与 de facto（事实上的）变化之间有什么区别？"},"ur":{"The Civil Rights Movement":"شہری حقوق کی تحریک","Weigh what changed, what changed slowly, and what stayed the same across the Civil Rights Movement (1954–1968), and judge whether it was a true turning point.":"غور کریں کہ شہری حقوق کی تحریک (1954–1968) کے دوران کیا تبدیل ہوا، کیا آہستہ آہستہ تبدیل ہوا، اور کیا برقرار رہا، اور فیصلہ کریں کہ آیا یہ ایک حقیقی موڑ تھا۔","Between 1954 and 1968, courts, laws, and mass movements dismantled the legal framework of segregation. But law on paper and life on the ground are not the same thing. Compare before, during, and after — then judge: was this era a genuine turning point in U.S. history, or the acceleration of a longer struggle?":"1954 اور 1968 کے درمیان، عدالتوں، قوانین اور عوامی تحریکوں نے علیحدگی کے قانونی ڈھانچے کو ختم کر دیا۔ لیکن کاغذ پر قانون اور زمینی زندگی ایک جیسی چیز نہیں ہیں۔ پہلے، دوران اور بعد کا موازنہ کریں — پھر فیصلہ کریں: کیا یہ دور امریکی تاریخ میں ایک حقیقی موڑ تھا، یا ایک طویل جدوجہد کی رفتار میں اضافہ؟","The United States":"ریاستہائے متحدہ امریکہ","Compare your ledgers with a partner. Did you sort the same items into 'changed' vs. 'stayed the same'?":"اپنے کھاتوں کا کسی ساتھی کے ساتھ موازنہ کریں۔ کیا آپ نے وہی اشیاء 'تبدیل ہوا' بمقابلہ 'برقرار رہا' میں رکھیں؟","Where did you disagree about whether something changed a lot, a little, or not at all?":"آپ نے کہاں اختلاف کیا کہ آیا کوئی چیز بہت زیادہ، تھوڑی، یا بالکل بھی تبدیل نہیں ہوئی؟","Was 1954–1968 a genuine turning point, or the acceleration of a longer struggle? Use evidence from at least two sources, cite specific laws or events, and address at least one way change was incomplete.":"کیا 1954–1968 ایک حقیقی موڑ تھا، یا ایک طویل جدوجہد کی رفتار میں اضافہ؟ کم از کم دو ذرائع سے شواہد استعمال کریں، مخصوص قوانین یا واقعات کا حوالہ دیں، اور کم از کم ایک ایسا پہلو بیان کریں جس میں تبدیلی نامکمل رہی۔","Explain the difference between de jure and de facto change using one example.":"ایک مثال کے ذریعے de jure (بلحاظِ قانون) اور de facto (بلحاظِ حقیقت) تبدیلی کے درمیان فرق بیان کریں۔","Connect a protest or event 'during' the movement to a law that came 'after' it.":"تحریک کے 'دوران' کسی احتجاج یا واقعے کو اس کے 'بعد' آنے والے کسی قانون سے جوڑیں۔","Apply the continuity-and-change lens to a rights movement happening today. What has changed, and what has not?":"تسلسل اور تبدیلی کے زاویے کو آج جاری کسی حقوق کی تحریک پر لاگو کریں۔ کیا تبدیل ہوا ہے، اور کیا نہیں؟","Civil Rights Act (1964) — National Archives":"شہری حقوق کا قانون (Civil Rights Act، 1964) — نیشنل آرکائیوز","The 1964 law banning discrimination and outlawing segregation in public accommodations and employment.":"1964 کا قانون جس نے امتیازی سلوک پر پابندی لگائی اور عوامی مقامات اور روزگار میں علیحدگی کو غیر قانونی قرار دیا۔","What did the Civil Rights Act make illegal?":"شہری حقوق کے قانون نے کیا چیز غیر قانونی قرار دی؟","What might a law like this not be able to change by itself?":"اس جیسا قانون خود بخود کیا چیز تبدیل نہ کر سکے؟","Voting Rights Act (1965) — National Archives":"حقِ رائے دہی کا قانون (Voting Rights Act، 1965) — نیشنل آرکائیوز","The 1965 law outlawing literacy tests and authorizing federal oversight of voter registration.":"1965 کا قانون جس نے خواندگی کے امتحانات کو غیر قانونی قرار دیا اور ووٹر رجسٹریشن پر وفاقی نگرانی کی اجازت دی۔","How did this law try to protect the right to vote?":"اس قانون نے حقِ رائے دہی کے تحفظ کی کوشش کیسے کی؟","Why might voting rights need federal enforcement?":"حقِ رائے دہی کو وفاقی نفاذ کی ضرورت کیوں پیش آ سکتی ہے؟","Little Rock Central High School National Historic Site — National Park Service":"لٹل راک سینٹرل ہائی اسکول قومی تاریخی مقام — نیشنل پارک سروس","How nine Black students integrated a school in 1957 and why federal troops were sent.":"کیسے نو سیاہ فام طلبہ نے 1957 میں ایک اسکول میں شمولیت اختیار کی اور وفاقی فوج کیوں بھیجی گئی۔","What did it take to enforce the court's desegregation order?":"عدالت کے علیحدگی ختم کرنے کے حکم کو نافذ کرنے کے لیے کیا کچھ درکار تھا؟","What does this show about the gap between law and practice?":"یہ قانون اور عمل کے درمیان فرق کے بارے میں کیا ظاہر کرتا ہے؟","Jim Crow laws and legally enforced segregation across the South":"جِم کرو قوانین اور پورے جنوب میں قانونی طور پر نافذ کردہ علیحدگی","Plessy v. Ferguson (1896) 'separate but equal' doctrine":"پلیسی بمقابلہ فرگوسن (Plessy v. Ferguson، 1896) کا 'علیحدہ مگر برابر' اصول","Systematic Black disenfranchisement — poll taxes, literacy tests, white primaries, intimidation":"سیاہ فاموں سے منظم طریقے سے حقِ رائے دہی چھیننا — پول ٹیکس، خواندگی کے امتحانات، صرف سفید فام پرائمری، اور دھمکیاں","Legal strategy in the courts (NAACP Legal Defense Fund; Brown v. Board, 1954)":"عدالتوں میں قانونی حکمتِ عملی (NAACP لیگل ڈیفنس فنڈ؛ Brown v. Board، 1954)","Nonviolent direct action — boycotts, sit-ins, Freedom Rides, marches":"عدم تشدد پر مبنی براہِ راست کارروائی — بائیکاٹ، دھرنے، فریڈم رائیڈز (Freedom Rides)، اور مارچ","Grassroots organizing (SCLC, SNCC, CORE, NAACP) and youth leadership":"زمینی سطح پر تنظیم سازی (SCLC، SNCC، CORE، NAACP) اور نوجوانوں کی قیادت","Federal intervention prompted by protest and violence (Little Rock; Selma → Voting Rights Act)":"احتجاج اور تشدد کے باعث وفاقی مداخلت (لٹل راک؛ سیلما Selma → حقِ رائے دہی کا قانون)","Landmark federal law: Civil Rights Act (1964), Voting Rights Act (1965), Fair Housing Act (1968)":"سنگِ میل وفاقی قوانین: شہری حقوق کا قانون (1964)، حقِ رائے دہی کا قانون (1965)، منصفانہ رہائش کا قانون (Fair Housing Act، 1968)","A sharp rise in Black voter registration and officeholding, especially in the South":"سیاہ فام ووٹروں کی رجسٹریشن اور عہدوں پر فائز ہونے میں تیز اضافہ، خاص طور پر جنوب میں","Persistent limits: de facto segregation, economic inequality, and later rollbacks (Shelby County v. Holder, 2013)":"مستقل حدود: de facto (بلحاظِ حقیقت) علیحدگی، معاشی عدم مساوات، اور بعد کے پسپائیاں (Shelby County v. Holder، 2013)","The legal status of segregation and voting: federal law made de jure segregation and discriminatory voting tests illegal.":"علیحدگی اور ووٹنگ کی قانونی حیثیت: وفاقی قانون نے de jure (بلحاظِ قانون) علیحدگی اور امتیازی ووٹنگ ٹیسٹوں کو غیر قانونی قرار دیا۔","Actual desegregation of schools and public life, and the growth of Black political participation — over years, not overnight.":"اسکولوں اور عوامی زندگی میں علیحدگی کا حقیقی خاتمہ، اور سیاہ فاموں کی سیاسی شرکت میں اضافہ — برسوں کے دوران، راتوں رات نہیں۔","De facto segregation and deep economic disparities in housing, wealth, and schooling persisted despite legal change.":"قانونی تبدیلی کے باوجود de facto (بلحاظِ حقیقت) علیحدگی اور رہائش، دولت اور تعلیم میں گہرے معاشی تفاوت برقرار رہے۔","Why did some conditions change quickly (the law on paper) while others changed slowly or barely at all (everyday economic and residential realities)? What is the difference between de jure and de facto change?":"کچھ حالات تیزی سے کیوں تبدیل ہوئے (کاغذ پر قانون) جبکہ دیگر آہستہ یا بمشکل ہی تبدیل ہوئے (روزمرہ کی معاشی اور رہائشی حقیقتیں)؟ de jure (بلحاظِ قانون) اور de facto (بلحاظِ حقیقت) تبدیلی کے درمیان کیا فرق ہے؟"},"hi":{"The Civil Rights Movement":"नागरिक अधिकार आंदोलन","Weigh what changed, what changed slowly, and what stayed the same across the Civil Rights Movement (1954–1968), and judge whether it was a true turning point.":"आकलन करें कि नागरिक अधिकार आंदोलन (1954–1968) के दौरान क्या बदला, क्या धीरे-धीरे बदला और क्या वैसा ही रहा, और यह निर्णय करें कि क्या यह एक सच्चा निर्णायक मोड़ था।","Between 1954 and 1968, courts, laws, and mass movements dismantled the legal framework of segregation. But law on paper and life on the ground are not the same thing. Compare before, during, and after — then judge: was this era a genuine turning point in U.S. history, or the acceleration of a longer struggle?":"1954 और 1968 के बीच, अदालतों, कानूनों और जन आंदोलनों ने अलगाव के कानूनी ढांचे को ध्वस्त कर दिया। लेकिन कागज़ पर कानून और ज़मीनी हकीकत एक चीज़ नहीं हैं। पहले, दौरान और बाद की तुलना करें — फिर निर्णय करें: क्या यह युग अमेरिकी इतिहास में एक वास्तविक निर्णायक मोड़ था, या एक लंबे संघर्ष की गति में तेज़ी?","The United States":"संयुक्त राज्य अमेरिका","Compare your ledgers with a partner. Did you sort the same items into 'changed' vs. 'stayed the same'?":"अपने अभिलेखों की तुलना किसी साथी के साथ करें। क्या आपने वही वस्तुएँ 'बदल गया' बनाम 'वैसा ही रहा' में छाँटीं?","Where did you disagree about whether something changed a lot, a little, or not at all?":"आप कहाँ असहमत थे कि कोई चीज़ बहुत बदली, थोड़ी बदली, या बिल्कुल नहीं बदली?","Was 1954–1968 a genuine turning point, or the acceleration of a longer struggle? Use evidence from at least two sources, cite specific laws or events, and address at least one way change was incomplete.":"क्या 1954–1968 एक सच्चा निर्णायक मोड़ था, या एक लंबे संघर्ष की गति में तेज़ी? कम से कम दो स्रोतों से साक्ष्य का उपयोग करें, विशिष्ट कानूनों या घटनाओं का हवाला दें, और कम से कम एक तरीका बताएँ जिसमें परिवर्तन अधूरा रहा।","Explain the difference between de jure and de facto change using one example.":"एक उदाहरण का उपयोग करते हुए de jure (कानूनी रूप से) और de facto (व्यवहार में) परिवर्तन के बीच अंतर समझाएँ।","Connect a protest or event 'during' the movement to a law that came 'after' it.":"आंदोलन के 'दौरान' हुए किसी विरोध या घटना को उसके 'बाद' आए किसी कानून से जोड़ें।","Apply the continuity-and-change lens to a rights movement happening today. What has changed, and what has not?":"निरंतरता और परिवर्तन के दृष्टिकोण को आज हो रहे किसी अधिकार आंदोलन पर लागू करें। क्या बदला है, और क्या नहीं?","Civil Rights Act (1964) — National Archives":"नागरिक अधिकार अधिनियम (Civil Rights Act, 1964) — नेशनल आर्काइव्स","The 1964 law banning discrimination and outlawing segregation in public accommodations and employment.":"1964 का कानून जिसने भेदभाव पर रोक लगाई और सार्वजनिक सुविधाओं तथा रोजगार में अलगाव को अवैध घोषित किया।","What did the Civil Rights Act make illegal?":"नागरिक अधिकार अधिनियम ने क्या अवैध बनाया?","What might a law like this not be able to change by itself?":"इस तरह का कानून अपने आप क्या नहीं बदल पाएगा?","Voting Rights Act (1965) — National Archives":"मताधिकार अधिनियम (Voting Rights Act, 1965) — नेशनल आर्काइव्स","The 1965 law outlawing literacy tests and authorizing federal oversight of voter registration.":"1965 का कानून जिसने साक्षरता परीक्षणों को अवैध ठहराया और मतदाता पंजीकरण की संघीय निगरानी को अधिकृत किया।","How did this law try to protect the right to vote?":"इस कानून ने मतदान के अधिकार की रक्षा करने का प्रयास कैसे किया?","Why might voting rights need federal enforcement?":"मताधिकार को संघीय प्रवर्तन की आवश्यकता क्यों पड़ सकती है?","Little Rock Central High School National Historic Site — National Park Service":"लिटिल रॉक सेंट्रल हाई स्कूल राष्ट्रीय ऐतिहासिक स्थल — नेशनल पार्क सर्विस","How nine Black students integrated a school in 1957 and why federal troops were sent.":"कैसे नौ अश्वेत छात्रों ने 1957 में एक स्कूल में एकीकरण किया और संघीय सैनिक क्यों भेजे गए।","What did it take to enforce the court's desegregation order?":"अदालत के अलगाव-समाप्ति आदेश को लागू करने के लिए क्या करना पड़ा?","What does this show about the gap between law and practice?":"यह कानून और व्यवहार के बीच की खाई के बारे में क्या दर्शाता है?","Jim Crow laws and legally enforced segregation across the South":"जिम क्रो कानून और पूरे दक्षिण में कानूनी रूप से लागू अलगाव","Plessy v. Ferguson (1896) 'separate but equal' doctrine":"प्लेसी बनाम फर्ग्यूसन (Plessy v. Ferguson, 1896) का 'पृथक किन्तु समान' सिद्धांत","Systematic Black disenfranchisement — poll taxes, literacy tests, white primaries, intimidation":"अश्वेतों का व्यवस्थित मताधिकार-हरण — मतदान कर, साक्षरता परीक्षण, केवल श्वेत प्राइमरी, और डराना-धमकाना","Legal strategy in the courts (NAACP Legal Defense Fund; Brown v. Board, 1954)":"अदालतों में कानूनी रणनीति (NAACP कानूनी रक्षा कोष; Brown v. Board, 1954)","Nonviolent direct action — boycotts, sit-ins, Freedom Rides, marches":"अहिंसक प्रत्यक्ष कार्रवाई — बहिष्कार, धरने, स्वतंत्रता यात्राएँ (Freedom Rides), और मार्च","Grassroots organizing (SCLC, SNCC, CORE, NAACP) and youth leadership":"जमीनी स्तर पर संगठन (SCLC, SNCC, CORE, NAACP) और युवा नेतृत्व","Federal intervention prompted by protest and violence (Little Rock; Selma → Voting Rights Act)":"विरोध और हिंसा से प्रेरित संघीय हस्तक्षेप (लिटिल रॉक; सेल्मा Selma → मताधिकार अधिनियम)","Landmark federal law: Civil Rights Act (1964), Voting Rights Act (1965), Fair Housing Act (1968)":"ऐतिहासिक संघीय कानून: नागरिक अधिकार अधिनियम (1964), मताधिकार अधिनियम (1965), निष्पक्ष आवास अधिनियम (Fair Housing Act, 1968)","A sharp rise in Black voter registration and officeholding, especially in the South":"अश्वेत मतदाता पंजीकरण और सार्वजनिक पदों पर आसीन होने में तीव्र वृद्धि, विशेषकर दक्षिण में","Persistent limits: de facto segregation, economic inequality, and later rollbacks (Shelby County v. Holder, 2013)":"लगातार बनी रहने वाली सीमाएँ: de facto (व्यवहार में) अलगाव, आर्थिक असमानता, और बाद में हुई वापसी (Shelby County v. Holder, 2013)","The legal status of segregation and voting: federal law made de jure segregation and discriminatory voting tests illegal.":"अलगाव और मतदान की कानूनी स्थिति: संघीय कानून ने de jure (कानूनी रूप से) अलगाव और भेदभावपूर्ण मतदान परीक्षणों को अवैध बना दिया।","Actual desegregation of schools and public life, and the growth of Black political participation — over years, not overnight.":"स्कूलों और सार्वजनिक जीवन में वास्तविक अलगाव-समाप्ति, और अश्वेतों की राजनीतिक भागीदारी में वृद्धि — वर्षों में, रातोंरात नहीं।","De facto segregation and deep economic disparities in housing, wealth, and schooling persisted despite legal change.":"कानूनी बदलाव के बावजूद de facto (व्यवहार में) अलगाव और आवास, संपत्ति तथा शिक्षा में गहरी आर्थिक असमानताएँ बनी रहीं।","Why did some conditions change quickly (the law on paper) while others changed slowly or barely at all (everyday economic and residential realities)? What is the difference between de jure and de facto change?":"कुछ स्थितियाँ तेज़ी से क्यों बदलीं (कागज़ पर कानून) जबकि अन्य धीरे-धीरे या मुश्किल से ही बदलीं (रोज़मर्रा की आर्थिक और आवासीय वास्तविकताएँ)? de jure (कानूनी रूप से) और de facto (व्यवहार में) परिवर्तन के बीच क्या अंतर है?"}},"cold-war-origins":{"es":{"What Caused the Cold War?":"¿Qué causó la Guerra Fría?","Build an evidence-based answer to a contested question: what caused the Cold War, and who bears more responsibility for its onset?":"Construye una respuesta basada en evidencia para una pregunta debatida: ¿qué causó la Guerra Fría y quién tiene mayor responsabilidad en su inicio?","By 1946 the wartime alliance between the United States and the Soviet Union had collapsed into mutual suspicion. Historians agree on the sequence of events but disagree sharply about the cause — and about who was more responsible. Weigh the evidence, note what conflicts and what is missing, and build a defensible working conclusion.":"Para 1946, la alianza de guerra entre los Estados Unidos y la Unión Soviética se había desmoronado en una desconfianza mutua. Los historiadores coinciden en la secuencia de los acontecimientos, pero discrepan profundamente sobre la causa —y sobre quién fue más responsable—. Sopesa la evidencia, observa lo que se contradice y lo que falta, y construye una conclusión provisional defendible.","The Origins of the Cold War":"Los orígenes de la Guerra Fría","United States, Soviet Union, and a divided Europe":"Estados Unidos, la Unión Soviética y una Europa dividida","Compare your evidence cards with a partner. Did you rate the same sources as reliable?":"Compara tus tarjetas de evidencia con un compañero. ¿Calificaron como confiables las mismas fuentes?","Did you and your partner lean toward the same 'school' of interpretation? What evidence moved you?":"¿Tú y tu compañero se inclinaron hacia la misma 'escuela' de interpretación? ¿Qué evidencia los influyó?","Write a working conclusion answering the historical question. Cite at least two evidence cards, acknowledge conflicting interpretations, and note one limitation of your evidence.":"Escribe una conclusión provisional que responda a la pregunta histórica. Cita al menos dos tarjetas de evidencia, reconoce las interpretaciones contradictorias y señala una limitación de tu evidencia.","State, in one sentence, your working answer to what caused the Cold War.":"Expón, en una sola oración, tu respuesta provisional sobre qué causó la Guerra Fría.","Connect the Truman Doctrine and the Novikov Telegram — how does each side justify itself?":"Relaciona la Doctrina Truman y el Telegrama de Novikov: ¿cómo se justifica cada bando?","Apply the idea of a 'security dilemma' to a rivalry between two countries today.":"Aplica la idea de un 'dilema de seguridad' a una rivalidad entre dos países en la actualidad.","Kennan and Containment, 1947 — Office of the Historian, U.S. Dept. of State":"Kennan y la contención, 1947 — Oficina del Historiador, Departamento de Estado de EE. UU.","Government history of Kennan's 'long telegram' and the birth of containment.":"Historia oficial del 'largo telegrama' de Kennan y el nacimiento de la contención.","How did Kennan explain Soviet behavior?":"¿Cómo explicó Kennan el comportamiento soviético?","How reliable is a single diplomat's analysis of a rival power?":"¿Cuán confiable es el análisis de un solo diplomático sobre una potencia rival?","Truman Doctrine — Harry S. Truman Library":"Doctrina Truman — Biblioteca Harry S. Truman","Truman's March 1947 message requesting aid for Greece and Turkey.":"El mensaje de Truman de marzo de 1947 solicitando ayuda para Grecia y Turquía.","How does Truman frame the choice facing the world?":"¿Cómo plantea Truman la disyuntiva que enfrenta el mundo?","What might this speech leave out or exaggerate?":"¿Qué podría omitir o exagerar este discurso?","Telegram from Nikolai Novikov to the Soviet Leadership (Sept. 1946) — Wilson Center Digital Archive":"Telegrama de Nikolái Novikov a la dirigencia soviética (septiembre de 1946) — Archivo Digital del Wilson Center","The Soviet ambassador's warning that the U.S. sought global domination.":"La advertencia del embajador soviético de que EE. UU. buscaba el dominio global.","How does the Soviet view mirror the American one?":"¿De qué manera la visión soviética refleja la estadounidense?","Why is it important to read both sides' cables?":"¿Por qué es importante leer los telegramas de ambos bandos?","What caused the Cold War — and who bears more responsibility for its onset (roughly 1945–1950): the United States or the Soviet Union?":"¿Qué causó la Guerra Fría —y quién tiene mayor responsabilidad en su inicio (aproximadamente 1945–1950): los Estados Unidos o la Unión Soviética?","By 1945–46 the alliance had collapsed over the political future of Eastern Europe (especially Poland) and occupied Germany. Between 1947 and 1949 the US adopted containment (Truman Doctrine, Marshall Plan, NATO) while the USSR consolidated Eastern Europe and rejected the Marshall Plan. Both sides genuinely feared the other.":"Para 1945–46, la alianza se había derrumbado por el futuro político de Europa del Este (especialmente Polonia) y la Alemania ocupada. Entre 1947 y 1949, Estados Unidos adoptó la contención (Doctrina Truman, Plan Marshall, OTAN), mientras que la URSS consolidaba Europa del Este y rechazaba el Plan Marshall. Ambos bandos temían genuinamente al otro.","Kennan's 'Long Telegram' (Feb. 1946)":"El 'largo telegrama' de Kennan (febrero de 1946)","Primary — U.S. diplomatic cable":"Fuente primaria — telegrama diplomático estadounidense","A senior U.S. diplomat argues Soviet hostility comes from ideology plus historic Russian insecurity, and must be met with long-term 'containment.'":"Un alto diplomático estadounidense sostiene que la hostilidad soviética proviene de la ideología sumada a una histórica inseguridad rusa, y que debe enfrentarse con una 'contención' a largo plazo.","It became the intellectual foundation of U.S. Cold War strategy — it shows how American policymakers interpreted Soviet behavior.":"Se convirtió en el fundamento intelectual de la estrategia estadounidense en la Guerra Fría: muestra cómo los responsables políticos estadounidenses interpretaban el comportamiento soviético.","One official's analysis, written to persuade Washington; it reads Soviet intentions from the outside, not from Soviet records.":"El análisis de un solo funcionario, escrito para persuadir a Washington; interpreta las intenciones soviéticas desde afuera, no a partir de los archivos soviéticos.","Truman Doctrine Address to Congress (March 12, 1947)":"Discurso de la Doctrina Truman ante el Congreso (12 de marzo de 1947)","Primary — presidential speech":"Fuente primaria — discurso presidencial","Truman frames world affairs as a choice between 'free' and 'totalitarian' ways of life and commits U.S. aid to nations resisting communism.":"Truman plantea los asuntos mundiales como una elección entre modos de vida 'libres' y 'totalitarios' y compromete la ayuda estadounidense a las naciones que resisten el comunismo.","Marks the public, global turn to containment and shows how the U.S. justified its commitments ideologically.":"Marca el giro público y global hacia la contención y muestra cómo Estados Unidos justificó ideológicamente sus compromisos.","Political rhetoric designed to win funding; scholars argue it may have overstated the threat and universalized a specific crisis.":"Retórica política diseñada para obtener financiación; los estudiosos sostienen que pudo haber exagerado la amenaza y universalizado una crisis concreta.","Novikov Telegram (Sept. 27, 1946)":"Telegrama de Novikov (27 de septiembre de 1946)","Primary — Soviet diplomatic cable":"Fuente primaria — telegrama diplomático soviético","The Soviet ambassador argues the United States is seeking global military and economic domination — the mirror image of Kennan's warning.":"El embajador soviético sostiene que Estados Unidos busca el dominio militar y económico global: la imagen especular de la advertencia de Kennan.","Documents the Soviet side's fears, essential for weighing responsibility fairly rather than one-sidedly.":"Documenta los temores del bando soviético, esenciales para sopesar la responsabilidad de manera justa y no unilateral.","Also one diplomat's interpretation; historians debate how much it reflected Stalin's actual thinking, and it too reads the adversary from the outside.":"También es la interpretación de un solo diplomático; los historiadores debaten en qué medida reflejaba el pensamiento real de Stalin, y también interpreta al adversario desde afuera.","Historians divide into schools. Orthodox interpretations blame Soviet expansionism; revisionist interpretations emphasize U.S. economic interests and 'atomic diplomacy'; post-revisionists stress a mutual security dilemma with shared responsibility. The same events (Marshall Plan, Berlin) read as defensive or provocative depending on the lens.":"Los historiadores se dividen en escuelas. Las interpretaciones ortodoxas culpan al expansionismo soviético; las interpretaciones revisionistas enfatizan los intereses económicos de EE. UU. y la 'diplomacia atómica'; los posrevisionistas subrayan un dilema de seguridad mutuo con responsabilidad compartida. Los mismos hechos (Plan Marshall, Berlín) se leen como defensivos o provocadores según el enfoque.","The biggest gap is direct evidence of Soviet internal decision-making — Stalin's private calculations and Politburo deliberations. Soviet records opened only partially after 1991, so interpretation long tilted toward the fuller U.S. archive.":"La mayor laguna es la evidencia directa de la toma de decisiones interna soviética: los cálculos privados de Stalin y las deliberaciones del Politburó. Los archivos soviéticos solo se abrieron parcialmente después de 1991, por lo que la interpretación se inclinó durante mucho tiempo hacia el archivo estadounidense, más completo.","One defensible interpretation (not the only one): the Cold War arose less from a single aggressor than from a security dilemma — Soviet insistence on a controlled buffer zone collided with U.S. commitment to open, capitalist democracies, and each read the other's defensive moves as offensive. A student could reasonably weight responsibility toward either side using the same evidence.":"Una interpretación defendible (no la única): la Guerra Fría surgió menos de un único agresor que de un dilema de seguridad. La insistencia soviética en una zona de amortiguación controlada chocó con el compromiso estadounidense con democracias abiertas y capitalistas, y cada bando interpretó las medidas defensivas del otro como ofensivas. Un estudiante podría razonablemente inclinar la responsabilidad hacia cualquiera de los dos bandos usando la misma evidencia."},"vi":{"What Caused the Cold War?":"Điều gì đã gây ra Chiến tranh Lạnh?","Build an evidence-based answer to a contested question: what caused the Cold War, and who bears more responsibility for its onset?":"Xây dựng một câu trả lời dựa trên bằng chứng cho một câu hỏi còn gây tranh cãi: điều gì đã gây ra Chiến tranh Lạnh, và ai phải chịu trách nhiệm nhiều hơn cho sự khởi đầu của nó?","By 1946 the wartime alliance between the United States and the Soviet Union had collapsed into mutual suspicion. Historians agree on the sequence of events but disagree sharply about the cause — and about who was more responsible. Weigh the evidence, note what conflicts and what is missing, and build a defensible working conclusion.":"Đến năm 1946, liên minh thời chiến giữa Hoa Kỳ và Liên Xô đã sụp đổ thành sự nghi kỵ lẫn nhau. Các nhà sử học đồng ý về trình tự các sự kiện nhưng bất đồng sâu sắc về nguyên nhân — và về việc ai phải chịu trách nhiệm nhiều hơn. Hãy cân nhắc bằng chứng, ghi nhận điều gì mâu thuẫn và điều gì còn thiếu, rồi xây dựng một kết luận sơ bộ có thể bảo vệ được.","The Origins of the Cold War":"Nguồn gốc của Chiến tranh Lạnh","United States, Soviet Union, and a divided Europe":"Hoa Kỳ, Liên Xô, và một châu Âu bị chia cắt","Compare your evidence cards with a partner. Did you rate the same sources as reliable?":"So sánh các thẻ bằng chứng của bạn với một người bạn cùng học. Các bạn có đánh giá cùng những nguồn nào là đáng tin cậy không?","Did you and your partner lean toward the same 'school' of interpretation? What evidence moved you?":"Bạn và người cùng học có nghiêng về cùng một 'trường phái' diễn giải không? Bằng chứng nào đã tác động đến bạn?","Write a working conclusion answering the historical question. Cite at least two evidence cards, acknowledge conflicting interpretations, and note one limitation of your evidence.":"Viết một kết luận sơ bộ trả lời câu hỏi lịch sử. Trích dẫn ít nhất hai thẻ bằng chứng, thừa nhận những cách diễn giải mâu thuẫn, và nêu một hạn chế trong bằng chứng của bạn.","State, in one sentence, your working answer to what caused the Cold War.":"Trình bày, trong một câu, câu trả lời sơ bộ của bạn về điều gì đã gây ra Chiến tranh Lạnh.","Connect the Truman Doctrine and the Novikov Telegram — how does each side justify itself?":"Kết nối Học thuyết Truman và Bức điện tín Novikov — mỗi bên biện minh cho mình như thế nào?","Apply the idea of a 'security dilemma' to a rivalry between two countries today.":"Áp dụng khái niệm 'thế lưỡng nan an ninh' vào một cuộc cạnh tranh giữa hai quốc gia hiện nay.","Kennan and Containment, 1947 — Office of the Historian, U.S. Dept. of State":"Kennan và chính sách ngăn chặn, 1947 — Văn phòng Sử gia, Bộ Ngoại giao Hoa Kỳ","Government history of Kennan's 'long telegram' and the birth of containment.":"Lịch sử chính thức của 'bức điện tín dài' của Kennan và sự ra đời của chính sách ngăn chặn.","How did Kennan explain Soviet behavior?":"Kennan đã giải thích hành vi của Liên Xô như thế nào?","How reliable is a single diplomat's analysis of a rival power?":"Phân tích của một nhà ngoại giao đơn lẻ về một cường quốc đối địch đáng tin cậy đến mức nào?","Truman Doctrine — Harry S. Truman Library":"Học thuyết Truman — Thư viện Harry S. Truman","Truman's March 1947 message requesting aid for Greece and Turkey.":"Thông điệp tháng 3 năm 1947 của Truman yêu cầu viện trợ cho Hy Lạp và Thổ Nhĩ Kỳ.","How does Truman frame the choice facing the world?":"Truman đã định hình lựa chọn mà thế giới đang đối mặt như thế nào?","What might this speech leave out or exaggerate?":"Bài diễn văn này có thể bỏ sót hoặc phóng đại điều gì?","Telegram from Nikolai Novikov to the Soviet Leadership (Sept. 1946) — Wilson Center Digital Archive":"Bức điện tín của Nikolai Novikov gửi Ban lãnh đạo Liên Xô (tháng 9 năm 1946) — Kho lưu trữ Kỹ thuật số của Wilson Center","The Soviet ambassador's warning that the U.S. sought global domination.":"Lời cảnh báo của đại sứ Liên Xô rằng Hoa Kỳ đang tìm kiếm sự thống trị toàn cầu.","How does the Soviet view mirror the American one?":"Quan điểm của Liên Xô phản chiếu quan điểm của Mỹ như thế nào?","Why is it important to read both sides' cables?":"Tại sao việc đọc điện tín của cả hai bên lại quan trọng?","What caused the Cold War — and who bears more responsibility for its onset (roughly 1945–1950): the United States or the Soviet Union?":"Điều gì đã gây ra Chiến tranh Lạnh — và ai phải chịu trách nhiệm nhiều hơn cho sự khởi đầu của nó (khoảng 1945–1950): Hoa Kỳ hay Liên Xô?","By 1945–46 the alliance had collapsed over the political future of Eastern Europe (especially Poland) and occupied Germany. Between 1947 and 1949 the US adopted containment (Truman Doctrine, Marshall Plan, NATO) while the USSR consolidated Eastern Europe and rejected the Marshall Plan. Both sides genuinely feared the other.":"Đến năm 1945–46, liên minh đã sụp đổ vì tương lai chính trị của Đông Âu (đặc biệt là Ba Lan) và nước Đức bị chiếm đóng. Từ năm 1947 đến 1949, Hoa Kỳ áp dụng chính sách ngăn chặn (Học thuyết Truman, Kế hoạch Marshall, NATO) trong khi Liên Xô củng cố Đông Âu và bác bỏ Kế hoạch Marshall. Cả hai bên đều thực sự lo sợ lẫn nhau.","Kennan's 'Long Telegram' (Feb. 1946)":"'Bức điện tín dài' của Kennan (tháng 2 năm 1946)","Primary — U.S. diplomatic cable":"Nguồn sơ cấp — điện tín ngoại giao của Hoa Kỳ","A senior U.S. diplomat argues Soviet hostility comes from ideology plus historic Russian insecurity, and must be met with long-term 'containment.'":"Một nhà ngoại giao cấp cao của Hoa Kỳ lập luận rằng sự thù địch của Liên Xô bắt nguồn từ hệ tư tưởng cộng với sự bất an có tính lịch sử của người Nga, và phải được đối phó bằng chính sách 'ngăn chặn' lâu dài.","It became the intellectual foundation of U.S. Cold War strategy — it shows how American policymakers interpreted Soviet behavior.":"Nó trở thành nền tảng tư tưởng cho chiến lược Chiến tranh Lạnh của Hoa Kỳ — cho thấy các nhà hoạch định chính sách Mỹ đã diễn giải hành vi của Liên Xô như thế nào.","One official's analysis, written to persuade Washington; it reads Soviet intentions from the outside, not from Soviet records.":"Đây là phân tích của một quan chức, được viết để thuyết phục Washington; nó suy đoán ý định của Liên Xô từ bên ngoài, chứ không phải từ hồ sơ của Liên Xô.","Truman Doctrine Address to Congress (March 12, 1947)":"Diễn văn Học thuyết Truman trước Quốc hội (12 tháng 3 năm 1947)","Primary — presidential speech":"Nguồn sơ cấp — bài diễn văn của tổng thống","Truman frames world affairs as a choice between 'free' and 'totalitarian' ways of life and commits U.S. aid to nations resisting communism.":"Truman định hình các vấn đề thế giới như một sự lựa chọn giữa lối sống 'tự do' và 'toàn trị' và cam kết viện trợ của Hoa Kỳ cho các quốc gia chống lại chủ nghĩa cộng sản.","Marks the public, global turn to containment and shows how the U.S. justified its commitments ideologically.":"Đánh dấu bước ngoặt công khai, mang tính toàn cầu hướng tới chính sách ngăn chặn và cho thấy Hoa Kỳ đã biện minh cho các cam kết của mình về mặt tư tưởng như thế nào.","Political rhetoric designed to win funding; scholars argue it may have overstated the threat and universalized a specific crisis.":"Đây là luận điệu chính trị nhằm giành được ngân sách; các học giả lập luận rằng nó có thể đã phóng đại mối đe dọa và phổ quát hóa một cuộc khủng hoảng cụ thể.","Novikov Telegram (Sept. 27, 1946)":"Bức điện tín Novikov (27 tháng 9 năm 1946)","Primary — Soviet diplomatic cable":"Nguồn sơ cấp — điện tín ngoại giao của Liên Xô","The Soviet ambassador argues the United States is seeking global military and economic domination — the mirror image of Kennan's warning.":"Đại sứ Liên Xô lập luận rằng Hoa Kỳ đang tìm kiếm sự thống trị quân sự và kinh tế toàn cầu — hình ảnh phản chiếu lời cảnh báo của Kennan.","Documents the Soviet side's fears, essential for weighing responsibility fairly rather than one-sidedly.":"Ghi lại những nỗi lo sợ của phía Liên Xô, điều thiết yếu để cân nhắc trách nhiệm một cách công bằng thay vì phiến diện.","Also one diplomat's interpretation; historians debate how much it reflected Stalin's actual thinking, and it too reads the adversary from the outside.":"Đây cũng là cách diễn giải của một nhà ngoại giao; các nhà sử học tranh luận nó phản ánh suy nghĩ thực sự của Stalin đến mức nào, và nó cũng suy đoán về đối thủ từ bên ngoài.","Historians divide into schools. Orthodox interpretations blame Soviet expansionism; revisionist interpretations emphasize U.S. economic interests and 'atomic diplomacy'; post-revisionists stress a mutual security dilemma with shared responsibility. The same events (Marshall Plan, Berlin) read as defensive or provocative depending on the lens.":"Các nhà sử học chia thành nhiều trường phái. Cách diễn giải chính thống (orthodox) quy trách nhiệm cho chủ nghĩa bành trướng của Liên Xô; cách diễn giải xét lại (revisionist) nhấn mạnh các lợi ích kinh tế của Hoa Kỳ và 'ngoại giao nguyên tử'; các nhà hậu xét lại (post-revisionist) nhấn mạnh một thế lưỡng nan an ninh chung với trách nhiệm được chia sẻ. Cùng những sự kiện (Kế hoạch Marshall, Berlin) được hiểu là phòng thủ hay khiêu khích tùy theo lăng kính.","The biggest gap is direct evidence of Soviet internal decision-making — Stalin's private calculations and Politburo deliberations. Soviet records opened only partially after 1991, so interpretation long tilted toward the fuller U.S. archive.":"Khoảng trống lớn nhất là bằng chứng trực tiếp về quá trình ra quyết định nội bộ của Liên Xô — những tính toán riêng của Stalin và các cuộc thảo luận của Bộ Chính trị. Hồ sơ của Liên Xô chỉ được mở một phần sau năm 1991, nên cách diễn giải trong một thời gian dài đã nghiêng về kho lưu trữ đầy đủ hơn của Hoa Kỳ.","One defensible interpretation (not the only one): the Cold War arose less from a single aggressor than from a security dilemma — Soviet insistence on a controlled buffer zone collided with U.S. commitment to open, capitalist democracies, and each read the other's defensive moves as offensive. A student could reasonably weight responsibility toward either side using the same evidence.":"Một cách diễn giải có thể bảo vệ được (không phải là duy nhất): Chiến tranh Lạnh nảy sinh không hẳn từ một kẻ gây hấn duy nhất mà từ một thế lưỡng nan an ninh — việc Liên Xô khăng khăng đòi một vùng đệm được kiểm soát đã xung đột với cam kết của Hoa Kỳ đối với các nền dân chủ tư bản cởi mở, và mỗi bên đều xem các động thái phòng thủ của bên kia là tấn công. Một học sinh có thể hợp lý nghiêng trách nhiệm về phía bên nào cũng được khi dùng cùng những bằng chứng ấy."},"ar":{"What Caused the Cold War?":"ما الذي تسبب في الحرب الباردة؟","Build an evidence-based answer to a contested question: what caused the Cold War, and who bears more responsibility for its onset?":"ابنِ إجابة قائمة على الأدلة عن سؤال محل خلاف: ما الذي تسبب في الحرب الباردة، ومن يتحمل المسؤولية الأكبر عن اندلاعها؟","By 1946 the wartime alliance between the United States and the Soviet Union had collapsed into mutual suspicion. Historians agree on the sequence of events but disagree sharply about the cause — and about who was more responsible. Weigh the evidence, note what conflicts and what is missing, and build a defensible working conclusion.":"بحلول عام 1946 كان التحالف الذي نشأ زمن الحرب بين الولايات المتحدة والاتحاد السوفيتي قد انهار إلى شكٍّ متبادل. يتفق المؤرخون على تسلسل الأحداث لكنهم يختلفون اختلافًا حادًا حول السبب — وحول من كان أكثر مسؤولية. زِن الأدلة، ولاحظ ما يتعارض وما هو مفقود، وابنِ استنتاجًا أوليًا قابلًا للدفاع عنه.","The Origins of the Cold War":"أصول الحرب الباردة","United States, Soviet Union, and a divided Europe":"الولايات المتحدة والاتحاد السوفيتي وأوروبا المنقسمة","Compare your evidence cards with a partner. Did you rate the same sources as reliable?":"قارن بطاقات الأدلة الخاصة بك مع زميل. هل صنّفتما المصادر نفسها على أنها موثوقة؟","Did you and your partner lean toward the same 'school' of interpretation? What evidence moved you?":"هل ملتَ أنت وزميلك إلى المدرسة التفسيرية نفسها؟ وما الدليل الذي أثّر فيك؟","Write a working conclusion answering the historical question. Cite at least two evidence cards, acknowledge conflicting interpretations, and note one limitation of your evidence.":"اكتب استنتاجًا أوليًا يجيب عن السؤال التاريخي. استشهد ببطاقتَي أدلة على الأقل، وأقرّ بالتفسيرات المتعارضة، وأشر إلى أحد قيود الأدلة لديك.","State, in one sentence, your working answer to what caused the Cold War.":"اذكر، في جملة واحدة، إجابتك الأولية عمّا تسبب في الحرب الباردة.","Connect the Truman Doctrine and the Novikov Telegram — how does each side justify itself?":"اربط بين مبدأ ترومان (Truman Doctrine) وبرقية نوفيكوف (Novikov Telegram) — كيف يبرر كل طرف موقفه؟","Apply the idea of a 'security dilemma' to a rivalry between two countries today.":"طبّق فكرة \"المعضلة الأمنية\" على تنافس بين دولتين في وقتنا الحالي.","Kennan and Containment, 1947 — Office of the Historian, U.S. Dept. of State":"كينان (Kennan) وسياسة الاحتواء، 1947 — مكتب المؤرخ، وزارة الخارجية الأمريكية","Government history of Kennan's 'long telegram' and the birth of containment.":"التاريخ الحكومي لـ\"البرقية الطويلة\" لكينان وميلاد سياسة الاحتواء.","How did Kennan explain Soviet behavior?":"كيف فسّر كينان السلوك السوفيتي؟","How reliable is a single diplomat's analysis of a rival power?":"ما مدى موثوقية تحليل دبلوماسي واحد لقوة منافسة؟","Truman Doctrine — Harry S. Truman Library":"مبدأ ترومان (Truman Doctrine) — مكتبة هاري إس. ترومان","Truman's March 1947 message requesting aid for Greece and Turkey.":"رسالة ترومان في آذار/مارس 1947 التي طلب فيها تقديم مساعدات لليونان وتركيا.","How does Truman frame the choice facing the world?":"كيف يصوغ ترومان الخيار الذي يواجه العالم؟","What might this speech leave out or exaggerate?":"ما الذي قد يُغفله هذا الخطاب أو يبالغ فيه؟","Telegram from Nikolai Novikov to the Soviet Leadership (Sept. 1946) — Wilson Center Digital Archive":"برقية من نيكولاي نوفيكوف (Nikolai Novikov) إلى القيادة السوفيتية (أيلول/سبتمبر 1946) — الأرشيف الرقمي لمركز ويلسون","The Soviet ambassador's warning that the U.S. sought global domination.":"تحذير السفير السوفيتي من أن الولايات المتحدة تسعى إلى الهيمنة العالمية.","How does the Soviet view mirror the American one?":"كيف تعكس الرؤية السوفيتية الرؤية الأمريكية كصورة في مرآة؟","Why is it important to read both sides' cables?":"لماذا من المهم قراءة برقيات الطرفين معًا؟","What caused the Cold War — and who bears more responsibility for its onset (roughly 1945–1950): the United States or the Soviet Union?":"ما الذي تسبب في الحرب الباردة — ومن يتحمل المسؤولية الأكبر عن اندلاعها (نحو 1945–1950): الولايات المتحدة أم الاتحاد السوفيتي؟","By 1945–46 the alliance had collapsed over the political future of Eastern Europe (especially Poland) and occupied Germany. Between 1947 and 1949 the US adopted containment (Truman Doctrine, Marshall Plan, NATO) while the USSR consolidated Eastern Europe and rejected the Marshall Plan. Both sides genuinely feared the other.":"بحلول عامَي 1945–46 كان التحالف قد انهار بسبب المستقبل السياسي لأوروبا الشرقية (وبخاصة بولندا) وألمانيا المحتلة. وبين عامَي 1947 و1949 تبنّت الولايات المتحدة سياسة الاحتواء (مبدأ ترومان، ومشروع مارشال، وحلف الناتو)، في حين رسّخ الاتحاد السوفيتي سيطرته على أوروبا الشرقية ورفض مشروع مارشال. وقد كان كلا الطرفين يخشى الآخر خشيةً حقيقية.","Kennan's 'Long Telegram' (Feb. 1946)":"\"البرقية الطويلة\" لكينان (شباط/فبراير 1946)","Primary — U.S. diplomatic cable":"مصدر أولي — برقية دبلوماسية أمريكية","A senior U.S. diplomat argues Soviet hostility comes from ideology plus historic Russian insecurity, and must be met with long-term 'containment.'":"يرى دبلوماسي أمريكي رفيع أن العداء السوفيتي ينبع من الأيديولوجيا إضافةً إلى انعدام أمن روسي تاريخي، وأنه يجب مواجهته بسياسة \"احتواء\" طويلة الأمد.","It became the intellectual foundation of U.S. Cold War strategy — it shows how American policymakers interpreted Soviet behavior.":"أصبحت الأساس الفكري للاستراتيجية الأمريكية في الحرب الباردة — فهي تُبيّن كيف فسّر صنّاع القرار الأمريكيون السلوك السوفيتي.","One official's analysis, written to persuade Washington; it reads Soviet intentions from the outside, not from Soviet records.":"إنه تحليل مسؤول واحد، كُتب لإقناع واشنطن؛ وهو يقرأ النوايا السوفيتية من الخارج، لا من الوثائق السوفيتية.","Truman Doctrine Address to Congress (March 12, 1947)":"خطاب مبدأ ترومان أمام الكونغرس (12 آذار/مارس 1947)","Primary — presidential speech":"مصدر أولي — خطاب رئاسي","Truman frames world affairs as a choice between 'free' and 'totalitarian' ways of life and commits U.S. aid to nations resisting communism.":"يصوغ ترومان الشؤون العالمية باعتبارها خيارًا بين نمطَي حياة \"حر\" و\"شمولي\"، ويلتزم بتقديم المساعدة الأمريكية للدول التي تقاوم الشيوعية.","Marks the public, global turn to containment and shows how the U.S. justified its commitments ideologically.":"يُشكّل التحول العلني والعالمي نحو سياسة الاحتواء، ويُبيّن كيف بررت الولايات المتحدة التزاماتها أيديولوجيًا.","Political rhetoric designed to win funding; scholars argue it may have overstated the threat and universalized a specific crisis.":"خطاب سياسي صُمّم لكسب التمويل؛ ويرى الباحثون أنه ربما بالغ في تصوير التهديد وعمّم أزمة محددة لتبدو عالمية.","Novikov Telegram (Sept. 27, 1946)":"برقية نوفيكوف (27 أيلول/سبتمبر 1946)","Primary — Soviet diplomatic cable":"مصدر أولي — برقية دبلوماسية سوفيتية","The Soviet ambassador argues the United States is seeking global military and economic domination — the mirror image of Kennan's warning.":"يرى السفير السوفيتي أن الولايات المتحدة تسعى إلى الهيمنة العسكرية والاقتصادية العالمية — وهي الصورة المعاكسة لتحذير كينان.","Documents the Soviet side's fears, essential for weighing responsibility fairly rather than one-sidedly.":"يوثّق مخاوف الجانب السوفيتي، وهي ضرورية لتقدير المسؤولية بإنصاف لا من جانب واحد.","Also one diplomat's interpretation; historians debate how much it reflected Stalin's actual thinking, and it too reads the adversary from the outside.":"وهو أيضًا تفسير دبلوماسي واحد؛ ويتجادل المؤرخون حول مدى انعكاسه لتفكير ستالين الفعلي، وهو كذلك يقرأ الخصم من الخارج.","Historians divide into schools. Orthodox interpretations blame Soviet expansionism; revisionist interpretations emphasize U.S. economic interests and 'atomic diplomacy'; post-revisionists stress a mutual security dilemma with shared responsibility. The same events (Marshall Plan, Berlin) read as defensive or provocative depending on the lens.":"ينقسم المؤرخون إلى مدارس. تُحمّل التفسيرات التقليدية (Orthodox) اللومَ للتوسعية السوفيتية؛ وتُشدد التفسيرات التحريفية (Revisionist) على المصالح الاقتصادية الأمريكية و\"الدبلوماسية الذرية\"؛ أما ما بعد التحريفيين (Post-revisionists) فيُبرزون معضلة أمنية متبادلة بمسؤولية مشتركة. والأحداث نفسها (مشروع مارشال، برلين) تُقرأ على أنها دفاعية أو استفزازية بحسب زاوية النظر.","The biggest gap is direct evidence of Soviet internal decision-making — Stalin's private calculations and Politburo deliberations. Soviet records opened only partially after 1991, so interpretation long tilted toward the fuller U.S. archive.":"أكبر ثغرة هي الأدلة المباشرة على صنع القرار الداخلي السوفيتي — حسابات ستالين الخاصة ومداولات المكتب السياسي. لم تُفتح الوثائق السوفيتية إلا جزئيًا بعد عام 1991، ولذلك ظل التفسير مائلًا لوقت طويل نحو الأرشيف الأمريكي الأكثر اكتمالًا.","One defensible interpretation (not the only one): the Cold War arose less from a single aggressor than from a security dilemma — Soviet insistence on a controlled buffer zone collided with U.S. commitment to open, capitalist democracies, and each read the other's defensive moves as offensive. A student could reasonably weight responsibility toward either side using the same evidence.":"أحد التفسيرات القابلة للدفاع عنها (وليس الوحيد): نشأت الحرب الباردة لا من معتدٍ واحد بقدر ما نشأت من معضلة أمنية — إذ اصطدم إصرار السوفيت على منطقة عازلة خاضعة لسيطرتهم بالتزام الولايات المتحدة بديمقراطيات رأسمالية منفتحة، وقرأ كل طرف تحركات الآخر الدفاعية على أنها هجومية. ويمكن للطالب أن يرجّح المسؤولية بشكل معقول نحو أيّ من الطرفين مستخدمًا الأدلة نفسها."},"zh":{"What Caused the Cold War?":"冷战的起因是什么？","Build an evidence-based answer to a contested question: what caused the Cold War, and who bears more responsibility for its onset?":"针对一个有争议的问题构建以证据为基础的答案：冷战的起因是什么，谁应为其爆发承担更大的责任？","By 1946 the wartime alliance between the United States and the Soviet Union had collapsed into mutual suspicion. Historians agree on the sequence of events but disagree sharply about the cause — and about who was more responsible. Weigh the evidence, note what conflicts and what is missing, and build a defensible working conclusion.":"到1946年，美国与苏联之间的战时同盟已经瓦解为相互猜疑。历史学家对事件的先后顺序看法一致，但对起因——以及谁负有更大责任——却存在尖锐分歧。请权衡证据，注意哪些内容相互矛盾、哪些内容缺失，并构建一个站得住脚的初步结论。","The Origins of the Cold War":"冷战的起源","United States, Soviet Union, and a divided Europe":"美国、苏联与分裂的欧洲","Compare your evidence cards with a partner. Did you rate the same sources as reliable?":"与同伴比较你们的证据卡片。你们是否将相同的来源评定为可靠？","Did you and your partner lean toward the same 'school' of interpretation? What evidence moved you?":"你和你的同伴是否倾向于同一个解释'学派'？是哪些证据打动了你？","Write a working conclusion answering the historical question. Cite at least two evidence cards, acknowledge conflicting interpretations, and note one limitation of your evidence.":"写一个回答该历史问题的初步结论。至少引用两张证据卡片，承认相互矛盾的解释，并指出你所用证据的一处局限。","State, in one sentence, your working answer to what caused the Cold War.":"用一句话陈述你对冷战起因的初步答案。","Connect the Truman Doctrine and the Novikov Telegram — how does each side justify itself?":"将杜鲁门主义（Truman Doctrine）与诺维科夫电报（Novikov Telegram）联系起来——各方如何为自己辩护？","Apply the idea of a 'security dilemma' to a rivalry between two countries today.":"将'安全困境'的概念应用于当今两个国家之间的对抗。","Kennan and Containment, 1947 — Office of the Historian, U.S. Dept. of State":"凯南（Kennan）与遏制政策，1947年——美国国务院历史学家办公室","Government history of Kennan's 'long telegram' and the birth of containment.":"关于凯南'长电报'及遏制政策诞生的官方历史记述。","How did Kennan explain Soviet behavior?":"凯南如何解释苏联的行为？","How reliable is a single diplomat's analysis of a rival power?":"单个外交官对一个敌对大国的分析有多可靠？","Truman Doctrine — Harry S. Truman Library":"杜鲁门主义（Truman Doctrine）——哈里·S·杜鲁门图书馆","Truman's March 1947 message requesting aid for Greece and Turkey.":"杜鲁门1947年3月请求向希腊和土耳其提供援助的咨文。","How does Truman frame the choice facing the world?":"杜鲁门如何界定世界所面临的抉择？","What might this speech leave out or exaggerate?":"这篇演说可能遗漏或夸大了什么？","Telegram from Nikolai Novikov to the Soviet Leadership (Sept. 1946) — Wilson Center Digital Archive":"尼古拉·诺维科夫（Nikolai Novikov）致苏联领导层的电报（1946年9月）——威尔逊中心数字档案馆","The Soviet ambassador's warning that the U.S. sought global domination.":"苏联大使发出的警告：美国正谋求全球主导地位。","How does the Soviet view mirror the American one?":"苏联的观点如何与美国的观点互为镜像？","Why is it important to read both sides' cables?":"为什么阅读双方的电报都很重要？","What caused the Cold War — and who bears more responsibility for its onset (roughly 1945–1950): the United States or the Soviet Union?":"冷战的起因是什么——谁应为其爆发（大约1945年至1950年）承担更大的责任：美国还是苏联？","By 1945–46 the alliance had collapsed over the political future of Eastern Europe (especially Poland) and occupied Germany. Between 1947 and 1949 the US adopted containment (Truman Doctrine, Marshall Plan, NATO) while the USSR consolidated Eastern Europe and rejected the Marshall Plan. Both sides genuinely feared the other.":"到1945年至1946年，因东欧（尤其是波兰）的政治前途和被占领的德国问题，同盟已经瓦解。1947年至1949年间，美国采取了遏制政策（杜鲁门主义、马歇尔计划、北约），而苏联则巩固了对东欧的控制并拒绝了马歇尔计划。双方都真切地惧怕对方。","Kennan's 'Long Telegram' (Feb. 1946)":"凯南的'长电报'（1946年2月）","Primary — U.S. diplomatic cable":"第一手史料——美国外交电报","A senior U.S. diplomat argues Soviet hostility comes from ideology plus historic Russian insecurity, and must be met with long-term 'containment.'":"一位美国资深外交官认为，苏联的敌意源于意识形态加上俄国历史上的不安全感，必须以长期的'遏制'加以应对。","It became the intellectual foundation of U.S. Cold War strategy — it shows how American policymakers interpreted Soviet behavior.":"它成为美国冷战战略的思想基础——展现了美国决策者如何解读苏联的行为。","One official's analysis, written to persuade Washington; it reads Soviet intentions from the outside, not from Soviet records.":"这是一位官员的分析，为说服华盛顿而写；它从外部揣度苏联的意图，而非依据苏联的档案。","Truman Doctrine Address to Congress (March 12, 1947)":"杜鲁门主义致国会咨文（1947年3月12日）","Primary — presidential speech":"第一手史料——总统演说","Truman frames world affairs as a choice between 'free' and 'totalitarian' ways of life and commits U.S. aid to nations resisting communism.":"杜鲁门将世界事务界定为'自由'与'极权'两种生活方式之间的抉择，并承诺向抵抗共产主义的国家提供美国援助。","Marks the public, global turn to containment and shows how the U.S. justified its commitments ideologically.":"标志着公开、全球性地转向遏制政策，并展现了美国如何从意识形态上为其承诺辩护。","Political rhetoric designed to win funding; scholars argue it may have overstated the threat and universalized a specific crisis.":"这是为争取拨款而设计的政治修辞；学者们认为它可能夸大了威胁，并将一场具体的危机普遍化。","Novikov Telegram (Sept. 27, 1946)":"诺维科夫电报（1946年9月27日）","Primary — Soviet diplomatic cable":"第一手史料——苏联外交电报","The Soviet ambassador argues the United States is seeking global military and economic domination — the mirror image of Kennan's warning.":"苏联大使认为美国正谋求全球军事与经济主导地位——这恰是凯南警告的镜像。","Documents the Soviet side's fears, essential for weighing responsibility fairly rather than one-sidedly.":"记录了苏联一方的担忧，这对于公正而非片面地衡量责任至关重要。","Also one diplomat's interpretation; historians debate how much it reflected Stalin's actual thinking, and it too reads the adversary from the outside.":"这同样是一位外交官的解读；历史学家对它在多大程度上反映了斯大林的真实想法争论不休，而它也是从外部揣度对手。","Historians divide into schools. Orthodox interpretations blame Soviet expansionism; revisionist interpretations emphasize U.S. economic interests and 'atomic diplomacy'; post-revisionists stress a mutual security dilemma with shared responsibility. The same events (Marshall Plan, Berlin) read as defensive or provocative depending on the lens.":"历史学家分成不同学派。正统派（orthodox）的解释归咎于苏联的扩张主义；修正派（revisionist）的解释强调美国的经济利益和'原子外交'；后修正派（post-revisionist）则强调一种带有共同责任的相互安全困境。同样的事件（马歇尔计划、柏林）依所用视角不同，可被解读为防御性的或挑衅性的。","The biggest gap is direct evidence of Soviet internal decision-making — Stalin's private calculations and Politburo deliberations. Soviet records opened only partially after 1991, so interpretation long tilted toward the fuller U.S. archive.":"最大的空白在于苏联内部决策的直接证据——斯大林的私下盘算和政治局的商议。苏联档案在1991年之后才部分开放，因此解释长期偏向于更为完整的美国档案。","One defensible interpretation (not the only one): the Cold War arose less from a single aggressor than from a security dilemma — Soviet insistence on a controlled buffer zone collided with U.S. commitment to open, capitalist democracies, and each read the other's defensive moves as offensive. A student could reasonably weight responsibility toward either side using the same evidence.":"一种站得住脚的解释（并非唯一）：冷战与其说源于单一侵略者，不如说源于一种安全困境——苏联坚持要有一个受其控制的缓冲地带，与美国对开放的资本主义民主国家的承诺相冲突，双方都把对方的防御性举动解读为进攻性的。学生使用相同的证据，可以合理地将责任偏向任何一方。"},"ur":{"What Caused the Cold War?":"سرد جنگ کی وجہ کیا تھی؟","Build an evidence-based answer to a contested question: what caused the Cold War, and who bears more responsibility for its onset?":"ایک متنازع سوال کا شواہد پر مبنی جواب تیار کریں: سرد جنگ کی وجہ کیا تھی، اور اس کے آغاز کی زیادہ ذمہ داری کس پر عائد ہوتی ہے؟","By 1946 the wartime alliance between the United States and the Soviet Union had collapsed into mutual suspicion. Historians agree on the sequence of events but disagree sharply about the cause — and about who was more responsible. Weigh the evidence, note what conflicts and what is missing, and build a defensible working conclusion.":"1946ء تک امریکہ اور سوویت یونین کے درمیان جنگ کے دوران قائم اتحاد باہمی بداعتمادی میں تبدیل ہو کر ٹوٹ چکا تھا۔ مورخین واقعات کی ترتیب پر متفق ہیں لیکن سبب کے بارے میں — اور اس بارے میں کہ زیادہ ذمہ دار کون تھا — شدید اختلاف رکھتے ہیں۔ شواہد کو تولیں، نوٹ کریں کہ کیا متضاد ہے اور کیا غائب ہے، اور ایک قابلِ دفاع عبوری نتیجہ اخذ کریں۔","The Origins of the Cold War":"سرد جنگ کے آغاز","United States, Soviet Union, and a divided Europe":"امریکہ، سوویت یونین، اور ایک منقسم یورپ","Compare your evidence cards with a partner. Did you rate the same sources as reliable?":"اپنے شواہد کے کارڈز کا کسی ساتھی کے ساتھ موازنہ کریں۔ کیا آپ دونوں نے انہی ذرائع کو قابلِ اعتماد قرار دیا؟","Did you and your partner lean toward the same 'school' of interpretation? What evidence moved you?":"کیا آپ اور آپ کے ساتھی تشریح کے ایک ہی 'مکتبِ فکر' کی طرف مائل ہوئے؟ کن شواہد نے آپ کو متاثر کیا؟","Write a working conclusion answering the historical question. Cite at least two evidence cards, acknowledge conflicting interpretations, and note one limitation of your evidence.":"تاریخی سوال کا جواب دیتے ہوئے ایک عبوری نتیجہ لکھیں۔ کم از کم دو شواہد کارڈز کا حوالہ دیں، متضاد تشریحات کو تسلیم کریں، اور اپنے شواہد کی ایک حد کی نشاندہی کریں۔","State, in one sentence, your working answer to what caused the Cold War.":"ایک جملے میں بیان کریں کہ سرد جنگ کی وجہ کے بارے میں آپ کا عبوری جواب کیا ہے۔","Connect the Truman Doctrine and the Novikov Telegram — how does each side justify itself?":"ٹرومین ڈاکٹرائن (Truman Doctrine) اور نوویکوف ٹیلی گرام (Novikov Telegram) کو آپس میں جوڑیں — ہر فریق اپنا جواز کیسے پیش کرتا ہے؟","Apply the idea of a 'security dilemma' to a rivalry between two countries today.":"'سلامتی کی کشمکش' کے تصور کو آج دو ممالک کے درمیان کسی رقابت پر لاگو کریں۔","Kennan and Containment, 1947 — Office of the Historian, U.S. Dept. of State":"کینان (Kennan) اور روک تھام کی پالیسی، 1947 — دفترِ مورخ، امریکی محکمہ خارجہ","Government history of Kennan's 'long telegram' and the birth of containment.":"کینان کے 'طویل ٹیلی گرام' اور روک تھام کی پالیسی کی پیدائش کی سرکاری تاریخ۔","How did Kennan explain Soviet behavior?":"کینان نے سوویت رویّے کی وضاحت کیسے کی؟","How reliable is a single diplomat's analysis of a rival power?":"کسی حریف طاقت کے بارے میں ایک اکیلے سفارت کار کا تجزیہ کتنا قابلِ اعتماد ہے؟","Truman Doctrine — Harry S. Truman Library":"ٹرومین ڈاکٹرائن (Truman Doctrine) — ہیری ایس ٹرومین لائبریری","Truman's March 1947 message requesting aid for Greece and Turkey.":"ٹرومین کا مارچ 1947 کا پیغام جس میں یونان اور ترکی کے لیے امداد کی درخواست کی گئی۔","How does Truman frame the choice facing the world?":"ٹرومین دنیا کو درپیش انتخاب کو کس طرح پیش کرتا ہے؟","What might this speech leave out or exaggerate?":"یہ تقریر کیا چیز نظرانداز کر سکتی ہے یا کس بات کو بڑھا چڑھا کر پیش کر سکتی ہے؟","Telegram from Nikolai Novikov to the Soviet Leadership (Sept. 1946) — Wilson Center Digital Archive":"نکولائی نوویکوف (Nikolai Novikov) کی طرف سے سوویت قیادت کو ٹیلی گرام (ستمبر 1946) — ولسن سینٹر ڈیجیٹل آرکائیو","The Soviet ambassador's warning that the U.S. sought global domination.":"سوویت سفیر کی تنبیہ کہ امریکہ عالمی تسلط کا خواہاں ہے۔","How does the Soviet view mirror the American one?":"سوویت نقطہ نظر امریکی نقطہ نظر کا عکس کیسے ہے؟","Why is it important to read both sides' cables?":"دونوں فریقوں کے مراسلے پڑھنا کیوں اہم ہے؟","What caused the Cold War — and who bears more responsibility for its onset (roughly 1945–1950): the United States or the Soviet Union?":"سرد جنگ کی وجہ کیا تھی — اور اس کے آغاز (تقریباً 1945–1950) کی زیادہ ذمہ داری کس پر عائد ہوتی ہے: امریکہ یا سوویت یونین؟","By 1945–46 the alliance had collapsed over the political future of Eastern Europe (especially Poland) and occupied Germany. Between 1947 and 1949 the US adopted containment (Truman Doctrine, Marshall Plan, NATO) while the USSR consolidated Eastern Europe and rejected the Marshall Plan. Both sides genuinely feared the other.":"1945ء–46ء تک یہ اتحاد مشرقی یورپ (خاص طور پر پولینڈ) اور زیرِ قبضہ جرمنی کے سیاسی مستقبل پر ٹوٹ چکا تھا۔ 1947ء اور 1949ء کے درمیان امریکہ نے روک تھام کی پالیسی (ٹرومین ڈاکٹرائن، مارشل پلان، نیٹو) اپنائی جبکہ سوویت یونین نے مشرقی یورپ پر اپنی گرفت مضبوط کی اور مارشل پلان کو مسترد کر دیا۔ دونوں فریق حقیقتاً ایک دوسرے سے خوفزدہ تھے۔","Kennan's 'Long Telegram' (Feb. 1946)":"کینان کا 'طویل ٹیلی گرام' (فروری 1946)","Primary — U.S. diplomatic cable":"بنیادی ماخذ — امریکی سفارتی مراسلہ","A senior U.S. diplomat argues Soviet hostility comes from ideology plus historic Russian insecurity, and must be met with long-term 'containment.'":"ایک اعلیٰ امریکی سفارت کار کا استدلال ہے کہ سوویت دشمنی نظریے کے ساتھ ساتھ تاریخی روسی عدم تحفظ سے پیدا ہوتی ہے، اور اس کا مقابلہ طویل مدتی 'روک تھام' سے کیا جانا چاہیے۔","It became the intellectual foundation of U.S. Cold War strategy — it shows how American policymakers interpreted Soviet behavior.":"یہ امریکی سرد جنگ کی حکمتِ عملی کی فکری بنیاد بن گیا — یہ ظاہر کرتا ہے کہ امریکی پالیسی ساز سوویت رویّے کی تشریح کیسے کرتے تھے۔","One official's analysis, written to persuade Washington; it reads Soviet intentions from the outside, not from Soviet records.":"یہ ایک اہلکار کا تجزیہ ہے، جو واشنگٹن کو قائل کرنے کے لیے لکھا گیا؛ یہ سوویت ارادوں کو باہر سے پڑھتا ہے، سوویت دستاویزات سے نہیں۔","Truman Doctrine Address to Congress (March 12, 1947)":"کانگریس سے ٹرومین ڈاکٹرائن کا خطاب (12 مارچ 1947)","Primary — presidential speech":"بنیادی ماخذ — صدارتی تقریر","Truman frames world affairs as a choice between 'free' and 'totalitarian' ways of life and commits U.S. aid to nations resisting communism.":"ٹرومین عالمی معاملات کو 'آزاد' اور 'مطلق العنان' طرزِ زندگی کے درمیان ایک انتخاب کے طور پر پیش کرتا ہے اور کمیونزم کے خلاف مزاحمت کرنے والی اقوام کو امریکی امداد کا وعدہ کرتا ہے۔","Marks the public, global turn to containment and shows how the U.S. justified its commitments ideologically.":"یہ روک تھام کی پالیسی کی طرف علانیہ، عالمی موڑ کی نشاندہی کرتا ہے اور ظاہر کرتا ہے کہ امریکہ نے اپنی وابستگیوں کا نظریاتی جواز کیسے پیش کیا۔","Political rhetoric designed to win funding; scholars argue it may have overstated the threat and universalized a specific crisis.":"یہ فنڈنگ حاصل کرنے کے لیے تیار کی گئی سیاسی بیان بازی ہے؛ محققین کا استدلال ہے کہ اس نے خطرے کو بڑھا چڑھا کر پیش کیا ہو گا اور ایک مخصوص بحران کو عالمگیر بنا دیا۔","Novikov Telegram (Sept. 27, 1946)":"نوویکوف ٹیلی گرام (27 ستمبر 1946)","Primary — Soviet diplomatic cable":"بنیادی ماخذ — سوویت سفارتی مراسلہ","The Soviet ambassador argues the United States is seeking global military and economic domination — the mirror image of Kennan's warning.":"سوویت سفیر کا استدلال ہے کہ امریکہ عالمی فوجی اور اقتصادی تسلط کا خواہاں ہے — یہ کینان کی تنبیہ کا عکسی رخ ہے۔","Documents the Soviet side's fears, essential for weighing responsibility fairly rather than one-sidedly.":"یہ سوویت فریق کے خدشات کو دستاویزی شکل دیتا ہے، جو ذمہ داری کو یک طرفہ کے بجائے منصفانہ طور پر تولنے کے لیے ناگزیر ہیں۔","Also one diplomat's interpretation; historians debate how much it reflected Stalin's actual thinking, and it too reads the adversary from the outside.":"یہ بھی ایک سفارت کار کی تشریح ہے؛ مورخین اس پر بحث کرتے ہیں کہ یہ اسٹالن کی اصل سوچ کی کس حد تک عکاسی کرتا تھا، اور یہ بھی حریف کو باہر سے پڑھتا ہے۔","Historians divide into schools. Orthodox interpretations blame Soviet expansionism; revisionist interpretations emphasize U.S. economic interests and 'atomic diplomacy'; post-revisionists stress a mutual security dilemma with shared responsibility. The same events (Marshall Plan, Berlin) read as defensive or provocative depending on the lens.":"مورخین مختلف مکاتبِ فکر میں بٹے ہوئے ہیں۔ روایتی (orthodox) تشریحات سوویت توسیع پسندی کو ذمہ دار ٹھہراتی ہیں؛ نظرثانی پسند (revisionist) تشریحات امریکی اقتصادی مفادات اور 'ایٹمی سفارت کاری' پر زور دیتی ہیں؛ ما بعد نظرثانی پسند (post-revisionist) مشترکہ ذمہ داری کے ساتھ ایک باہمی سلامتی کی کشمکش پر زور دیتے ہیں۔ ایک ہی واقعات (مارشل پلان، برلن) نقطہ نظر کے لحاظ سے دفاعی یا اشتعال انگیز کے طور پر پڑھے جاتے ہیں۔","The biggest gap is direct evidence of Soviet internal decision-making — Stalin's private calculations and Politburo deliberations. Soviet records opened only partially after 1991, so interpretation long tilted toward the fuller U.S. archive.":"سب سے بڑا خلا سوویت اندرونی فیصلہ سازی کے براہِ راست شواہد کا ہے — اسٹالن کے ذاتی حساب کتاب اور پولٹ بیورو کی مشاورتیں۔ سوویت دستاویزات 1991ء کے بعد صرف جزوی طور پر کھلیں، چنانچہ تشریح طویل عرصے تک زیادہ مکمل امریکی آرکائیو کی طرف جھکی رہی۔","One defensible interpretation (not the only one): the Cold War arose less from a single aggressor than from a security dilemma — Soviet insistence on a controlled buffer zone collided with U.S. commitment to open, capitalist democracies, and each read the other's defensive moves as offensive. A student could reasonably weight responsibility toward either side using the same evidence.":"ایک قابلِ دفاع تشریح (واحد نہیں): سرد جنگ کسی ایک جارح سے کم اور ایک سلامتی کی کشمکش سے زیادہ پیدا ہوئی — ایک زیرِ کنٹرول حائل خطے پر سوویت اصرار کا امریکہ کی کھلی، سرمایہ دارانہ جمہوریتوں سے وابستگی کے ساتھ ٹکراؤ ہوا، اور ہر فریق نے دوسرے کے دفاعی اقدامات کو جارحانہ سمجھا۔ ایک طالب علم انہی شواہد کا استعمال کرتے ہوئے معقول طور پر ذمہ داری کو کسی بھی فریق کی طرف جھکا سکتا ہے۔"},"hi":{"What Caused the Cold War?":"शीत युद्ध का कारण क्या था?","Build an evidence-based answer to a contested question: what caused the Cold War, and who bears more responsibility for its onset?":"एक विवादित प्रश्न का साक्ष्य-आधारित उत्तर तैयार करें: शीत युद्ध का कारण क्या था, और इसकी शुरुआत के लिए अधिक जिम्मेदारी किसकी है?","By 1946 the wartime alliance between the United States and the Soviet Union had collapsed into mutual suspicion. Historians agree on the sequence of events but disagree sharply about the cause — and about who was more responsible. Weigh the evidence, note what conflicts and what is missing, and build a defensible working conclusion.":"1946 तक संयुक्त राज्य अमेरिका और सोवियत संघ के बीच युद्धकालीन गठबंधन आपसी संदेह में ढहकर बिखर चुका था। इतिहासकार घटनाओं के क्रम पर सहमत हैं, लेकिन कारण के बारे में — और इस बारे में कि अधिक जिम्मेदार कौन था — तीखे मतभेद रखते हैं। साक्ष्य को तौलें, ध्यान दें कि क्या विरोधाभासी है और क्या अनुपस्थित है, और एक बचाव-योग्य अस्थायी निष्कर्ष तैयार करें।","The Origins of the Cold War":"शीत युद्ध की उत्पत्ति","United States, Soviet Union, and a divided Europe":"संयुक्त राज्य अमेरिका, सोवियत संघ, और एक विभाजित यूरोप","Compare your evidence cards with a partner. Did you rate the same sources as reliable?":"अपने साक्ष्य कार्डों की तुलना किसी साथी के साथ करें। क्या आप दोनों ने समान स्रोतों को विश्वसनीय माना?","Did you and your partner lean toward the same 'school' of interpretation? What evidence moved you?":"क्या आप और आपका साथी व्याख्या के एक ही 'विचारधारा' की ओर झुके? किस साक्ष्य ने आपको प्रभावित किया?","Write a working conclusion answering the historical question. Cite at least two evidence cards, acknowledge conflicting interpretations, and note one limitation of your evidence.":"ऐतिहासिक प्रश्न का उत्तर देते हुए एक अस्थायी निष्कर्ष लिखें। कम से कम दो साक्ष्य कार्डों का हवाला दें, विरोधाभासी व्याख्याओं को स्वीकार करें, और अपने साक्ष्य की एक सीमा का उल्लेख करें।","State, in one sentence, your working answer to what caused the Cold War.":"एक वाक्य में बताएं कि शीत युद्ध के कारण के बारे में आपका अस्थायी उत्तर क्या है।","Connect the Truman Doctrine and the Novikov Telegram — how does each side justify itself?":"ट्रूमैन सिद्धांत (Truman Doctrine) और नोविकोव टेलीग्राम (Novikov Telegram) को जोड़ें — प्रत्येक पक्ष स्वयं को कैसे उचित ठहराता है?","Apply the idea of a 'security dilemma' to a rivalry between two countries today.":"'सुरक्षा दुविधा' के विचार को आज दो देशों के बीच की प्रतिद्वंद्विता पर लागू करें।","Kennan and Containment, 1947 — Office of the Historian, U.S. Dept. of State":"केनन (Kennan) और नियंत्रण (Containment), 1947 — इतिहासकार का कार्यालय, अमेरिकी विदेश विभाग","Government history of Kennan's 'long telegram' and the birth of containment.":"केनन के 'लंबे टेलीग्राम' और नियंत्रण नीति के जन्म का सरकारी इतिहास।","How did Kennan explain Soviet behavior?":"केनन ने सोवियत व्यवहार की व्याख्या कैसे की?","How reliable is a single diplomat's analysis of a rival power?":"किसी प्रतिद्वंद्वी शक्ति के बारे में एक अकेले राजनयिक का विश्लेषण कितना विश्वसनीय है?","Truman Doctrine — Harry S. Truman Library":"ट्रूमैन सिद्धांत (Truman Doctrine) — हैरी एस. ट्रूमैन लाइब्रेरी","Truman's March 1947 message requesting aid for Greece and Turkey.":"ट्रूमैन का मार्च 1947 का संदेश जिसमें ग्रीस और तुर्की के लिए सहायता का अनुरोध किया गया।","How does Truman frame the choice facing the world?":"ट्रूमैन दुनिया के सामने मौजूद विकल्प को किस तरह प्रस्तुत करता है?","What might this speech leave out or exaggerate?":"यह भाषण क्या छोड़ सकता है या किस बात को बढ़ा-चढ़ाकर पेश कर सकता है?","Telegram from Nikolai Novikov to the Soviet Leadership (Sept. 1946) — Wilson Center Digital Archive":"निकोलाई नोविकोव (Nikolai Novikov) की ओर से सोवियत नेतृत्व को टेलीग्राम (सितंबर 1946) — विल्सन सेंटर डिजिटल अभिलेखागार","The Soviet ambassador's warning that the U.S. sought global domination.":"सोवियत राजदूत की यह चेतावनी कि अमेरिका वैश्विक वर्चस्व चाहता है।","How does the Soviet view mirror the American one?":"सोवियत दृष्टिकोण अमेरिकी दृष्टिकोण का प्रतिबिंब किस तरह है?","Why is it important to read both sides' cables?":"दोनों पक्षों के संदेश (केबल) पढ़ना क्यों महत्वपूर्ण है?","What caused the Cold War — and who bears more responsibility for its onset (roughly 1945–1950): the United States or the Soviet Union?":"शीत युद्ध का कारण क्या था — और इसकी शुरुआत (लगभग 1945–1950) के लिए अधिक जिम्मेदारी किसकी है: संयुक्त राज्य अमेरिका या सोवियत संघ?","By 1945–46 the alliance had collapsed over the political future of Eastern Europe (especially Poland) and occupied Germany. Between 1947 and 1949 the US adopted containment (Truman Doctrine, Marshall Plan, NATO) while the USSR consolidated Eastern Europe and rejected the Marshall Plan. Both sides genuinely feared the other.":"1945–46 तक पूर्वी यूरोप (विशेषकर पोलैंड) और अधिकृत जर्मनी के राजनीतिक भविष्य को लेकर गठबंधन ढह चुका था। 1947 और 1949 के बीच अमेरिका ने नियंत्रण नीति (ट्रूमैन सिद्धांत, मार्शल योजना, नाटो) अपनाई, जबकि सोवियत संघ ने पूर्वी यूरोप पर अपनी पकड़ मजबूत की और मार्शल योजना को अस्वीकार कर दिया। दोनों पक्ष वास्तव में एक-दूसरे से भयभीत थे।","Kennan's 'Long Telegram' (Feb. 1946)":"केनन का 'लंबा टेलीग्राम' (फरवरी 1946)","Primary — U.S. diplomatic cable":"प्राथमिक स्रोत — अमेरिकी राजनयिक संदेश (केबल)","A senior U.S. diplomat argues Soviet hostility comes from ideology plus historic Russian insecurity, and must be met with long-term 'containment.'":"एक वरिष्ठ अमेरिकी राजनयिक का तर्क है कि सोवियत शत्रुता विचारधारा के साथ-साथ ऐतिहासिक रूसी असुरक्षा से उपजती है, और इसका सामना दीर्घकालिक 'नियंत्रण' से किया जाना चाहिए।","It became the intellectual foundation of U.S. Cold War strategy — it shows how American policymakers interpreted Soviet behavior.":"यह अमेरिकी शीत युद्ध रणनीति की बौद्धिक नींव बन गया — यह दर्शाता है कि अमेरिकी नीति-निर्माताओं ने सोवियत व्यवहार की व्याख्या कैसे की।","One official's analysis, written to persuade Washington; it reads Soviet intentions from the outside, not from Soviet records.":"यह एक अधिकारी का विश्लेषण है, जो वाशिंगटन को समझाने के लिए लिखा गया; यह सोवियत इरादों को बाहर से आंकता है, सोवियत अभिलेखों से नहीं।","Truman Doctrine Address to Congress (March 12, 1947)":"कांग्रेस के समक्ष ट्रूमैन सिद्धांत का संबोधन (12 मार्च 1947)","Primary — presidential speech":"प्राथमिक स्रोत — राष्ट्रपति का भाषण","Truman frames world affairs as a choice between 'free' and 'totalitarian' ways of life and commits U.S. aid to nations resisting communism.":"ट्रूमैन विश्व मामलों को 'स्वतंत्र' और 'अधिनायकवादी' जीवन-शैलियों के बीच एक विकल्प के रूप में प्रस्तुत करता है और साम्यवाद का प्रतिरोध करने वाले राष्ट्रों को अमेरिकी सहायता देने की प्रतिबद्धता जताता है।","Marks the public, global turn to containment and shows how the U.S. justified its commitments ideologically.":"यह नियंत्रण नीति की ओर सार्वजनिक, वैश्विक मोड़ को चिह्नित करता है और दर्शाता है कि अमेरिका ने अपनी प्रतिबद्धताओं को वैचारिक रूप से किस तरह उचित ठहराया।","Political rhetoric designed to win funding; scholars argue it may have overstated the threat and universalized a specific crisis.":"यह धन जुटाने के लिए रची गई राजनीतिक बयानबाजी है; विद्वानों का तर्क है कि इसने खतरे को बढ़ा-चढ़ाकर पेश किया हो सकता है और एक विशिष्ट संकट को सार्वभौमिक बना दिया।","Novikov Telegram (Sept. 27, 1946)":"नोविकोव टेलीग्राम (27 सितंबर 1946)","Primary — Soviet diplomatic cable":"प्राथमिक स्रोत — सोवियत राजनयिक संदेश (केबल)","The Soviet ambassador argues the United States is seeking global military and economic domination — the mirror image of Kennan's warning.":"सोवियत राजदूत का तर्क है कि अमेरिका वैश्विक सैन्य और आर्थिक वर्चस्व चाहता है — यह केनन की चेतावनी का दर्पण-प्रतिबिंब है।","Documents the Soviet side's fears, essential for weighing responsibility fairly rather than one-sidedly.":"यह सोवियत पक्ष के भय को दर्ज करता है, जो जिम्मेदारी को एकतरफा के बजाय निष्पक्ष रूप से तौलने के लिए आवश्यक है।","Also one diplomat's interpretation; historians debate how much it reflected Stalin's actual thinking, and it too reads the adversary from the outside.":"यह भी एक राजनयिक की व्याख्या है; इतिहासकार इस पर बहस करते हैं कि यह स्टालिन की वास्तविक सोच को कितना दर्शाता था, और यह भी प्रतिद्वंद्वी को बाहर से आंकता है।","Historians divide into schools. Orthodox interpretations blame Soviet expansionism; revisionist interpretations emphasize U.S. economic interests and 'atomic diplomacy'; post-revisionists stress a mutual security dilemma with shared responsibility. The same events (Marshall Plan, Berlin) read as defensive or provocative depending on the lens.":"इतिहासकार विभिन्न विचारधाराओं में बंटे हैं। रूढ़िवादी (orthodox) व्याख्याएं सोवियत विस्तारवाद को दोषी ठहराती हैं; संशोधनवादी (revisionist) व्याख्याएं अमेरिकी आर्थिक हितों और 'परमाणु कूटनीति' पर जोर देती हैं; उत्तर-संशोधनवादी (post-revisionist) साझा जिम्मेदारी के साथ एक पारस्परिक सुरक्षा दुविधा पर बल देते हैं। समान घटनाएं (मार्शल योजना, बर्लिन) दृष्टिकोण के आधार पर रक्षात्मक या उकसावे वाली के रूप में पढ़ी जाती हैं।","The biggest gap is direct evidence of Soviet internal decision-making — Stalin's private calculations and Politburo deliberations. Soviet records opened only partially after 1991, so interpretation long tilted toward the fuller U.S. archive.":"सबसे बड़ी कमी सोवियत आंतरिक निर्णय-निर्माण के प्रत्यक्ष साक्ष्य की है — स्टालिन की निजी गणनाएं और पोलितब्यूरो के विचार-विमर्श। सोवियत अभिलेख 1991 के बाद केवल आंशिक रूप से खुले, इसलिए व्याख्या लंबे समय तक अधिक पूर्ण अमेरिकी अभिलेखागार की ओर झुकी रही।","One defensible interpretation (not the only one): the Cold War arose less from a single aggressor than from a security dilemma — Soviet insistence on a controlled buffer zone collided with U.S. commitment to open, capitalist democracies, and each read the other's defensive moves as offensive. A student could reasonably weight responsibility toward either side using the same evidence.":"एक बचाव-योग्य व्याख्या (एकमात्र नहीं): शीत युद्ध किसी एक हमलावर से कम, बल्कि एक सुरक्षा दुविधा से अधिक उपजा — एक नियंत्रित बफर क्षेत्र पर सोवियत आग्रह खुले, पूंजीवादी लोकतंत्रों के प्रति अमेरिकी प्रतिबद्धता से टकराया, और प्रत्येक पक्ष ने दूसरे के रक्षात्मक कदमों को आक्रामक के रूप में पढ़ा। एक छात्र समान साक्ष्य का उपयोग करते हुए उचित रूप से जिम्मेदारी को किसी भी पक्ष की ओर झुका सकता है।"}},"great-depression":{"es":{"The Great Depression":"La Gran Depresión","Trace how one economic collapse sent shockwaves through four systems — political, economic, social-cultural, and geographic-environmental — and decide which change lasted longest.":"Traza cómo un solo colapso económico envió ondas de choque a través de cuatro sistemas —político, económico, sociocultural y geográfico-ambiental— y decide qué cambio perduró más tiempo.","The 1929 crash did more than empty bank accounts. Its shockwaves reshaped American politics, the economy, society and culture, and even the land itself. Follow the event outward through four systems, weigh who benefited and who bore the costs, and decide which change left the deepest mark.":"El desplome de 1929 hizo más que vaciar cuentas bancarias. Sus ondas de choque transformaron la política estadounidense, la economía, la sociedad y la cultura, e incluso la tierra misma. Sigue el suceso hacia afuera a través de cuatro sistemas, sopesa quién se benefició y quién asumió los costos, y decide qué cambio dejó la huella más profunda.","The United States":"Los Estados Unidos","Compare your four pathways with a partner. Did you find the same immediate and secondary effects?":"Compara tus cuatro trayectorias con un compañero. ¿Encontraron los mismos efectos inmediatos y secundarios?","Did you rank the same pathway as most lasting? Defend your ranking with evidence.":"¿Clasificaron la misma trayectoria como la más duradera? Defiende tu clasificación con evidencia.","Which system's change lasted longest after the Great Depression? Support your ranking with specific evidence from at least two pathways and two sources.":"¿El cambio de qué sistema perduró más tiempo después de la Gran Depresión? Respalda tu clasificación con evidencia específica de al menos dos trayectorias y dos fuentes.","Summarize how the Great Depression affected one system in your own words.":"Resume con tus propias palabras cómo la Gran Depresión afectó a un sistema.","Connect an immediate effect in one pathway to a secondary effect that still shapes life today.":"Conecta un efecto inmediato de una trayectoria con un efecto secundario que aún moldea la vida actual.","Apply the 'shockwave through systems' idea to a more recent crisis, such as a recession or pandemic.":"Aplica la idea de la 'onda de choque a través de los sistemas' a una crisis más reciente, como una recesión o una pandemia.","The Great Depression — Federal Reserve History":"La Gran Depresión — Historia de la Reserva Federal","How bank failures and a shrinking money supply deepened the collapse.":"Cómo las quiebras bancarias y una oferta monetaria en contracción profundizaron el colapso.","What role did bank failures and the Federal Reserve play?":"¿Qué papel desempeñaron las quiebras bancarias y la Reserva Federal?","How does this source explain the depth of the Depression?":"¿Cómo explica esta fuente la profundidad de la Depresión?","Farm Security Administration / OWI Photographs — Library of Congress":"Fotografías de la Farm Security Administration / OWI — Biblioteca del Congreso","Government photographs documenting Dust Bowl migrants and rural poverty.":"Fotografías gubernamentales que documentan a los migrantes del Dust Bowl y la pobreza rural.","What do the photographs show about who bore the costs?":"¿Qué muestran las fotografías sobre quién asumió los costos?","How do images shape the way we remember an era?":"¿Cómo moldean las imágenes la manera en que recordamos una época?","Franklin D. Roosevelt Presidential Library & Museum (National Archives)":"Biblioteca y Museo Presidencial Franklin D. Roosevelt (Archivos Nacionales)","FDR's fireside chats and New Deal records documenting the federal response.":"Las charlas junto a la chimenea de FDR y los registros del New Deal que documentan la respuesta federal.","How did FDR explain his response to the public?":"¿Cómo explicó FDR su respuesta al público?","Which New Deal program seems most consequential? Why?":"¿Qué programa del New Deal parece más trascendental? ¿Por qué?","Voters reject Hoover's approach; FDR and the Democrats sweep the 1932 election.":"Los votantes rechazan el enfoque de Hoover; FDR y los demócratas arrasan en las elecciones de 1932.","A lasting expansion of the federal government's role in the economy and social welfare; a new Democratic coalition.":"Una expansión duradera del papel del gobierno federal en la economía y el bienestar social; una nueva coalición demócrata.","New Deal laws (Emergency Banking Act, Social Security Act); FDR's fireside chats; growth of federal agencies.":"Leyes del New Deal (Ley de Emergencia Bancaria, Ley de Seguridad Social); las charlas junto a la chimenea de FDR; el crecimiento de las agencias federales.","Waves of bank failures, collapsing credit, ~25% unemployment, and a ~30% drop in output.":"Oleadas de quiebras bancarias, colapso del crédito, ~25 % de desempleo y una caída de ~30 % en la producción.","New federal financial regulation and safety nets to prevent a recurrence.":"Nueva regulación financiera federal y redes de seguridad para prevenir una recurrencia.","FDIC (1933), SEC (1934), Social Security (1935); Federal Reserve data on bank suspensions and the money supply.":"FDIC (1933), SEC (1934), Seguridad Social (1935); datos de la Reserva Federal sobre suspensiones bancarias y la oferta monetaria.","Widespread poverty, homelessness ('Hoovervilles'), and breadlines; repatriation pressure on people of Mexican heritage.":"Pobreza generalizada, falta de vivienda ('Hoovervilles') y filas para el pan; presión de repatriación sobre las personas de ascendencia mexicana.","A strengthened labor movement and a documentary and protest culture.":"Un movimiento obrero fortalecido y una cultura documental y de protesta.","FSA photographs (Dorothea Lange's Migrant Mother); Steinbeck's The Grapes of Wrath (1939); WPA arts projects.":"Fotografías de la FSA (Madre migrante de Dorothea Lange); Las uvas de la ira de Steinbeck (1939); proyectos artísticos de la WPA.","The Dust Bowl — drought, over-plowing, and dust storms ruin southern Plains farmland.":"El Dust Bowl: la sequía, el exceso de arado y las tormentas de polvo arruinan las tierras de cultivo del sur de las Grandes Llanuras.","Mass 'Okie' migration to California and new federal soil-conservation policy.":"Migración masiva de los 'Okies' a California y una nueva política federal de conservación del suelo.","The Soil Conservation Service (1935); FSA migration photos and California migrant-camp records.":"El Servicio de Conservación del Suelo (1935); las fotografías de migración de la FSA y los registros de los campamentos de migrantes de California.","Depositors and investors gained lasting protections (FDIC/SEC); the elderly, unemployed, and unionized workers gained a permanent safety net; jobless workers got jobs through the WPA and CCC.":"Los depositantes e inversores obtuvieron protecciones duraderas (FDIC/SEC); los ancianos, los desempleados y los trabajadores sindicalizados obtuvieron una red de seguridad permanente; los trabajadores sin empleo consiguieron trabajo a través de la WPA y el CCC.","Displaced farmers and Dust Bowl migrants; unemployed industrial and Black workers (last hired, first fired); Mexican Americans targeted by repatriation; uninsured depositors of banks that failed before 1933.":"Agricultores desplazados y migrantes del Dust Bowl; trabajadores industriales y negros desempleados (los últimos en ser contratados, los primeros en ser despedidos); mexicano-estadounidenses señalados por la repatriación; depositantes sin seguro de los bancos que quebraron antes de 1933.","Which pathway — political, economic, social-cultural, or geographic-environmental — produced the most lasting change in American life? Use specific evidence to defend your ranking.":"¿Qué trayectoria —política, económica, sociocultural o geográfico-ambiental— produjo el cambio más duradero en la vida estadounidense? Usa evidencia específica para defender tu clasificación."},"vi":{"The Great Depression":"Cuộc Đại Suy Thoái","Trace how one economic collapse sent shockwaves through four systems — political, economic, social-cultural, and geographic-environmental — and decide which change lasted longest.":"Hãy lần theo cách một cuộc sụp đổ kinh tế lan tỏa những chấn động qua bốn hệ thống — chính trị, kinh tế, văn hóa-xã hội và địa lý-môi trường — và quyết định thay đổi nào kéo dài lâu nhất.","The 1929 crash did more than empty bank accounts. Its shockwaves reshaped American politics, the economy, society and culture, and even the land itself. Follow the event outward through four systems, weigh who benefited and who bore the costs, and decide which change left the deepest mark.":"Cuộc sụp đổ năm 1929 không chỉ làm cạn kiệt các tài khoản ngân hàng. Những chấn động của nó đã định hình lại nền chính trị Mỹ, nền kinh tế, xã hội và văn hóa, và thậm chí cả chính vùng đất. Hãy theo dõi sự kiện lan ra qua bốn hệ thống, cân nhắc ai được lợi và ai gánh chịu tổn thất, và quyết định thay đổi nào để lại dấu ấn sâu đậm nhất.","The United States":"Hoa Kỳ","Compare your four pathways with a partner. Did you find the same immediate and secondary effects?":"Hãy so sánh bốn con đường của em với một bạn học. Các em có tìm ra những tác động tức thời và thứ cấp giống nhau không?","Did you rank the same pathway as most lasting? Defend your ranking with evidence.":"Các em có xếp hạng cùng một con đường là bền lâu nhất không? Hãy bảo vệ thứ hạng của em bằng bằng chứng.","Which system's change lasted longest after the Great Depression? Support your ranking with specific evidence from at least two pathways and two sources.":"Sự thay đổi của hệ thống nào kéo dài lâu nhất sau cuộc Đại Suy Thoái? Hãy củng cố thứ hạng của em bằng bằng chứng cụ thể từ ít nhất hai con đường và hai nguồn.","Summarize how the Great Depression affected one system in your own words.":"Hãy tóm tắt bằng lời của chính em cách cuộc Đại Suy Thoái đã tác động đến một hệ thống.","Connect an immediate effect in one pathway to a secondary effect that still shapes life today.":"Hãy kết nối một tác động tức thời trong một con đường với một tác động thứ cấp vẫn còn định hình cuộc sống ngày nay.","Apply the 'shockwave through systems' idea to a more recent crisis, such as a recession or pandemic.":"Hãy áp dụng ý tưởng 'chấn động lan qua các hệ thống' vào một cuộc khủng hoảng gần đây hơn, chẳng hạn như một cuộc suy thoái hoặc đại dịch.","The Great Depression — Federal Reserve History":"Cuộc Đại Suy Thoái — Lịch sử Cục Dự trữ Liên bang","How bank failures and a shrinking money supply deepened the collapse.":"Cách các vụ đổ vỡ ngân hàng và lượng cung tiền thu hẹp làm sâu sắc thêm cuộc sụp đổ.","What role did bank failures and the Federal Reserve play?":"Các vụ đổ vỡ ngân hàng và Cục Dự trữ Liên bang đã đóng vai trò gì?","How does this source explain the depth of the Depression?":"Nguồn này giải thích như thế nào về mức độ nghiêm trọng của cuộc Suy Thoái?","Farm Security Administration / OWI Photographs — Library of Congress":"Ảnh của Cơ quan An ninh Nông trại / OWI — Thư viện Quốc hội","Government photographs documenting Dust Bowl migrants and rural poverty.":"Những bức ảnh của chính phủ ghi lại người di cư vùng Dust Bowl và cảnh nghèo đói ở nông thôn.","What do the photographs show about who bore the costs?":"Những bức ảnh cho thấy điều gì về việc ai đã gánh chịu tổn thất?","How do images shape the way we remember an era?":"Hình ảnh định hình cách chúng ta ghi nhớ một thời đại như thế nào?","Franklin D. Roosevelt Presidential Library & Museum (National Archives)":"Thư viện & Bảo tàng Tổng thống Franklin D. Roosevelt (Cục Lưu trữ Quốc gia)","FDR's fireside chats and New Deal records documenting the federal response.":"Các buổi trò chuyện bên lò sưởi của FDR và các hồ sơ New Deal ghi lại phản ứng của chính phủ liên bang.","How did FDR explain his response to the public?":"FDR đã giải thích phản ứng của mình với công chúng như thế nào?","Which New Deal program seems most consequential? Why?":"Chương trình New Deal nào có vẻ có ảnh hưởng lớn nhất? Vì sao?","Voters reject Hoover's approach; FDR and the Democrats sweep the 1932 election.":"Cử tri bác bỏ đường lối của Hoover; FDR và Đảng Dân chủ giành thắng lợi áp đảo trong cuộc bầu cử năm 1932.","A lasting expansion of the federal government's role in the economy and social welfare; a new Democratic coalition.":"Sự mở rộng lâu dài vai trò của chính phủ liên bang trong nền kinh tế và phúc lợi xã hội; một liên minh Dân chủ mới.","New Deal laws (Emergency Banking Act, Social Security Act); FDR's fireside chats; growth of federal agencies.":"Các đạo luật New Deal (Đạo luật Ngân hàng Khẩn cấp, Đạo luật An sinh Xã hội); các buổi trò chuyện bên lò sưởi của FDR; sự phát triển của các cơ quan liên bang.","Waves of bank failures, collapsing credit, ~25% unemployment, and a ~30% drop in output.":"Những đợt đổ vỡ ngân hàng, tín dụng sụp đổ, tỷ lệ thất nghiệp ~25% và sản lượng giảm ~30%.","New federal financial regulation and safety nets to prevent a recurrence.":"Quy định tài chính liên bang mới và các mạng lưới an sinh nhằm ngăn ngừa tái diễn.","FDIC (1933), SEC (1934), Social Security (1935); Federal Reserve data on bank suspensions and the money supply.":"FDIC (1933), SEC (1934), An sinh Xã hội (1935); dữ liệu của Cục Dự trữ Liên bang về việc đình chỉ hoạt động ngân hàng và lượng cung tiền.","Widespread poverty, homelessness ('Hoovervilles'), and breadlines; repatriation pressure on people of Mexican heritage.":"Nghèo đói lan rộng, tình trạng vô gia cư ('Hoovervilles') và những hàng người xếp hàng nhận bánh mì; áp lực hồi hương đối với những người gốc Mexico.","A strengthened labor movement and a documentary and protest culture.":"Một phong trào lao động được củng cố cùng một nền văn hóa ghi chép tư liệu và phản kháng.","FSA photographs (Dorothea Lange's Migrant Mother); Steinbeck's The Grapes of Wrath (1939); WPA arts projects.":"Ảnh của FSA (bức Migrant Mother của Dorothea Lange); tiểu thuyết The Grapes of Wrath (Chùm nho phẫn nộ) của Steinbeck (1939); các dự án nghệ thuật của WPA.","The Dust Bowl — drought, over-plowing, and dust storms ruin southern Plains farmland.":"Vùng Dust Bowl — hạn hán, cày xới quá mức và những cơn bão bụi tàn phá đất canh tác ở miền nam Đại Bình nguyên.","Mass 'Okie' migration to California and new federal soil-conservation policy.":"Cuộc di cư ồ ạt của những người 'Okie' đến California và chính sách bảo tồn đất mới của liên bang.","The Soil Conservation Service (1935); FSA migration photos and California migrant-camp records.":"Cơ quan Bảo tồn Đất (1935); các bức ảnh về di cư của FSA và hồ sơ về trại di dân ở California.","Depositors and investors gained lasting protections (FDIC/SEC); the elderly, unemployed, and unionized workers gained a permanent safety net; jobless workers got jobs through the WPA and CCC.":"Người gửi tiền và nhà đầu tư có được sự bảo vệ lâu dài (FDIC/SEC); người cao tuổi, người thất nghiệp và công nhân thuộc công đoàn có được một mạng lưới an sinh vĩnh viễn; người thất nghiệp có được việc làm thông qua WPA và CCC.","Displaced farmers and Dust Bowl migrants; unemployed industrial and Black workers (last hired, first fired); Mexican Americans targeted by repatriation; uninsured depositors of banks that failed before 1933.":"Nông dân bị mất đất và người di cư vùng Dust Bowl; công nhân công nghiệp và công nhân Da đen thất nghiệp (được thuê sau cùng, bị sa thải trước tiên); người Mỹ gốc Mexico bị nhắm đến trong việc hồi hương; người gửi tiền không được bảo hiểm tại các ngân hàng đổ vỡ trước năm 1933.","Which pathway — political, economic, social-cultural, or geographic-environmental — produced the most lasting change in American life? Use specific evidence to defend your ranking.":"Con đường nào — chính trị, kinh tế, văn hóa-xã hội, hay địa lý-môi trường — đã tạo ra sự thay đổi lâu dài nhất trong đời sống nước Mỹ? Hãy dùng bằng chứng cụ thể để bảo vệ thứ hạng của em."},"ar":{"The Great Depression":"الكساد الكبير","Trace how one economic collapse sent shockwaves through four systems — political, economic, social-cultural, and geographic-environmental — and decide which change lasted longest.":"تتبَّع كيف أرسل انهيار اقتصادي واحد موجات صدمة عبر أربعة أنظمة — سياسي واقتصادي واجتماعي-ثقافي وجغرافي-بيئي — وقرِّر أيُّ تغيير دام أطول مدة.","The 1929 crash did more than empty bank accounts. Its shockwaves reshaped American politics, the economy, society and culture, and even the land itself. Follow the event outward through four systems, weigh who benefited and who bore the costs, and decide which change left the deepest mark.":"لم يكتفِ انهيار عام 1929 بإفراغ الحسابات المصرفية. فقد أعادت موجات صدمته تشكيل السياسة الأمريكية والاقتصاد والمجتمع والثقافة، بل والأرض نفسها. تابِع الحدث في انتشاره عبر أربعة أنظمة، ووازِن بين من استفاد ومن تحمَّل التكاليف، وقرِّر أيُّ تغيير ترك الأثر الأعمق.","The United States":"الولايات المتحدة","Compare your four pathways with a partner. Did you find the same immediate and secondary effects?":"قارِن مساراتك الأربعة مع زميل. هل وجدتما الآثار المباشرة والثانوية نفسها؟","Did you rank the same pathway as most lasting? Defend your ranking with evidence.":"هل صنَّفتما المسار نفسه بوصفه الأطول بقاءً؟ دافِع عن ترتيبك بالأدلة.","Which system's change lasted longest after the Great Depression? Support your ranking with specific evidence from at least two pathways and two sources.":"تغيُّرُ أيِّ نظام دام أطول مدة بعد الكساد الكبير؟ ادعم ترتيبك بأدلة محددة من مسارين اثنين على الأقل ومصدرين اثنين.","Summarize how the Great Depression affected one system in your own words.":"لخِّص بأسلوبك الخاص كيف أثَّر الكساد الكبير في أحد الأنظمة.","Connect an immediate effect in one pathway to a secondary effect that still shapes life today.":"اربِط أثرًا مباشرًا في أحد المسارات بأثر ثانوي لا يزال يشكِّل الحياة اليوم.","Apply the 'shockwave through systems' idea to a more recent crisis, such as a recession or pandemic.":"طبِّق فكرة 'موجة الصدمة عبر الأنظمة' على أزمة أحدث عهدًا، مثل ركود اقتصادي أو جائحة.","The Great Depression — Federal Reserve History":"الكساد الكبير — تاريخ الاحتياطي الفيدرالي","How bank failures and a shrinking money supply deepened the collapse.":"كيف عمَّقت إخفاقات المصارف وتقلُّص المعروض النقدي الانهيار.","What role did bank failures and the Federal Reserve play?":"ما الدور الذي أدَّته إخفاقات المصارف والاحتياطي الفيدرالي؟","How does this source explain the depth of the Depression?":"كيف يفسِّر هذا المصدر عمق الكساد؟","Farm Security Administration / OWI Photographs — Library of Congress":"صور إدارة أمن المزارع / مكتب معلومات الحرب (OWI) — مكتبة الكونغرس","Government photographs documenting Dust Bowl migrants and rural poverty.":"صور حكومية توثِّق مهاجري وعاء الغبار (Dust Bowl) والفقر الريفي.","What do the photographs show about who bore the costs?":"ماذا تُظهِر الصور عمَّن تحمَّل التكاليف؟","How do images shape the way we remember an era?":"كيف تشكِّل الصور الطريقة التي نتذكَّر بها حقبةً ما؟","Franklin D. Roosevelt Presidential Library & Museum (National Archives)":"مكتبة ومتحف الرئيس فرانكلين د. روزفلت (الأرشيف الوطني)","FDR's fireside chats and New Deal records documenting the federal response.":"أحاديث روزفلت بجانب المدفأة وسجلات الصفقة الجديدة (New Deal) التي توثِّق الاستجابة الفيدرالية.","How did FDR explain his response to the public?":"كيف شرح روزفلت استجابته للجمهور؟","Which New Deal program seems most consequential? Why?":"أيُّ برنامج من برامج الصفقة الجديدة يبدو الأكثر تأثيرًا؟ ولماذا؟","Voters reject Hoover's approach; FDR and the Democrats sweep the 1932 election.":"يرفض الناخبون نهج هوفر؛ ويكتسح روزفلت والديمقراطيون انتخابات عام 1932.","A lasting expansion of the federal government's role in the economy and social welfare; a new Democratic coalition.":"توسُّع دائم في دور الحكومة الفيدرالية في الاقتصاد والرعاية الاجتماعية؛ وائتلاف ديمقراطي جديد.","New Deal laws (Emergency Banking Act, Social Security Act); FDR's fireside chats; growth of federal agencies.":"قوانين الصفقة الجديدة (قانون الطوارئ المصرفية، قانون الضمان الاجتماعي)؛ أحاديث روزفلت بجانب المدفأة؛ نمو الوكالات الفيدرالية.","Waves of bank failures, collapsing credit, ~25% unemployment, and a ~30% drop in output.":"موجات من إخفاقات المصارف، وانهيار الائتمان، وبطالة بنسبة ~25%، وانخفاض في الإنتاج بنحو ~30%.","New federal financial regulation and safety nets to prevent a recurrence.":"تنظيم مالي فيدرالي جديد وشبكات أمان لمنع تكرار الأزمة.","FDIC (1933), SEC (1934), Social Security (1935); Federal Reserve data on bank suspensions and the money supply.":"المؤسسة الفيدرالية للتأمين على الودائع FDIC (1933)، وهيئة الأوراق المالية والبورصات SEC (1934)، والضمان الاجتماعي (1935)؛ بيانات الاحتياطي الفيدرالي عن تعليق نشاط المصارف والمعروض النقدي.","Widespread poverty, homelessness ('Hoovervilles'), and breadlines; repatriation pressure on people of Mexican heritage.":"فقر واسع الانتشار، وتشرُّد ('هوفرفيل' Hoovervilles)، وطوابير الخبز؛ وضغوط الترحيل على المنحدرين من أصل مكسيكي.","A strengthened labor movement and a documentary and protest culture.":"حركة عمالية أكثر قوة وثقافة توثيقية واحتجاجية.","FSA photographs (Dorothea Lange's Migrant Mother); Steinbeck's The Grapes of Wrath (1939); WPA arts projects.":"صور إدارة أمن المزارع FSA (صورة 'الأم المهاجرة' Migrant Mother لدوروثيا لانج Dorothea Lange)؛ رواية 'عناقيد الغضب' The Grapes of Wrath لستاينبك Steinbeck (1939)؛ المشاريع الفنية لهيئة تقدُّم الأعمال WPA.","The Dust Bowl — drought, over-plowing, and dust storms ruin southern Plains farmland.":"وعاء الغبار (Dust Bowl) — الجفاف والإفراط في الحراثة والعواصف الترابية تدمِّر الأراضي الزراعية في جنوب السهول الكبرى.","Mass 'Okie' migration to California and new federal soil-conservation policy.":"هجرة جماعية لـ'الأوكيين' ('Okie') إلى كاليفورنيا وسياسة فيدرالية جديدة لحفظ التربة.","The Soil Conservation Service (1935); FSA migration photos and California migrant-camp records.":"دائرة حفظ التربة (1935)؛ صور الهجرة الخاصة بإدارة أمن المزارع FSA وسجلات مخيمات المهاجرين في كاليفورنيا.","Depositors and investors gained lasting protections (FDIC/SEC); the elderly, unemployed, and unionized workers gained a permanent safety net; jobless workers got jobs through the WPA and CCC.":"حصل المودِعون والمستثمرون على حماية دائمة (FDIC/SEC)؛ وحصل المسنُّون والعاطلون عن العمل والعمال النقابيون على شبكة أمان دائمة؛ وحصل العاطلون على وظائف من خلال هيئة تقدُّم الأعمال WPA وفيلق الحفاظ المدني CCC.","Displaced farmers and Dust Bowl migrants; unemployed industrial and Black workers (last hired, first fired); Mexican Americans targeted by repatriation; uninsured depositors of banks that failed before 1933.":"مزارعون نزحوا عن أراضيهم ومهاجرو وعاء الغبار (Dust Bowl)؛ عمال الصناعة والعمال السود العاطلون (آخر من يُوظَّف وأول من يُطرَد)؛ الأمريكيون من أصل مكسيكي المستهدَفون بالترحيل؛ المودِعون غير المؤمَّن عليهم في المصارف التي أفلست قبل عام 1933.","Which pathway — political, economic, social-cultural, or geographic-environmental — produced the most lasting change in American life? Use specific evidence to defend your ranking.":"أيُّ مسار — سياسي أو اقتصادي أو اجتماعي-ثقافي أو جغرافي-بيئي — أحدث التغيير الأطول بقاءً في الحياة الأمريكية؟ استخدم أدلة محددة للدفاع عن ترتيبك."},"zh":{"The Great Depression":"大萧条","Trace how one economic collapse sent shockwaves through four systems — political, economic, social-cultural, and geographic-environmental — and decide which change lasted longest.":"追踪一次经济崩溃如何在四个系统——政治、经济、社会文化以及地理环境——中掀起冲击波，并判断哪一项变化持续得最久。","The 1929 crash did more than empty bank accounts. Its shockwaves reshaped American politics, the economy, society and culture, and even the land itself. Follow the event outward through four systems, weigh who benefited and who bore the costs, and decide which change left the deepest mark.":"1929年的股市崩盘不仅仅是掏空了银行账户。它的冲击波重塑了美国政治、经济、社会与文化，甚至改变了土地本身。请沿着这一事件向外追踪它穿越四个系统的过程，权衡谁受益、谁承担了代价，并判断哪一项变化留下了最深刻的印记。","The United States":"美国","Compare your four pathways with a partner. Did you find the same immediate and secondary effects?":"与同伴比较你的四条路径。你们是否发现了相同的直接影响和次生影响？","Did you rank the same pathway as most lasting? Defend your ranking with evidence.":"你们是否把同一条路径评为最持久的？请用证据为你的排名辩护。","Which system's change lasted longest after the Great Depression? Support your ranking with specific evidence from at least two pathways and two sources.":"大萧条之后，哪个系统的变化持续得最久？请用至少两条路径和两个来源中的具体证据来支持你的排名。","Summarize how the Great Depression affected one system in your own words.":"用你自己的话概括大萧条如何影响了某一个系统。","Connect an immediate effect in one pathway to a secondary effect that still shapes life today.":"将某一条路径中的一个直接影响与至今仍在塑造生活的次生影响联系起来。","Apply the 'shockwave through systems' idea to a more recent crisis, such as a recession or pandemic.":"将“冲击波穿越各系统”这一理念应用于一场更近期的危机，例如一次经济衰退或一场大流行病。","The Great Depression — Federal Reserve History":"大萧条——美国联邦储备系统历史","How bank failures and a shrinking money supply deepened the collapse.":"银行倒闭和货币供应量萎缩如何加深了这场崩溃。","What role did bank failures and the Federal Reserve play?":"银行倒闭和联邦储备系统各自扮演了什么角色？","How does this source explain the depth of the Depression?":"这份资料如何解释大萧条的严重程度？","Farm Security Administration / OWI Photographs — Library of Congress":"农场安全管理局／战时新闻局（OWI）照片——美国国会图书馆","Government photographs documenting Dust Bowl migrants and rural poverty.":"记录“沙尘暴”（Dust Bowl）移民和农村贫困的政府照片。","What do the photographs show about who bore the costs?":"这些照片揭示了谁承担了代价？","How do images shape the way we remember an era?":"影像如何塑造我们记忆一个时代的方式？","Franklin D. Roosevelt Presidential Library & Museum (National Archives)":"富兰克林·D·罗斯福总统图书馆暨博物馆（美国国家档案馆）","FDR's fireside chats and New Deal records documenting the federal response.":"罗斯福的“炉边谈话”以及记录联邦政府应对措施的新政（New Deal）档案。","How did FDR explain his response to the public?":"罗斯福如何向公众解释他的应对措施？","Which New Deal program seems most consequential? Why?":"哪一项新政计划看起来影响最为深远？为什么？","Voters reject Hoover's approach; FDR and the Democrats sweep the 1932 election.":"选民否定了胡佛的路线；罗斯福和民主党在1932年大选中大获全胜。","A lasting expansion of the federal government's role in the economy and social welfare; a new Democratic coalition.":"联邦政府在经济和社会福利中的作用得到持久扩张；一个新的民主党联盟形成。","New Deal laws (Emergency Banking Act, Social Security Act); FDR's fireside chats; growth of federal agencies.":"新政法律（《紧急银行法》《社会保障法》）；罗斯福的“炉边谈话”；联邦机构的扩张。","Waves of bank failures, collapsing credit, ~25% unemployment, and a ~30% drop in output.":"一波波银行倒闭、信贷崩溃、约25%的失业率，以及产出下降约30%。","New federal financial regulation and safety nets to prevent a recurrence.":"新的联邦金融监管和安全网，以防止危机重演。","FDIC (1933), SEC (1934), Social Security (1935); Federal Reserve data on bank suspensions and the money supply.":"联邦存款保险公司FDIC（1933年）、证券交易委员会SEC（1934年）、社会保障（1935年）；美国联邦储备系统关于银行停业和货币供应量的数据。","Widespread poverty, homelessness ('Hoovervilles'), and breadlines; repatriation pressure on people of Mexican heritage.":"普遍的贫困、无家可归（“胡佛村”Hoovervilles）以及领面包的长队；对墨西哥裔民众施加的遣返压力。","A strengthened labor movement and a documentary and protest culture.":"一场得到壮大的劳工运动，以及一种纪实与抗议文化。","FSA photographs (Dorothea Lange's Migrant Mother); Steinbeck's The Grapes of Wrath (1939); WPA arts projects.":"FSA照片（多萝西娅·兰格Dorothea Lange的《移民母亲》Migrant Mother）；斯坦贝克Steinbeck的《愤怒的葡萄》The Grapes of Wrath（1939年）；公共事业振兴署WPA的艺术项目。","The Dust Bowl — drought, over-plowing, and dust storms ruin southern Plains farmland.":"“沙尘暴”（Dust Bowl）——干旱、过度耕作和沙尘暴摧毁了南部大平原的农田。","Mass 'Okie' migration to California and new federal soil-conservation policy.":"“俄州人”（Okie）向加利福尼亚的大规模迁移，以及新的联邦土壤保护政策。","The Soil Conservation Service (1935); FSA migration photos and California migrant-camp records.":"土壤保护局（1935年）；FSA的移民照片以及加利福尼亚移民营的记录。","Depositors and investors gained lasting protections (FDIC/SEC); the elderly, unemployed, and unionized workers gained a permanent safety net; jobless workers got jobs through the WPA and CCC.":"储户和投资者获得了持久的保护（FDIC／SEC）；老年人、失业者和加入工会的工人获得了永久性的安全网；失业工人通过WPA和CCC获得了工作。","Displaced farmers and Dust Bowl migrants; unemployed industrial and Black workers (last hired, first fired); Mexican Americans targeted by repatriation; uninsured depositors of banks that failed before 1933.":"流离失所的农民和“沙尘暴”（Dust Bowl）移民；失业的产业工人和黑人工人（最后被雇用、最先被解雇）；成为遣返目标的墨西哥裔美国人；1933年以前倒闭的银行中未受保险保障的储户。","Which pathway — political, economic, social-cultural, or geographic-environmental — produced the most lasting change in American life? Use specific evidence to defend your ranking.":"哪一条路径——政治、经济、社会文化，还是地理环境——在美国生活中造成了最持久的变化？请用具体证据为你的排名辩护。"},"ur":{"The Great Depression":"عظیم کساد بازاری","Trace how one economic collapse sent shockwaves through four systems — political, economic, social-cultural, and geographic-environmental — and decide which change lasted longest.":"اس بات کا سراغ لگائیں کہ ایک معاشی زوال نے چار نظاموں — سیاسی، معاشی، سماجی-ثقافتی اور جغرافیائی-ماحولیاتی — میں کس طرح جھٹکے پہنچائے، اور فیصلہ کریں کہ کون سی تبدیلی سب سے زیادہ دیر تک قائم رہی۔","The 1929 crash did more than empty bank accounts. Its shockwaves reshaped American politics, the economy, society and culture, and even the land itself. Follow the event outward through four systems, weigh who benefited and who bore the costs, and decide which change left the deepest mark.":"1929 کے زوال نے صرف بینک کھاتوں کو خالی نہیں کیا۔ اس کے جھٹکوں نے امریکی سیاست، معیشت، معاشرے اور ثقافت، اور حتیٰ کہ زمین کو بھی نئی شکل دی۔ اس واقعے کو چار نظاموں میں باہر کی جانب پھیلتے ہوئے دیکھیں، تولیں کہ کس نے فائدہ اٹھایا اور کس نے قیمت ادا کی، اور فیصلہ کریں کہ کون سی تبدیلی نے سب سے گہرا نشان چھوڑا۔","The United States":"ریاستہائے متحدہ امریکہ","Compare your four pathways with a partner. Did you find the same immediate and secondary effects?":"اپنے چاروں راستوں کا کسی ساتھی کے ساتھ موازنہ کریں۔ کیا آپ دونوں کو ایک جیسے فوری اور ثانوی اثرات ملے؟","Did you rank the same pathway as most lasting? Defend your ranking with evidence.":"کیا آپ دونوں نے ایک ہی راستے کو سب سے دیرپا قرار دیا؟ اپنی درجہ بندی کا دفاع شواہد سے کریں۔","Which system's change lasted longest after the Great Depression? Support your ranking with specific evidence from at least two pathways and two sources.":"عظیم کساد بازاری کے بعد کس نظام کی تبدیلی سب سے زیادہ دیر تک قائم رہی؟ اپنی درجہ بندی کی تائید کم از کم دو راستوں اور دو ذرائع سے مخصوص شواہد کے ساتھ کریں۔","Summarize how the Great Depression affected one system in your own words.":"اپنے الفاظ میں خلاصہ بیان کریں کہ عظیم کساد بازاری نے کسی ایک نظام کو کس طرح متاثر کیا۔","Connect an immediate effect in one pathway to a secondary effect that still shapes life today.":"کسی ایک راستے کے فوری اثر کو ایسے ثانوی اثر سے جوڑیں جو آج بھی زندگی کو تشکیل دیتا ہے۔","Apply the 'shockwave through systems' idea to a more recent crisis, such as a recession or pandemic.":"'نظاموں کے آر پار جھٹکے' کے تصور کو کسی زیادہ حالیہ بحران، جیسے کساد بازاری یا وبائی مرض، پر لاگو کریں۔","The Great Depression — Federal Reserve History":"عظیم کساد بازاری — فیڈرل ریزرو کی تاریخ","How bank failures and a shrinking money supply deepened the collapse.":"بینکوں کی ناکامیوں اور سکڑتی ہوئی زرِ رسائی نے زوال کو کس طرح گہرا کیا۔","What role did bank failures and the Federal Reserve play?":"بینکوں کی ناکامیوں اور فیڈرل ریزرو نے کیا کردار ادا کیا؟","How does this source explain the depth of the Depression?":"یہ ماخذ کساد بازاری کی گہرائی کی وضاحت کس طرح کرتا ہے؟","Farm Security Administration / OWI Photographs — Library of Congress":"فارم سیکیورٹی ایڈمنسٹریشن / OWI کی تصاویر — لائبریری آف کانگریس","Government photographs documenting Dust Bowl migrants and rural poverty.":"سرکاری تصاویر جو ڈسٹ باؤل (Dust Bowl) کے مہاجرین اور دیہی غربت کو دستاویزی شکل دیتی ہیں۔","What do the photographs show about who bore the costs?":"تصاویر اس بارے میں کیا ظاہر کرتی ہیں کہ قیمت کس نے ادا کی؟","How do images shape the way we remember an era?":"تصاویر اس انداز کو کس طرح تشکیل دیتی ہیں جس میں ہم کسی دور کو یاد کرتے ہیں؟","Franklin D. Roosevelt Presidential Library & Museum (National Archives)":"فرینکلن ڈی۔ روزویلٹ صدارتی لائبریری اور عجائب گھر (نیشنل آرکائیوز)","FDR's fireside chats and New Deal records documenting the federal response.":"ایف ڈی آر کی فائر سائیڈ چیٹس اور نیو ڈیل (New Deal) کے ریکارڈ جو وفاقی ردِعمل کو دستاویزی شکل دیتے ہیں۔","How did FDR explain his response to the public?":"ایف ڈی آر نے عوام کو اپنے ردِعمل کی وضاحت کس طرح کی؟","Which New Deal program seems most consequential? Why?":"نیو ڈیل کا کون سا پروگرام سب سے زیادہ نتیجہ خیز معلوم ہوتا ہے؟ اور کیوں؟","Voters reject Hoover's approach; FDR and the Democrats sweep the 1932 election.":"ووٹر ہوور کے طریقۂ کار کو مسترد کر دیتے ہیں؛ ایف ڈی آر اور ڈیموکریٹس 1932 کے انتخابات میں بھاری کامیابی حاصل کرتے ہیں۔","A lasting expansion of the federal government's role in the economy and social welfare; a new Democratic coalition.":"معیشت اور سماجی بہبود میں وفاقی حکومت کے کردار کی ایک دیرپا توسیع؛ ایک نیا ڈیموکریٹک اتحاد۔","New Deal laws (Emergency Banking Act, Social Security Act); FDR's fireside chats; growth of federal agencies.":"نیو ڈیل کے قوانین (ایمرجنسی بینکنگ ایکٹ، سوشل سیکیورٹی ایکٹ)؛ ایف ڈی آر کی فائر سائیڈ چیٹس؛ وفاقی اداروں کی نمو۔","Waves of bank failures, collapsing credit, ~25% unemployment, and a ~30% drop in output.":"بینکوں کی ناکامیوں کی لہریں، کریڈٹ کا انہدام، تقریباً 25% بے روزگاری، اور پیداوار میں تقریباً 30% کی کمی۔","New federal financial regulation and safety nets to prevent a recurrence.":"دوبارہ وقوع کو روکنے کے لیے نئی وفاقی مالیاتی ضابطہ بندی اور حفاظتی جال۔","FDIC (1933), SEC (1934), Social Security (1935); Federal Reserve data on bank suspensions and the money supply.":"ایف ڈی آئی سی FDIC (1933)، ایس ای سی SEC (1934)، سوشل سیکیورٹی (1935)؛ بینکوں کی معطلی اور زرِ رسائی سے متعلق فیڈرل ریزرو کے اعداد و شمار۔","Widespread poverty, homelessness ('Hoovervilles'), and breadlines; repatriation pressure on people of Mexican heritage.":"بڑے پیمانے پر غربت، بے گھری ('ہوورویلز' Hoovervilles)، اور روٹی کی قطاریں؛ میکسیکن نسل کے لوگوں پر وطن واپسی کا دباؤ۔","A strengthened labor movement and a documentary and protest culture.":"ایک مضبوط تر مزدور تحریک اور ایک دستاویزی و احتجاجی ثقافت۔","FSA photographs (Dorothea Lange's Migrant Mother); Steinbeck's The Grapes of Wrath (1939); WPA arts projects.":"ایف ایس اے FSA کی تصاویر (ڈوروتھیا لینج Dorothea Lange کی 'مائیگرنٹ مدر' Migrant Mother)؛ اسٹائن بیک Steinbeck کا ناول 'دی گریپس آف ریتھ' The Grapes of Wrath (1939)؛ ڈبلیو پی اے WPA کے فنون کے منصوبے۔","The Dust Bowl — drought, over-plowing, and dust storms ruin southern Plains farmland.":"ڈسٹ باؤل (Dust Bowl) — خشک سالی، حد سے زیادہ ہل چلانے اور دھول کے طوفانوں نے جنوبی میدانی علاقوں کی زرعی زمین کو تباہ کر دیا۔","Mass 'Okie' migration to California and new federal soil-conservation policy.":"'اوکی' ('Okie') لوگوں کی کیلیفورنیا کی جانب بڑے پیمانے پر ہجرت اور مٹی کے تحفظ کی نئی وفاقی پالیسی۔","The Soil Conservation Service (1935); FSA migration photos and California migrant-camp records.":"مٹی کے تحفظ کا محکمہ (1935)؛ ایف ایس اے FSA کی ہجرت کی تصاویر اور کیلیفورنیا کے مہاجر کیمپوں کے ریکارڈ۔","Depositors and investors gained lasting protections (FDIC/SEC); the elderly, unemployed, and unionized workers gained a permanent safety net; jobless workers got jobs through the WPA and CCC.":"جمع کنندگان اور سرمایہ کاروں کو دیرپا تحفظات ملے (FDIC/SEC)؛ بزرگوں، بے روزگاروں اور یونین سے وابستہ کارکنوں کو ایک مستقل حفاظتی جال ملا؛ بے روزگار کارکنوں کو ڈبلیو پی اے WPA اور سی سی سی CCC کے ذریعے روزگار ملا۔","Displaced farmers and Dust Bowl migrants; unemployed industrial and Black workers (last hired, first fired); Mexican Americans targeted by repatriation; uninsured depositors of banks that failed before 1933.":"بے گھر ہونے والے کسان اور ڈسٹ باؤل (Dust Bowl) کے مہاجرین؛ بے روزگار صنعتی اور سیاہ فام کارکن (سب سے آخر میں ملازم رکھے گئے، سب سے پہلے نکالے گئے)؛ وطن واپسی کا نشانہ بننے والے میکسیکن امریکی؛ 1933 سے پہلے ناکام ہونے والے بینکوں کے غیر بیمہ شدہ جمع کنندگان۔","Which pathway — political, economic, social-cultural, or geographic-environmental — produced the most lasting change in American life? Use specific evidence to defend your ranking.":"کون سا راستہ — سیاسی، معاشی، سماجی-ثقافتی، یا جغرافیائی-ماحولیاتی — نے امریکی زندگی میں سب سے دیرپا تبدیلی پیدا کی؟ اپنی درجہ بندی کے دفاع کے لیے مخصوص شواہد استعمال کریں۔"},"hi":{"The Great Depression":"महामंदी","Trace how one economic collapse sent shockwaves through four systems — political, economic, social-cultural, and geographic-environmental — and decide which change lasted longest.":"पता लगाएँ कि एक आर्थिक पतन ने चार प्रणालियों — राजनीतिक, आर्थिक, सामाजिक-सांस्कृतिक और भौगोलिक-पर्यावरणीय — में किस तरह आघात-तरंगें भेजीं, और तय करें कि कौन-सा परिवर्तन सबसे लंबे समय तक टिका रहा।","The 1929 crash did more than empty bank accounts. Its shockwaves reshaped American politics, the economy, society and culture, and even the land itself. Follow the event outward through four systems, weigh who benefited and who bore the costs, and decide which change left the deepest mark.":"1929 के पतन ने केवल बैंक खाते ही खाली नहीं किए। इसकी आघात-तरंगों ने अमेरिकी राजनीति, अर्थव्यवस्था, समाज और संस्कृति, और यहाँ तक कि भूमि को भी नए सिरे से ढाल दिया। इस घटना का चार प्रणालियों में बाहर की ओर फैलते हुए अनुसरण करें, तौलें कि किसे लाभ हुआ और किसने कीमत चुकाई, और तय करें कि किस परिवर्तन ने सबसे गहरी छाप छोड़ी।","The United States":"संयुक्त राज्य अमेरिका","Compare your four pathways with a partner. Did you find the same immediate and secondary effects?":"अपने चारों मार्गों की तुलना किसी साथी के साथ करें। क्या आप दोनों को समान तात्कालिक और द्वितीयक प्रभाव मिले?","Did you rank the same pathway as most lasting? Defend your ranking with evidence.":"क्या आपने उसी मार्ग को सबसे स्थायी के रूप में क्रमबद्ध किया? अपनी रैंकिंग का बचाव प्रमाण के साथ करें।","Which system's change lasted longest after the Great Depression? Support your ranking with specific evidence from at least two pathways and two sources.":"महामंदी के बाद किस प्रणाली का परिवर्तन सबसे लंबे समय तक टिका रहा? अपनी रैंकिंग को कम से कम दो मार्गों और दो स्रोतों से विशिष्ट प्रमाण के साथ पुष्ट करें।","Summarize how the Great Depression affected one system in your own words.":"अपने शब्दों में सारांश दें कि महामंदी ने एक प्रणाली को किस प्रकार प्रभावित किया।","Connect an immediate effect in one pathway to a secondary effect that still shapes life today.":"किसी एक मार्ग के तात्कालिक प्रभाव को ऐसे द्वितीयक प्रभाव से जोड़ें जो आज भी जीवन को आकार देता है।","Apply the 'shockwave through systems' idea to a more recent crisis, such as a recession or pandemic.":"'प्रणालियों के आर-पार आघात-तरंग' के विचार को किसी अधिक हालिया संकट, जैसे मंदी या महामारी, पर लागू करें।","The Great Depression — Federal Reserve History":"महामंदी — फ़ेडरल रिज़र्व का इतिहास","How bank failures and a shrinking money supply deepened the collapse.":"बैंकों की विफलताओं और सिकुड़ती मुद्रा आपूर्ति ने पतन को किस प्रकार गहरा किया।","What role did bank failures and the Federal Reserve play?":"बैंकों की विफलताओं और फ़ेडरल रिज़र्व ने क्या भूमिका निभाई?","How does this source explain the depth of the Depression?":"यह स्रोत मंदी की गहराई की व्याख्या किस प्रकार करता है?","Farm Security Administration / OWI Photographs — Library of Congress":"फ़ार्म सिक्योरिटी एडमिनिस्ट्रेशन / OWI की तस्वीरें — लाइब्रेरी ऑफ़ कांग्रेस","Government photographs documenting Dust Bowl migrants and rural poverty.":"सरकारी तस्वीरें जो डस्ट बाउल (Dust Bowl) प्रवासियों और ग्रामीण गरीबी का दस्तावेज़ीकरण करती हैं।","What do the photographs show about who bore the costs?":"तस्वीरें इस बारे में क्या दिखाती हैं कि कीमत किसने चुकाई?","How do images shape the way we remember an era?":"छवियाँ किसी युग को याद करने के हमारे तरीके को किस प्रकार आकार देती हैं?","Franklin D. Roosevelt Presidential Library & Museum (National Archives)":"फ़्रैंकलिन डी. रूज़वेल्ट प्रेसिडेंशियल लाइब्रेरी एवं संग्रहालय (नेशनल आर्काइव्स)","FDR's fireside chats and New Deal records documenting the federal response.":"एफ़डीआर की फ़ायरसाइड चैट्स और न्यू डील (New Deal) के अभिलेख जो संघीय प्रतिक्रिया का दस्तावेज़ीकरण करते हैं।","How did FDR explain his response to the public?":"एफ़डीआर ने जनता को अपनी प्रतिक्रिया किस प्रकार समझाई?","Which New Deal program seems most consequential? Why?":"न्यू डील का कौन-सा कार्यक्रम सबसे अधिक परिणामकारी प्रतीत होता है? और क्यों?","Voters reject Hoover's approach; FDR and the Democrats sweep the 1932 election.":"मतदाता हूवर के दृष्टिकोण को अस्वीकार करते हैं; एफ़डीआर और डेमोक्रेट्स 1932 के चुनाव में भारी जीत हासिल करते हैं।","A lasting expansion of the federal government's role in the economy and social welfare; a new Democratic coalition.":"अर्थव्यवस्था और सामाजिक कल्याण में संघीय सरकार की भूमिका का एक स्थायी विस्तार; एक नया डेमोक्रेटिक गठबंधन।","New Deal laws (Emergency Banking Act, Social Security Act); FDR's fireside chats; growth of federal agencies.":"न्यू डील के कानून (आपातकालीन बैंकिंग अधिनियम, सामाजिक सुरक्षा अधिनियम); एफ़डीआर की फ़ायरसाइड चैट्स; संघीय एजेंसियों की वृद्धि।","Waves of bank failures, collapsing credit, ~25% unemployment, and a ~30% drop in output.":"बैंकों की विफलताओं की लहरें, ऋण का पतन, ~25% बेरोज़गारी, और उत्पादन में ~30% की गिरावट।","New federal financial regulation and safety nets to prevent a recurrence.":"पुनरावृत्ति रोकने के लिए नया संघीय वित्तीय विनियमन और सुरक्षा जाल।","FDIC (1933), SEC (1934), Social Security (1935); Federal Reserve data on bank suspensions and the money supply.":"एफ़डीआईसी FDIC (1933), एसईसी SEC (1934), सामाजिक सुरक्षा (1935); बैंक निलंबनों और मुद्रा आपूर्ति पर फ़ेडरल रिज़र्व के आंकड़े।","Widespread poverty, homelessness ('Hoovervilles'), and breadlines; repatriation pressure on people of Mexican heritage.":"व्यापक गरीबी, बेघरी ('हूवरविल्स' Hoovervilles), और रोटी के लिए लगी कतारें; मेक्सिकन मूल के लोगों पर स्वदेश-वापसी का दबाव।","A strengthened labor movement and a documentary and protest culture.":"एक सुदृढ़ श्रमिक आंदोलन तथा एक वृत्तचित्रात्मक और विरोध की संस्कृति।","FSA photographs (Dorothea Lange's Migrant Mother); Steinbeck's The Grapes of Wrath (1939); WPA arts projects.":"एफ़एसए FSA की तस्वीरें (डोरोथिया लैंग Dorothea Lange की 'माइग्रेंट मदर' Migrant Mother); स्टाइनबेक Steinbeck का 'द ग्रेप्स ऑफ़ रैथ' The Grapes of Wrath (1939); डब्ल्यूपीए WPA की कला परियोजनाएँ।","The Dust Bowl — drought, over-plowing, and dust storms ruin southern Plains farmland.":"डस्ट बाउल (Dust Bowl) — सूखा, अत्यधिक जुताई और धूल भरे तूफ़ान दक्षिणी मैदानों की कृषि भूमि को बर्बाद कर देते हैं।","Mass 'Okie' migration to California and new federal soil-conservation policy.":"'ओकी' ('Okie') लोगों का कैलिफ़ोर्निया की ओर बड़े पैमाने पर पलायन और एक नई संघीय मृदा-संरक्षण नीति।","The Soil Conservation Service (1935); FSA migration photos and California migrant-camp records.":"मृदा संरक्षण सेवा (1935); एफ़एसए FSA की पलायन तस्वीरें और कैलिफ़ोर्निया के प्रवासी शिविरों के अभिलेख।","Depositors and investors gained lasting protections (FDIC/SEC); the elderly, unemployed, and unionized workers gained a permanent safety net; jobless workers got jobs through the WPA and CCC.":"जमाकर्ताओं और निवेशकों को स्थायी संरक्षण मिला (FDIC/SEC); बुज़ुर्गों, बेरोज़गारों और संघबद्ध श्रमिकों को एक स्थायी सुरक्षा जाल मिला; बेरोज़गार श्रमिकों को WPA और CCC के माध्यम से रोज़गार मिला।","Displaced farmers and Dust Bowl migrants; unemployed industrial and Black workers (last hired, first fired); Mexican Americans targeted by repatriation; uninsured depositors of banks that failed before 1933.":"विस्थापित किसान और डस्ट बाउल (Dust Bowl) प्रवासी; बेरोज़गार औद्योगिक और अश्वेत श्रमिक (सबसे बाद में काम पर रखे गए, सबसे पहले निकाले गए); स्वदेश-वापसी का निशाना बने मेक्सिकन अमेरिकी; 1933 से पहले विफल हुए बैंकों के बिना बीमा वाले जमाकर्ता।","Which pathway — political, economic, social-cultural, or geographic-environmental — produced the most lasting change in American life? Use specific evidence to defend your ranking.":"कौन-सा मार्ग — राजनीतिक, आर्थिक, सामाजिक-सांस्कृतिक, या भौगोलिक-पर्यावरणीय — ने अमेरिकी जीवन में सबसे स्थायी परिवर्तन उत्पन्न किया? अपनी रैंकिंग का बचाव करने के लिए विशिष्ट प्रमाण का उपयोग करें।"}},"great-migration":{"es":{"The Great Migration":"La Gran Migración","Connect the people, places, and changes of the Great Migration, when about six million African Americans moved from the rural South to cities across the country.":"Conecta las personas, los lugares y los cambios de la Gran Migración, cuando unos seis millones de afroamericanos se mudaron del Sur rural a ciudades de todo el país.","Between about 1910 and 1970, roughly six million African Americans left the rural South and moved to cities in the North, Midwest, and West — one of the largest movements of people in U.S. history. Who moved, where did they go, and what changed because of it? Map how people, place, and change connect.":"Entre aproximadamente 1910 y 1970, cerca de seis millones de afroamericanos dejaron el Sur rural y se mudaron a ciudades del Norte, el Medio Oeste y el Oeste, uno de los mayores movimientos de personas en la historia de Estados Unidos. ¿Quiénes se mudaron, a dónde fueron y qué cambió por eso? Traza cómo se conectan las personas, el lugar y el cambio.","The rural South to Northern, Midwestern, and Western cities":"Del Sur rural a las ciudades del Norte, el Medio Oeste y el Oeste","Compare your three lenses with a partner. Did you connect the same people to the same places and changes?":"Compara tus tres perspectivas con un compañero. ¿Conectaron a las mismas personas con los mismos lugares y cambios?","Which change do you think mattered most to families who moved? Why?":"¿Qué cambio crees que fue más importante para las familias que se mudaron? ¿Por qué?","In your own words, explain how people, place, and change connect in the Great Migration. Use at least one detail from each lens and one source.":"Con tus propias palabras, explica cómo se conectan las personas, el lugar y el cambio en la Gran Migración. Usa al menos un detalle de cada perspectiva y una fuente.","Explain what the Great Migration was and why families made the move.":"Explica qué fue la Gran Migración y por qué las familias se mudaron.","Connect a push factor in the South to a change that happened in a Northern city.":"Conecta un factor de expulsión en el Sur con un cambio que ocurrió en una ciudad del Norte.","Apply the idea of push and pull factors to a move your own family or community has made.":"Aplica la idea de los factores de expulsión y atracción a una mudanza que haya hecho tu propia familia o comunidad.","Jacob Lawrence: The Migration Series (The Phillips Collection)":"Jacob Lawrence: The Migration Series (The Phillips Collection)","Sixty painted panels (1940–41) telling the story of the Great Migration.":"Sesenta paneles pintados (1940–41) que cuentan la historia de la Gran Migración.","What does one panel show about why people moved or what they found?":"¿Qué muestra un panel sobre por qué se mudaron las personas o qué encontraron?","How does art help us understand history?":"¿Cómo nos ayuda el arte a comprender la historia?","The Great Migration — Classroom Materials (Library of Congress)":"La Gran Migración — Materiales para el aula (Library of Congress)","Background and primary sources on one of the largest internal migrations in U.S. history.":"Antecedentes y fuentes primarias sobre una de las mayores migraciones internas en la historia de Estados Unidos.","What were two reasons families chose to move north?":"¿Cuáles fueron dos razones por las que las familias decidieron mudarse al Norte?","What is one thing that stayed hard even after moving?":"¿Qué es una cosa que siguió siendo difícil incluso después de mudarse?","The Great Migration — African American Heritage (National Archives)":"La Gran Migración — Patrimonio afroamericano (National Archives)","Overview of the two waves of the migration and their effects.":"Panorama general de las dos oleadas de la migración y sus efectos.","About how many people moved, and over how many years?":"¿Aproximadamente cuántas personas se mudaron, y a lo largo de cuántos años?","How were the two waves connected to the world wars?":"¿Cómo se relacionaron las dos oleadas con las guerras mundiales?","African American families and workers from the rural South — sharecroppers, farm laborers, and their children":"Familias y trabajadores afroamericanos del Sur rural: aparceros, jornaleros agrícolas y sus hijos","Jacob Lawrence — a young Black painter who told the story in his Migration Series":"Jacob Lawrence: un joven pintor negro que contó la historia en su Migration Series","Robert S. Abbott — editor of the Chicago Defender, which urged people to move north":"Robert S. Abbott: editor del Chicago Defender, que instaba a la gente a mudarse al Norte","Pullman porters — Black railroad workers who carried news north and south":"Los mozos Pullman: trabajadores ferroviarios negros que llevaban noticias del Norte al Sur y viceversa","From the South — Mississippi, Alabama, Georgia, Louisiana, and Texas":"Desde el Sur: Mississippi, Alabama, Georgia, Louisiana y Texas","To the North and Midwest — Chicago, Detroit, New York (Harlem), Pittsburgh, Cleveland":"Hacia el Norte y el Medio Oeste: Chicago, Detroit, Nueva York (Harlem), Pittsburgh, Cleveland","To the West (later wave) — Los Angeles, Oakland, Seattle":"Hacia el Oeste (oleada posterior): Los Ángeles, Oakland, Seattle","Along the railroads — the rail lines were the highways of the migration":"A lo largo de los ferrocarriles: las líneas de tren fueron las carreteras de la migración","Community: big new African American neighborhoods grew in Northern and Western cities":"Comunidad: crecieron grandes barrios afroamericanos nuevos en las ciudades del Norte y del Oeste","Economy: families moved from farm work to paid factory, steel, and railroad jobs":"Economía: las familias pasaron del trabajo agrícola a empleos remunerados en fábricas, acerías y ferrocarriles","Culture: a burst of art, music, and writing — the Harlem Renaissance, jazz, and blues":"Cultura: un florecimiento de arte, música y escritura: el Renacimiento de Harlem, el jazz y el blues","Daily life: children attended better-funded schools and adults could vote — but families faced new housing discrimination":"Vida cotidiana: los niños asistían a escuelas con más recursos y los adultos podían votar, pero las familias enfrentaban una nueva discriminación en la vivienda","The nation's map: the Black population shifted from mostly rural-Southern to urban and nationwide":"El mapa del país: la población negra pasó de ser principalmente rural y sureña a ser urbana y estar por todo el país","When millions of families left Southern farms and rode the railroads to cities like Chicago, Detroit, and New York, they built new communities, took new jobs, and created new music and art — changing both their own lives and the whole country.":"Cuando millones de familias dejaron las granjas del Sur y viajaron en tren a ciudades como Chicago, Detroit y Nueva York, formaron nuevas comunidades, consiguieron nuevos empleos y crearon nueva música y arte, cambiando tanto sus propias vidas como todo el país."},"vi":{"The Great Migration":"Cuộc Đại Di Cư","Connect the people, places, and changes of the Great Migration, when about six million African Americans moved from the rural South to cities across the country.":"Hãy kết nối những con người, những nơi chốn và những thay đổi của Cuộc Đại Di Cư, khi khoảng sáu triệu người Mỹ gốc Phi rời vùng nông thôn miền Nam để đến các thành phố khắp cả nước.","Between about 1910 and 1970, roughly six million African Americans left the rural South and moved to cities in the North, Midwest, and West — one of the largest movements of people in U.S. history. Who moved, where did they go, and what changed because of it? Map how people, place, and change connect.":"Từ khoảng năm 1910 đến năm 1970, gần sáu triệu người Mỹ gốc Phi đã rời vùng nông thôn miền Nam và chuyển đến các thành phố ở miền Bắc, miền Trung Tây và miền Tây — một trong những cuộc di chuyển lớn nhất của con người trong lịch sử Hoa Kỳ. Ai đã di cư, họ đi đâu, và điều gì đã thay đổi vì cuộc di cư này? Hãy vẽ sơ đồ cách con người, nơi chốn và thay đổi kết nối với nhau.","The rural South to Northern, Midwestern, and Western cities":"Từ vùng nông thôn miền Nam đến các thành phố miền Bắc, miền Trung Tây và miền Tây","Compare your three lenses with a partner. Did you connect the same people to the same places and changes?":"Hãy so sánh ba góc nhìn của em với một bạn. Các em có kết nối cùng những con người với cùng những nơi chốn và thay đổi không?","Which change do you think mattered most to families who moved? Why?":"Em nghĩ thay đổi nào quan trọng nhất đối với những gia đình đã di cư? Vì sao?","In your own words, explain how people, place, and change connect in the Great Migration. Use at least one detail from each lens and one source.":"Bằng lời của chính em, hãy giải thích cách con người, nơi chốn và thay đổi kết nối với nhau trong Cuộc Đại Di Cư. Hãy dùng ít nhất một chi tiết từ mỗi góc nhìn và một nguồn tư liệu.","Explain what the Great Migration was and why families made the move.":"Hãy giải thích Cuộc Đại Di Cư là gì và vì sao các gia đình đã di cư.","Connect a push factor in the South to a change that happened in a Northern city.":"Hãy kết nối một yếu tố đẩy ở miền Nam với một thay đổi đã diễn ra ở một thành phố miền Bắc.","Apply the idea of push and pull factors to a move your own family or community has made.":"Hãy áp dụng ý tưởng về các yếu tố đẩy và kéo vào một lần di chuyển mà chính gia đình hoặc cộng đồng của em đã trải qua.","Jacob Lawrence: The Migration Series (The Phillips Collection)":"Jacob Lawrence: The Migration Series (The Phillips Collection)","Sixty painted panels (1940–41) telling the story of the Great Migration.":"Sáu mươi bức tranh (1940–41) kể lại câu chuyện về Cuộc Đại Di Cư.","What does one panel show about why people moved or what they found?":"Một bức tranh cho thấy điều gì về lý do người ta di cư hoặc điều họ đã tìm thấy?","How does art help us understand history?":"Nghệ thuật giúp chúng ta hiểu lịch sử như thế nào?","The Great Migration — Classroom Materials (Library of Congress)":"Cuộc Đại Di Cư — Tài liệu lớp học (Library of Congress)","Background and primary sources on one of the largest internal migrations in U.S. history.":"Bối cảnh và các nguồn tư liệu gốc về một trong những cuộc di cư nội địa lớn nhất trong lịch sử Hoa Kỳ.","What were two reasons families chose to move north?":"Hai lý do khiến các gia đình chọn di cư lên miền Bắc là gì?","What is one thing that stayed hard even after moving?":"Một điều gì vẫn còn khó khăn ngay cả sau khi đã di cư?","The Great Migration — African American Heritage (National Archives)":"Cuộc Đại Di Cư — Di sản người Mỹ gốc Phi (National Archives)","Overview of the two waves of the migration and their effects.":"Tổng quan về hai đợt di cư và những tác động của chúng.","About how many people moved, and over how many years?":"Khoảng bao nhiêu người đã di cư, và trong bao nhiêu năm?","How were the two waves connected to the world wars?":"Hai đợt di cư này liên quan đến các cuộc thế chiến như thế nào?","African American families and workers from the rural South — sharecroppers, farm laborers, and their children":"Các gia đình và người lao động Mỹ gốc Phi từ vùng nông thôn miền Nam — những người làm rẽ, người làm thuê trong nông trại, và con cái của họ","Jacob Lawrence — a young Black painter who told the story in his Migration Series":"Jacob Lawrence — một họa sĩ da đen trẻ tuổi đã kể lại câu chuyện trong Migration Series của mình","Robert S. Abbott — editor of the Chicago Defender, which urged people to move north":"Robert S. Abbott — chủ bút của tờ Chicago Defender, tờ báo đã kêu gọi người dân di cư lên miền Bắc","Pullman porters — Black railroad workers who carried news north and south":"Những người phục vụ toa Pullman — công nhân đường sắt da đen đã mang tin tức đi khắp miền Bắc và miền Nam","From the South — Mississippi, Alabama, Georgia, Louisiana, and Texas":"Từ miền Nam — Mississippi, Alabama, Georgia, Louisiana và Texas","To the North and Midwest — Chicago, Detroit, New York (Harlem), Pittsburgh, Cleveland":"Đến miền Bắc và miền Trung Tây — Chicago, Detroit, New York (Harlem), Pittsburgh, Cleveland","To the West (later wave) — Los Angeles, Oakland, Seattle":"Đến miền Tây (đợt sau) — Los Angeles, Oakland, Seattle","Along the railroads — the rail lines were the highways of the migration":"Dọc theo các tuyến đường sắt — những tuyến đường sắt chính là đường lớn của cuộc di cư","Community: big new African American neighborhoods grew in Northern and Western cities":"Cộng đồng: những khu phố người Mỹ gốc Phi mới rộng lớn đã hình thành ở các thành phố miền Bắc và miền Tây","Economy: families moved from farm work to paid factory, steel, and railroad jobs":"Kinh tế: các gia đình chuyển từ làm nông sang những công việc được trả lương trong nhà máy, ngành thép và đường sắt","Culture: a burst of art, music, and writing — the Harlem Renaissance, jazz, and blues":"Văn hóa: một sự bùng nổ của nghệ thuật, âm nhạc và văn chương — phong trào Phục hưng Harlem, nhạc jazz và nhạc blues","Daily life: children attended better-funded schools and adults could vote — but families faced new housing discrimination":"Cuộc sống hằng ngày: trẻ em được học ở những trường có kinh phí tốt hơn và người lớn được đi bầu — nhưng các gia đình lại đối mặt với sự phân biệt đối xử mới về nhà ở","The nation's map: the Black population shifted from mostly rural-Southern to urban and nationwide":"Bản đồ của cả nước: dân số người da đen chuyển từ chủ yếu ở nông thôn miền Nam sang sống ở thành thị và trải rộng khắp cả nước","When millions of families left Southern farms and rode the railroads to cities like Chicago, Detroit, and New York, they built new communities, took new jobs, and created new music and art — changing both their own lives and the whole country.":"Khi hàng triệu gia đình rời những nông trại miền Nam và đi tàu hỏa đến các thành phố như Chicago, Detroit và New York, họ đã xây dựng những cộng đồng mới, nhận những công việc mới, và sáng tạo ra âm nhạc và nghệ thuật mới — thay đổi cả cuộc sống của chính họ lẫn cả đất nước."},"ar":{"The Great Migration":"الهجرة الكبرى","Connect the people, places, and changes of the Great Migration, when about six million African Americans moved from the rural South to cities across the country.":"اربط بين الناس والأماكن والتغيّرات في الهجرة الكبرى، عندما انتقل نحو ستة ملايين أمريكي من أصل أفريقي من الريف الجنوبي إلى المدن في أنحاء البلاد.","Between about 1910 and 1970, roughly six million African Americans left the rural South and moved to cities in the North, Midwest, and West — one of the largest movements of people in U.S. history. Who moved, where did they go, and what changed because of it? Map how people, place, and change connect.":"بين نحو عامي 1910 و1970، غادر قرابة ستة ملايين أمريكي من أصل أفريقي الريف الجنوبي وانتقلوا إلى مدن في الشمال والغرب الأوسط والغرب — وهي إحدى أكبر حركات الناس في تاريخ الولايات المتحدة. مَن الذين انتقلوا، وإلى أين ذهبوا، وما الذي تغيّر بسبب ذلك؟ ارسم كيف يترابط الناس والمكان والتغيّر.","The rural South to Northern, Midwestern, and Western cities":"من الريف الجنوبي إلى مدن الشمال والغرب الأوسط والغرب","Compare your three lenses with a partner. Did you connect the same people to the same places and changes?":"قارن عدساتك الثلاث مع زميل. هل ربطتما الأشخاص أنفسهم بالأماكن والتغيّرات نفسها؟","Which change do you think mattered most to families who moved? Why?":"أيّ تغيّر تعتقد أنه كان الأهم للعائلات التي انتقلت؟ ولماذا؟","In your own words, explain how people, place, and change connect in the Great Migration. Use at least one detail from each lens and one source.":"بأسلوبك الخاص، اشرح كيف يترابط الناس والمكان والتغيّر في الهجرة الكبرى. استخدم تفصيلاً واحداً على الأقل من كل عدسة ومصدراً واحداً.","Explain what the Great Migration was and why families made the move.":"اشرح ما كانت الهجرة الكبرى ولماذا انتقلت العائلات.","Connect a push factor in the South to a change that happened in a Northern city.":"اربط عاملاً دافعاً في الجنوب بتغيّر حدث في مدينة شمالية.","Apply the idea of push and pull factors to a move your own family or community has made.":"طبّق فكرة عوامل الدفع والجذب على انتقال قامت به عائلتك أو مجتمعك.","Jacob Lawrence: The Migration Series (The Phillips Collection)":"جيكوب لورانس: سلسلة الهجرة (The Migration Series) (The Phillips Collection)","Sixty painted panels (1940–41) telling the story of the Great Migration.":"ستون لوحة مرسومة (1940–41) تروي قصة الهجرة الكبرى.","What does one panel show about why people moved or what they found?":"ماذا تُظهر إحدى اللوحات عن سبب انتقال الناس أو ما وجدوه؟","How does art help us understand history?":"كيف يساعدنا الفن على فهم التاريخ؟","The Great Migration — Classroom Materials (Library of Congress)":"الهجرة الكبرى — مواد صفّية (Library of Congress)","Background and primary sources on one of the largest internal migrations in U.S. history.":"خلفية ومصادر أولية عن إحدى أكبر الهجرات الداخلية في تاريخ الولايات المتحدة.","What were two reasons families chose to move north?":"ما هما سببان دفعا العائلات إلى اختيار الانتقال شمالاً؟","What is one thing that stayed hard even after moving?":"ما الشيء الذي ظل صعباً حتى بعد الانتقال؟","The Great Migration — African American Heritage (National Archives)":"الهجرة الكبرى — التراث الأمريكي الأفريقي (National Archives)","Overview of the two waves of the migration and their effects.":"نظرة عامة على موجتي الهجرة وآثارهما.","About how many people moved, and over how many years?":"كم عدد الناس الذين انتقلوا تقريباً، وعلى مدى كم سنة؟","How were the two waves connected to the world wars?":"كيف ارتبطت الموجتان بالحربين العالميتين؟","African American families and workers from the rural South — sharecroppers, farm laborers, and their children":"العائلات والعمال الأمريكيون من أصل أفريقي من الريف الجنوبي — المزارعون بالمشاركة والعمال الزراعيون وأطفالهم","Jacob Lawrence — a young Black painter who told the story in his Migration Series":"جيكوب لورانس — رسّام أسود شاب روى القصة في سلسلته Migration Series","Robert S. Abbott — editor of the Chicago Defender, which urged people to move north":"روبرت س. أبوت — محرّر صحيفة Chicago Defender التي حثّت الناس على الانتقال شمالاً","Pullman porters — Black railroad workers who carried news north and south":"حمّالو قطارات بولمان — عمّال سكك حديدية سود نقلوا الأخبار بين الشمال والجنوب","From the South — Mississippi, Alabama, Georgia, Louisiana, and Texas":"من الجنوب — ميسيسيبي وألاباما وجورجيا ولويزيانا وتكساس","To the North and Midwest — Chicago, Detroit, New York (Harlem), Pittsburgh, Cleveland":"إلى الشمال والغرب الأوسط — شيكاغو وديترويت ونيويورك (هارلم) وبيتسبرغ وكليفلاند","To the West (later wave) — Los Angeles, Oakland, Seattle":"إلى الغرب (الموجة اللاحقة) — لوس أنجلوس وأوكلاند وسياتل","Along the railroads — the rail lines were the highways of the migration":"على امتداد السكك الحديدية — كانت خطوط السكك طرقات الهجرة الرئيسية","Community: big new African American neighborhoods grew in Northern and Western cities":"المجتمع: نشأت أحياء أمريكية أفريقية جديدة كبيرة في مدن الشمال والغرب","Economy: families moved from farm work to paid factory, steel, and railroad jobs":"الاقتصاد: انتقلت العائلات من العمل الزراعي إلى وظائف مأجورة في المصانع والصلب والسكك الحديدية","Culture: a burst of art, music, and writing — the Harlem Renaissance, jazz, and blues":"الثقافة: انفجار في الفن والموسيقى والكتابة — نهضة هارلم وموسيقى الجاز والبلوز","Daily life: children attended better-funded schools and adults could vote — but families faced new housing discrimination":"الحياة اليومية: التحق الأطفال بمدارس أفضل تمويلاً وتمكّن الكبار من التصويت — لكن العائلات واجهت تمييزاً جديداً في السكن","The nation's map: the Black population shifted from mostly rural-Southern to urban and nationwide":"خريطة الأمة: تحوّل السكان السود من ريفيين جنوبيين في معظمهم إلى حضريين ومنتشرين في أنحاء البلاد","When millions of families left Southern farms and rode the railroads to cities like Chicago, Detroit, and New York, they built new communities, took new jobs, and created new music and art — changing both their own lives and the whole country.":"عندما غادر ملايين العائلات مزارع الجنوب واستقلّوا القطارات إلى مدن مثل شيكاغو وديترويت ونيويورك، بنوا مجتمعات جديدة، وتولّوا وظائف جديدة، وأبدعوا موسيقى وفناً جديدين — فغيّروا حياتهم وحياة البلد كله."},"zh":{"The Great Migration":"大迁徙","Connect the people, places, and changes of the Great Migration, when about six million African Americans moved from the rural South to cities across the country.":"把大迁徙中的人物、地点和变化连起来。当时约有六百万非裔美国人从南方乡村搬到了全国各地的城市。","Between about 1910 and 1970, roughly six million African Americans left the rural South and moved to cities in the North, Midwest, and West — one of the largest movements of people in U.S. history. Who moved, where did they go, and what changed because of it? Map how people, place, and change connect.":"大约在1910年到1970年之间，将近六百万非裔美国人离开南方乡村，搬到北方、中西部和西部的城市——这是美国历史上规模最大的人口迁移之一。是谁搬走了，他们去了哪里，因此又发生了什么变化？画出人物、地点和变化是如何连起来的。","The rural South to Northern, Midwestern, and Western cities":"从南方乡村到北方、中西部和西部的城市","Compare your three lenses with a partner. Did you connect the same people to the same places and changes?":"和同伴比一比你的三个视角。你们是否把同样的人连到了同样的地点和变化上？","Which change do you think mattered most to families who moved? Why?":"你觉得对搬迁的家庭来说，哪一个变化最重要？为什么？","In your own words, explain how people, place, and change connect in the Great Migration. Use at least one detail from each lens and one source.":"用你自己的话说一说，在大迁徙中人物、地点和变化是如何连在一起的。至少从每个视角各用一个细节，并使用一份资料。","Explain what the Great Migration was and why families made the move.":"说一说大迁徙是什么，以及各个家庭为什么要搬家。","Connect a push factor in the South to a change that happened in a Northern city.":"把南方的一个推力因素和北方城市里发生的一个变化连起来。","Apply the idea of push and pull factors to a move your own family or community has made.":"把推力和拉力因素的想法用到你自己家庭或社区曾经的一次搬迁上。","Jacob Lawrence: The Migration Series (The Phillips Collection)":"雅各布·劳伦斯（Jacob Lawrence）：《迁徙系列》（The Migration Series，菲利普斯收藏馆 The Phillips Collection）","Sixty painted panels (1940–41) telling the story of the Great Migration.":"六十幅画作（1940–41年），讲述大迁徙的故事。","What does one panel show about why people moved or what they found?":"有一幅画告诉我们人们为什么搬迁，或者他们找到了什么？","How does art help us understand history?":"艺术怎样帮助我们理解历史？","The Great Migration — Classroom Materials (Library of Congress)":"大迁徙——课堂材料（美国国会图书馆 Library of Congress）","Background and primary sources on one of the largest internal migrations in U.S. history.":"关于美国历史上规模最大的国内迁移之一的背景资料和原始资料。","What were two reasons families chose to move north?":"各个家庭选择北迁的两个原因是什么？","What is one thing that stayed hard even after moving?":"有哪一件事，即使搬家之后仍然很艰难？","The Great Migration — African American Heritage (National Archives)":"大迁徙——非裔美国人遗产（美国国家档案馆 National Archives）","Overview of the two waves of the migration and their effects.":"对这次迁徙的两次浪潮及其影响的概述。","About how many people moved, and over how many years?":"大约有多少人搬迁，历时多少年？","How were the two waves connected to the world wars?":"这两次浪潮和两次世界大战有什么联系？","African American families and workers from the rural South — sharecroppers, farm laborers, and their children":"来自南方乡村的非裔美国家庭和工人——分成佃农、农场工人以及他们的孩子","Jacob Lawrence — a young Black painter who told the story in his Migration Series":"雅各布·劳伦斯（Jacob Lawrence）——一位年轻的黑人画家，用他的《迁徙系列》（Migration Series）讲述了这个故事","Robert S. Abbott — editor of the Chicago Defender, which urged people to move north":"罗伯特·S·阿博特（Robert S. Abbott）——《芝加哥卫报》（Chicago Defender）的编辑，这份报纸鼓励人们北迁","Pullman porters — Black railroad workers who carried news north and south":"普尔曼列车服务员（Pullman porters）——黑人铁路工人，把消息在南北之间传递","From the South — Mississippi, Alabama, Georgia, Louisiana, and Texas":"来自南方——密西西比（Mississippi）、亚拉巴马（Alabama）、佐治亚（Georgia）、路易斯安那（Louisiana）和得克萨斯（Texas）","To the North and Midwest — Chicago, Detroit, New York (Harlem), Pittsburgh, Cleveland":"前往北方和中西部——芝加哥（Chicago）、底特律（Detroit）、纽约（New York，哈莱姆区 Harlem）、匹兹堡（Pittsburgh）、克利夫兰（Cleveland）","To the West (later wave) — Los Angeles, Oakland, Seattle":"前往西部（较晚的一次浪潮）——洛杉矶（Los Angeles）、奥克兰（Oakland）、西雅图（Seattle）","Along the railroads — the rail lines were the highways of the migration":"沿着铁路——铁路线就是这次迁徙的大道","Community: big new African American neighborhoods grew in Northern and Western cities":"社区：北方和西部的城市里出现了大片新的非裔美国人社区","Economy: families moved from farm work to paid factory, steel, and railroad jobs":"经济：各个家庭从农活转向工厂、钢铁厂和铁路上的有薪工作","Culture: a burst of art, music, and writing — the Harlem Renaissance, jazz, and blues":"文化：艺术、音乐和写作的大爆发——哈莱姆文艺复兴（Harlem Renaissance）、爵士乐和布鲁斯","Daily life: children attended better-funded schools and adults could vote — but families faced new housing discrimination":"日常生活：孩子们上了经费更充足的学校，大人可以投票——但各个家庭又遇到了新的住房歧视","The nation's map: the Black population shifted from mostly rural-Southern to urban and nationwide":"全国的地图：黑人人口从主要集中在南方乡村，转变为分布在城市和全国各地","When millions of families left Southern farms and rode the railroads to cities like Chicago, Detroit, and New York, they built new communities, took new jobs, and created new music and art — changing both their own lives and the whole country.":"当数百万个家庭离开南方的农场，乘火车来到芝加哥、底特律和纽约这样的城市时，他们建立了新的社区，从事了新的工作，创造了新的音乐和艺术——既改变了自己的生活，也改变了整个国家。"},"ur":{"The Great Migration":"عظیم ہجرت","Connect the people, places, and changes of the Great Migration, when about six million African Americans moved from the rural South to cities across the country.":"عظیم ہجرت کے لوگوں، مقامات اور تبدیلیوں کو آپس میں جوڑیں، جب تقریباً ساٹھ لاکھ افریقی امریکی دیہی جنوب سے ملک بھر کے شہروں میں منتقل ہوئے۔","Between about 1910 and 1970, roughly six million African Americans left the rural South and moved to cities in the North, Midwest, and West — one of the largest movements of people in U.S. history. Who moved, where did they go, and what changed because of it? Map how people, place, and change connect.":"تقریباً 1910 اور 1970 کے درمیان قریب ساٹھ لاکھ افریقی امریکیوں نے دیہی جنوب کو چھوڑا اور شمال، وسط مغرب اور مغرب کے شہروں میں منتقل ہو گئے — یہ امریکی تاریخ میں لوگوں کی سب سے بڑی نقل مکانیوں میں سے ایک تھی۔ کون منتقل ہوئے، وہ کہاں گئے، اور اس کی وجہ سے کیا بدلا؟ نقشہ بنائیں کہ لوگ، مقام اور تبدیلی کیسے آپس میں جڑے ہیں۔","The rural South to Northern, Midwestern, and Western cities":"دیہی جنوب سے شمالی، وسط مغربی اور مغربی شہروں تک","Compare your three lenses with a partner. Did you connect the same people to the same places and changes?":"اپنے تین زاویوں کا ایک ساتھی کے ساتھ موازنہ کریں۔ کیا آپ نے وہی لوگ وہی مقامات اور تبدیلیوں سے جوڑے؟","Which change do you think mattered most to families who moved? Why?":"آپ کے خیال میں کون سی تبدیلی منتقل ہونے والے خاندانوں کے لیے سب سے اہم تھی؟ کیوں؟","In your own words, explain how people, place, and change connect in the Great Migration. Use at least one detail from each lens and one source.":"اپنے الفاظ میں بیان کریں کہ عظیم ہجرت میں لوگ، مقام اور تبدیلی کیسے آپس میں جڑتے ہیں۔ ہر زاویے سے کم از کم ایک تفصیل اور ایک ماخذ استعمال کریں۔","Explain what the Great Migration was and why families made the move.":"بیان کریں کہ عظیم ہجرت کیا تھی اور خاندانوں نے نقل مکانی کیوں کی۔","Connect a push factor in the South to a change that happened in a Northern city.":"جنوب کے ایک دھکیلنے والے عامل کو کسی شمالی شہر میں ہونے والی تبدیلی سے جوڑیں۔","Apply the idea of push and pull factors to a move your own family or community has made.":"دھکیلنے اور کھینچنے والے عوامل کے تصور کو اپنے خاندان یا برادری کی کسی نقل مکانی پر لاگو کریں۔","Jacob Lawrence: The Migration Series (The Phillips Collection)":"جیکب لارنس: دی مائیگریشن سیریز (The Migration Series) (The Phillips Collection)","Sixty painted panels (1940–41) telling the story of the Great Migration.":"ساٹھ مصور تختیاں (1940–41) جو عظیم ہجرت کی کہانی سناتی ہیں۔","What does one panel show about why people moved or what they found?":"ایک تختی لوگوں کے منتقل ہونے کی وجہ یا انہیں جو ملا اس کے بارے میں کیا دکھاتی ہے؟","How does art help us understand history?":"فن ہمیں تاریخ سمجھنے میں کیسے مدد دیتا ہے؟","The Great Migration — Classroom Materials (Library of Congress)":"عظیم ہجرت — کلاس روم مواد (Library of Congress)","Background and primary sources on one of the largest internal migrations in U.S. history.":"امریکی تاریخ کی سب سے بڑی اندرونی ہجرتوں میں سے ایک کے بارے میں پس منظر اور بنیادی مآخذ۔","What were two reasons families chose to move north?":"خاندانوں نے شمال کی طرف جانے کا فیصلہ کیوں کیا، اس کی دو وجوہات کیا تھیں؟","What is one thing that stayed hard even after moving?":"ایک ایسی چیز کیا ہے جو منتقل ہونے کے بعد بھی مشکل رہی؟","The Great Migration — African American Heritage (National Archives)":"عظیم ہجرت — افریقی امریکی ورثہ (National Archives)","Overview of the two waves of the migration and their effects.":"ہجرت کی دو لہروں اور ان کے اثرات کا جائزہ۔","About how many people moved, and over how many years?":"تقریباً کتنے لوگ منتقل ہوئے، اور کتنے سالوں میں؟","How were the two waves connected to the world wars?":"یہ دو لہریں عالمی جنگوں سے کیسے جڑی تھیں؟","African American families and workers from the rural South — sharecroppers, farm laborers, and their children":"دیہی جنوب سے افریقی امریکی خاندان اور مزدور — بٹائی دار کسان، کھیت مزدور، اور ان کے بچے","Jacob Lawrence — a young Black painter who told the story in his Migration Series":"جیکب لارنس — ایک نوجوان سیاہ فام مصور جس نے اپنی Migration Series میں یہ کہانی بیان کی","Robert S. Abbott — editor of the Chicago Defender, which urged people to move north":"رابرٹ ایس ایبٹ — Chicago Defender کے مدیر، جس نے لوگوں کو شمال کی طرف جانے کی ترغیب دی","Pullman porters — Black railroad workers who carried news north and south":"پلمین پورٹرز — سیاہ فام ریلوے مزدور جو شمال اور جنوب کے درمیان خبریں لے جاتے تھے","From the South — Mississippi, Alabama, Georgia, Louisiana, and Texas":"جنوب سے — مسیسیپی، الاباما، جارجیا، لوزیانا، اور ٹیکساس","To the North and Midwest — Chicago, Detroit, New York (Harlem), Pittsburgh, Cleveland":"شمال اور وسط مغرب کی طرف — شکاگو، ڈیٹرائٹ، نیویارک (ہارلم)، پٹسبرگ، کلیولینڈ","To the West (later wave) — Los Angeles, Oakland, Seattle":"مغرب کی طرف (بعد کی لہر) — لاس اینجلس، اوکلینڈ، سیئٹل","Along the railroads — the rail lines were the highways of the migration":"ریلوے لائنوں کے ساتھ ساتھ — ریل کی پٹریاں ہی اس ہجرت کی شاہراہیں تھیں","Community: big new African American neighborhoods grew in Northern and Western cities":"برادری: شمالی اور مغربی شہروں میں بڑے نئے افریقی امریکی محلے پروان چڑھے","Economy: families moved from farm work to paid factory, steel, and railroad jobs":"معیشت: خاندان کھیتی باڑی سے نکل کر کارخانوں، فولاد اور ریلوے کی تنخواہ دار نوکریوں کی طرف آ گئے","Culture: a burst of art, music, and writing — the Harlem Renaissance, jazz, and blues":"ثقافت: فن، موسیقی اور تحریر کا ایک عروج — ہارلم نشاۃِ ثانیہ، جاز اور بلیوز","Daily life: children attended better-funded schools and adults could vote — but families faced new housing discrimination":"روزمرہ زندگی: بچے بہتر مالی وسائل والے اسکولوں میں جانے لگے اور بڑے ووٹ ڈال سکتے تھے — لیکن خاندانوں کو رہائش میں نئے امتیازی سلوک کا سامنا ہوا","The nation's map: the Black population shifted from mostly rural-Southern to urban and nationwide":"قوم کا نقشہ: سیاہ فام آبادی زیادہ تر دیہی جنوبی سے بدل کر شہری اور ملک بھر میں پھیل گئی","When millions of families left Southern farms and rode the railroads to cities like Chicago, Detroit, and New York, they built new communities, took new jobs, and created new music and art — changing both their own lives and the whole country.":"جب لاکھوں خاندانوں نے جنوبی کھیت چھوڑے اور ریل گاڑیوں پر سوار ہو کر شکاگو، ڈیٹرائٹ اور نیویارک جیسے شہروں میں پہنچے، تو انہوں نے نئی برادریاں بنائیں، نئی نوکریاں کیں، اور نئی موسیقی اور فن تخلیق کیا — اور یوں اپنی زندگی اور پورے ملک دونوں کو بدل ڈالا۔"},"hi":{"The Great Migration":"महान प्रवास","Connect the people, places, and changes of the Great Migration, when about six million African Americans moved from the rural South to cities across the country.":"महान प्रवास के लोगों, स्थानों और बदलावों को जोड़ो, जब लगभग साठ लाख अफ्रीकी अमेरिकी ग्रामीण दक्षिण से देश भर के शहरों में चले गए।","Between about 1910 and 1970, roughly six million African Americans left the rural South and moved to cities in the North, Midwest, and West — one of the largest movements of people in U.S. history. Who moved, where did they go, and what changed because of it? Map how people, place, and change connect.":"लगभग 1910 से 1970 के बीच, करीब साठ लाख अफ्रीकी अमेरिकियों ने ग्रामीण दक्षिण को छोड़ा और उत्तर, मध्य-पश्चिम और पश्चिम के शहरों में जाकर बस गए — यह अमेरिकी इतिहास में लोगों के सबसे बड़े आंदोलनों में से एक था। कौन गए, वे कहाँ गए, और इसके कारण क्या बदला? नक्शा बनाओ कि लोग, स्थान और बदलाव कैसे जुड़ते हैं।","The rural South to Northern, Midwestern, and Western cities":"ग्रामीण दक्षिण से उत्तरी, मध्य-पश्चिमी और पश्चिमी शहरों तक","Compare your three lenses with a partner. Did you connect the same people to the same places and changes?":"अपने तीन नज़रियों की तुलना किसी साथी से करो। क्या तुमने वही लोग वही स्थानों और बदलावों से जोड़े?","Which change do you think mattered most to families who moved? Why?":"तुम्हें क्या लगता है, प्रवास करने वाले परिवारों के लिए कौन-सा बदलाव सबसे ज़्यादा मायने रखता था? क्यों?","In your own words, explain how people, place, and change connect in the Great Migration. Use at least one detail from each lens and one source.":"अपने शब्दों में समझाओ कि महान प्रवास में लोग, स्थान और बदलाव कैसे जुड़ते हैं। हर नज़रिये से कम से कम एक जानकारी और एक स्रोत का उपयोग करो।","Explain what the Great Migration was and why families made the move.":"समझाओ कि महान प्रवास क्या था और परिवारों ने प्रवास क्यों किया।","Connect a push factor in the South to a change that happened in a Northern city.":"दक्षिण के एक धकेलने वाले कारण को उत्तरी शहर में हुए किसी बदलाव से जोड़ो।","Apply the idea of push and pull factors to a move your own family or community has made.":"धकेलने और खींचने वाले कारणों के विचार को अपने परिवार या समुदाय द्वारा किए गए किसी प्रवास पर लागू करो।","Jacob Lawrence: The Migration Series (The Phillips Collection)":"जैकब लॉरेंस: द माइग्रेशन सीरीज़ (The Migration Series) (The Phillips Collection)","Sixty painted panels (1940–41) telling the story of the Great Migration.":"साठ चित्रित पैनल (1940–41) जो महान प्रवास की कहानी कहते हैं।","What does one panel show about why people moved or what they found?":"एक पैनल यह क्या दिखाता है कि लोग क्यों गए या उन्हें क्या मिला?","How does art help us understand history?":"कला हमें इतिहास समझने में कैसे मदद करती है?","The Great Migration — Classroom Materials (Library of Congress)":"महान प्रवास — कक्षा सामग्री (Library of Congress)","Background and primary sources on one of the largest internal migrations in U.S. history.":"अमेरिकी इतिहास के सबसे बड़े आंतरिक प्रवासों में से एक के बारे में पृष्ठभूमि और प्राथमिक स्रोत।","What were two reasons families chose to move north?":"परिवारों ने उत्तर की ओर जाने का चुनाव किन दो कारणों से किया?","What is one thing that stayed hard even after moving?":"एक ऐसी बात क्या है जो प्रवास के बाद भी कठिन बनी रही?","The Great Migration — African American Heritage (National Archives)":"महान प्रवास — अफ्रीकी अमेरिकी विरासत (National Archives)","Overview of the two waves of the migration and their effects.":"प्रवास की दो लहरों और उनके प्रभावों का अवलोकन।","About how many people moved, and over how many years?":"लगभग कितने लोग गए, और कितने वर्षों में?","How were the two waves connected to the world wars?":"ये दो लहरें विश्व युद्धों से कैसे जुड़ी थीं?","African American families and workers from the rural South — sharecroppers, farm laborers, and their children":"ग्रामीण दक्षिण से अफ्रीकी अमेरिकी परिवार और मज़दूर — बटाईदार किसान, खेत मज़दूर, और उनके बच्चे","Jacob Lawrence — a young Black painter who told the story in his Migration Series":"जैकब लॉरेंस — एक युवा अश्वेत चित्रकार जिसने अपनी माइग्रेशन सीरीज़ (Migration Series) में यह कहानी बताई","Robert S. Abbott — editor of the Chicago Defender, which urged people to move north":"रॉबर्ट एस. एबॉट — शिकागो डिफेंडर (Chicago Defender) के संपादक, जिसने लोगों को उत्तर की ओर जाने के लिए प्रेरित किया","Pullman porters — Black railroad workers who carried news north and south":"पुलमैन पोर्टर — अश्वेत रेलवे कर्मचारी जो उत्तर और दक्षिण के बीच खबरें ले जाते थे","From the South — Mississippi, Alabama, Georgia, Louisiana, and Texas":"दक्षिण से — मिसिसिपी, अलबामा, जॉर्जिया, लुइज़ियाना और टेक्सास","To the North and Midwest — Chicago, Detroit, New York (Harlem), Pittsburgh, Cleveland":"उत्तर और मध्य-पश्चिम की ओर — शिकागो, डेट्रॉइट, न्यूयॉर्क (हार्लेम), पिट्सबर्ग, क्लीवलैंड","To the West (later wave) — Los Angeles, Oakland, Seattle":"पश्चिम की ओर (बाद की लहर) — लॉस एंजिल्स, ओकलैंड, सिएटल","Along the railroads — the rail lines were the highways of the migration":"रेलमार्गों के साथ-साथ — रेल की पटरियाँ ही इस प्रवास के राजमार्ग थीं","Community: big new African American neighborhoods grew in Northern and Western cities":"समुदाय: उत्तरी और पश्चिमी शहरों में बड़े नए अफ्रीकी अमेरिकी मोहल्ले बढ़े","Economy: families moved from farm work to paid factory, steel, and railroad jobs":"अर्थव्यवस्था: परिवार खेती के काम से हटकर कारखानों, इस्पात और रेलवे की वेतन वाली नौकरियों में आ गए","Culture: a burst of art, music, and writing — the Harlem Renaissance, jazz, and blues":"संस्कृति: कला, संगीत और लेखन का एक उभार — हार्लेम पुनर्जागरण, जैज़ और ब्लूज़","Daily life: children attended better-funded schools and adults could vote — but families faced new housing discrimination":"रोज़मर्रा का जीवन: बच्चे बेहतर धन वाले स्कूलों में जाने लगे और बड़े वोट दे सकते थे — पर परिवारों को आवास में नए भेदभाव का सामना करना पड़ा","The nation's map: the Black population shifted from mostly rural-Southern to urban and nationwide":"देश का नक्शा: अश्वेत आबादी ज़्यादातर ग्रामीण-दक्षिणी से बदलकर शहरी और देशभर में फैल गई","When millions of families left Southern farms and rode the railroads to cities like Chicago, Detroit, and New York, they built new communities, took new jobs, and created new music and art — changing both their own lives and the whole country.":"जब लाखों परिवार दक्षिण के खेतों को छोड़कर रेलगाड़ियों से शिकागो, डेट्रॉइट और न्यूयॉर्क जैसे शहरों में पहुँचे, तो उन्होंने नए समुदाय बनाए, नई नौकरियाँ कीं, और नया संगीत और कला रची — और इस तरह अपना जीवन और पूरा देश दोनों बदल दिए।"}},"lewis-clark":{"es":{"The Lewis & Clark Expedition":"La expedición de Lewis y Clark","Put the Corps of Discovery's 1804–1806 journey in order, name the people who made it possible, and ask what it meant for the Native nations along the way.":"Ordena el viaje del Cuerpo de Descubrimiento de 1804–1806, nombra a las personas que lo hicieron posible y pregunta qué significó para las naciones indígenas del camino.","In 1804, President Jefferson sent a team called the Corps of Discovery to explore the huge new land west of the Mississippi River, all the way to the Pacific Ocean. What did they do first, next, and last — and who helped them along the way? Follow the trail and put the journey in order.":"En 1804, el presidente Jefferson envió un equipo llamado el Cuerpo de Descubrimiento a explorar la enorme tierra nueva al oeste del río Misisipi, hasta el océano Pacífico. ¿Qué hicieron primero, después y al final, y quién los ayudó en el camino? Sigue la ruta y ordena el viaje.","Lewis & Clark Expedition":"Expedición de Lewis y Clark","St. Louis to the Pacific Ocean":"De San Luis al océano Pacífico","Compare your trail order with a partner. Did you put the moments in the same sequence? Where did you disagree?":"Compara el orden de tu ruta con el de un compañero. ¿Pusieron los momentos en la misma secuencia? ¿En qué no estuvieron de acuerdo?","Which moment do you think was the most important turning point of the journey? Why?":"¿Cuál momento crees que fue el punto de inflexión más importante del viaje? ¿Por qué?","Tell the story of the expedition in your own words, in order. Use at least three moments from your trail and name at least two people or groups who made the journey possible.":"Cuenta la historia de la expedición con tus propias palabras, en orden. Usa al menos tres momentos de tu ruta y nombra al menos a dos personas o grupos que hicieron posible el viaje.","Explain what the Corps of Discovery set out to do, and whether they succeeded.":"Explica qué se propuso hacer el Cuerpo de Descubrimiento y si lo lograron.","Connect the Louisiana Purchase to why Jefferson wanted this expedition.":"Relaciona la Compra de Luisiana con la razón por la que Jefferson quería esta expedición.","Apply the idea of 'exploring the unknown' to an explorer or scientist today. What do they risk, and who helps them?":"Aplica la idea de 'explorar lo desconocido' a un explorador o científico de hoy. ¿Qué arriesgan y quién los ayuda?","Travel the Lewis & Clark Expedition — Expedition by Date (National Park Service)":"Recorre la expedición de Lewis y Clark: la expedición por fecha (Servicio de Parques Nacionales)","A day-by-day timeline of the journey from the National Park Service.":"Una cronología día a día del viaje, del Servicio de Parques Nacionales.","What are three events in order from the timeline?":"¿Cuáles son tres eventos en orden de la cronología?","How long did the whole journey take?":"¿Cuánto tiempo duró todo el viaje?","Jefferson's Secret Message Regarding the Lewis & Clark Expedition (Library of Congress)":"El mensaje secreto de Jefferson sobre la expedición de Lewis y Clark (Biblioteca del Congreso)","Jefferson's confidential January 1803 message to Congress asking for money to fund the expedition.":"El mensaje confidencial de Jefferson al Congreso, de enero de 1803, pidiendo dinero para financiar la expedición.","Why did Jefferson want to send the expedition west?":"¿Por qué quería Jefferson enviar la expedición hacia el oeste?","What does a 'secret message' tell you about the plan?":"¿Qué te dice un 'mensaje secreto' sobre el plan?","Expedition Timeline (Thomas Jefferson's Monticello)":"Cronología de la expedición (Monticello de Thomas Jefferson)","A timeline and background on the expedition's goals.":"Una cronología e información de contexto sobre los objetivos de la expedición.","What were the expedition's main goals?":"¿Cuáles eran los objetivos principales de la expedición?","Which goal do you think mattered most?":"¿Cuál objetivo crees que fue el más importante?","1804 (May 14) — The Corps sets off up the Missouri River near St. Louis.":"1804 (14 de mayo): el Cuerpo parte río arriba por el Misuri, cerca de San Luis.","1804–1805 (winter) — The Corps builds Fort Mandan; Sacagawea joins the group.":"1804–1805 (invierno): el Cuerpo construye Fort Mandan; Sacagawea se une al grupo.","1805 (summer) — The Corps crosses the Rocky Mountains with Shoshone and Nez Perce help.":"1805 (verano): el Cuerpo cruza las Montañas Rocosas con la ayuda de los shoshone y los nez percé.","1805 (November) — The Corps reaches the Pacific Ocean and builds Fort Clatsop.":"1805 (noviembre): el Cuerpo llega al océano Pacífico y construye Fort Clatsop.","1806 (Sept 23) — The Corps returns safely to St. Louis.":"1806 (23 de septiembre): el Cuerpo regresa a salvo a San Luis.","Meriwether Lewis & William Clark — co-captains":"Meriwether Lewis y William Clark: cocapitanes","Sacagawea (Lemhi Shoshone) — interpreter who helped guide and trade":"Sacagawea (shoshone lemhi): intérprete que ayudó a guiar y a comerciar","York — Clark's enslaved man, a full working member of the Corps":"York: el hombre esclavizado de Clark, miembro pleno y trabajador del Cuerpo","Corps of Discovery — about 45 soldiers and explorers":"Cuerpo de Descubrimiento: unos 45 soldados y exploradores","Mandan, Hidatsa, Shoshone & Nez Perce nations — hosts who gave food, directions, and horses":"Las naciones mandan, hidatsa, shoshone y nez percé: anfitriones que dieron comida, indicaciones y caballos","The journey mapped a huge new part of the country, recorded hundreds of plants, animals, and Native nations, and opened the West to more American travel and settlement.":"El viaje cartografió una enorme parte nueva del país, registró cientos de plantas, animales y naciones indígenas, y abrió el Oeste a más viajes y asentamientos estadounidenses.","How did the Native nations along the trail feel about the strangers crossing their homelands — and what happened to those nations afterward?":"¿Cómo se sintieron las naciones indígenas del camino ante los extraños que cruzaban sus tierras natales, y qué les pasó a esas naciones después?"},"vi":{"The Lewis & Clark Expedition":"Cuộc thám hiểm của Lewis và Clark","Put the Corps of Discovery's 1804–1806 journey in order, name the people who made it possible, and ask what it meant for the Native nations along the way.":"Sắp xếp hành trình năm 1804–1806 của Đoàn Thám hiểm theo đúng thứ tự, nêu tên những người đã giúp hành trình thành hiện thực, và tự hỏi điều đó có ý nghĩa gì đối với các dân tộc bản địa dọc đường đi.","In 1804, President Jefferson sent a team called the Corps of Discovery to explore the huge new land west of the Mississippi River, all the way to the Pacific Ocean. What did they do first, next, and last — and who helped them along the way? Follow the trail and put the journey in order.":"Năm 1804, Tổng thống Jefferson đã cử một nhóm gọi là Đoàn Thám hiểm đi khám phá vùng đất mới rộng lớn ở phía tây sông Mississippi, đến tận Thái Bình Dương. Họ đã làm gì trước, tiếp theo, và cuối cùng — và ai đã giúp họ dọc đường? Hãy đi theo con đường và sắp xếp hành trình theo thứ tự.","Lewis & Clark Expedition":"Cuộc thám hiểm Lewis và Clark","St. Louis to the Pacific Ocean":"Từ St. Louis đến Thái Bình Dương","Compare your trail order with a partner. Did you put the moments in the same sequence? Where did you disagree?":"So sánh thứ tự con đường của em với một bạn. Các em có xếp các khoảnh khắc theo cùng một trình tự không? Các em không đồng ý ở chỗ nào?","Which moment do you think was the most important turning point of the journey? Why?":"Em nghĩ khoảnh khắc nào là bước ngoặt quan trọng nhất của hành trình? Vì sao?","Tell the story of the expedition in your own words, in order. Use at least three moments from your trail and name at least two people or groups who made the journey possible.":"Kể lại câu chuyện của cuộc thám hiểm bằng lời của chính em, theo thứ tự. Dùng ít nhất ba khoảnh khắc từ con đường của em và nêu tên ít nhất hai người hoặc nhóm đã giúp hành trình thành hiện thực.","Explain what the Corps of Discovery set out to do, and whether they succeeded.":"Giải thích Đoàn Thám hiểm đã đặt ra mục tiêu làm gì, và họ có thành công hay không.","Connect the Louisiana Purchase to why Jefferson wanted this expedition.":"Hãy nối việc Mua Louisiana với lý do vì sao Jefferson muốn có cuộc thám hiểm này.","Apply the idea of 'exploring the unknown' to an explorer or scientist today. What do they risk, and who helps them?":"Hãy áp dụng ý tưởng 'khám phá điều chưa biết' cho một nhà thám hiểm hoặc nhà khoa học ngày nay. Họ mạo hiểm điều gì, và ai giúp họ?","Travel the Lewis & Clark Expedition — Expedition by Date (National Park Service)":"Đi theo cuộc thám hiểm Lewis và Clark — Hành trình theo ngày tháng (Cục Công viên Quốc gia)","A day-by-day timeline of the journey from the National Park Service.":"Một dòng thời gian từng ngày của hành trình từ Cục Công viên Quốc gia.","What are three events in order from the timeline?":"Ba sự kiện theo thứ tự trong dòng thời gian là gì?","How long did the whole journey take?":"Cả hành trình mất bao lâu?","Jefferson's Secret Message Regarding the Lewis & Clark Expedition (Library of Congress)":"Thông điệp bí mật của Jefferson về cuộc thám hiểm Lewis và Clark (Thư viện Quốc hội)","Jefferson's confidential January 1803 message to Congress asking for money to fund the expedition.":"Thông điệp mật của Jefferson gửi Quốc hội vào tháng 1 năm 1803, xin tiền để tài trợ cho cuộc thám hiểm.","Why did Jefferson want to send the expedition west?":"Vì sao Jefferson muốn cử cuộc thám hiểm đi về phía tây?","What does a 'secret message' tell you about the plan?":"Một 'thông điệp bí mật' cho em biết điều gì về kế hoạch?","Expedition Timeline (Thomas Jefferson's Monticello)":"Dòng thời gian của cuộc thám hiểm (Monticello của Thomas Jefferson)","A timeline and background on the expedition's goals.":"Một dòng thời gian và bối cảnh về các mục tiêu của cuộc thám hiểm.","What were the expedition's main goals?":"Các mục tiêu chính của cuộc thám hiểm là gì?","Which goal do you think mattered most?":"Em nghĩ mục tiêu nào quan trọng nhất?","1804 (May 14) — The Corps sets off up the Missouri River near St. Louis.":"1804 (14 tháng 5) — Đoàn xuất phát ngược dòng sông Missouri gần St. Louis.","1804–1805 (winter) — The Corps builds Fort Mandan; Sacagawea joins the group.":"1804–1805 (mùa đông) — Đoàn xây Pháo đài Mandan; Sacagawea gia nhập nhóm.","1805 (summer) — The Corps crosses the Rocky Mountains with Shoshone and Nez Perce help.":"1805 (mùa hè) — Đoàn vượt qua Dãy núi Rocky với sự giúp đỡ của người Shoshone và người Nez Perce.","1805 (November) — The Corps reaches the Pacific Ocean and builds Fort Clatsop.":"1805 (tháng 11) — Đoàn đến Thái Bình Dương và xây Pháo đài Clatsop.","1806 (Sept 23) — The Corps returns safely to St. Louis.":"1806 (23 tháng 9) — Đoàn trở về St. Louis an toàn.","Meriwether Lewis & William Clark — co-captains":"Meriwether Lewis và William Clark — đồng đội trưởng","Sacagawea (Lemhi Shoshone) — interpreter who helped guide and trade":"Sacagawea (người Lemhi Shoshone) — thông dịch viên đã giúp dẫn đường và trao đổi buôn bán","York — Clark's enslaved man, a full working member of the Corps":"York — người bị Clark nô dịch, một thành viên làm việc trọn vẹn của Đoàn","Corps of Discovery — about 45 soldiers and explorers":"Đoàn Thám hiểm — khoảng 45 người lính và nhà thám hiểm","Mandan, Hidatsa, Shoshone & Nez Perce nations — hosts who gave food, directions, and horses":"Các dân tộc Mandan, Hidatsa, Shoshone và Nez Perce — những chủ nhà đã cho lương thực, chỉ đường và ngựa","The journey mapped a huge new part of the country, recorded hundreds of plants, animals, and Native nations, and opened the West to more American travel and settlement.":"Hành trình đã lập bản đồ một phần đất mới rộng lớn của đất nước, ghi chép hàng trăm loài cây, loài vật và các dân tộc bản địa, và mở đường cho người Mỹ đi lại và định cư nhiều hơn ở miền Tây.","How did the Native nations along the trail feel about the strangers crossing their homelands — and what happened to those nations afterward?":"Các dân tộc bản địa dọc con đường cảm thấy thế nào về những người lạ băng qua quê hương của họ — và sau đó chuyện gì đã xảy ra với những dân tộc ấy?"},"ar":{"The Lewis & Clark Expedition":"رحلة لويس وكلارك الاستكشافية","Put the Corps of Discovery's 1804–1806 journey in order, name the people who made it possible, and ask what it meant for the Native nations along the way.":"رتّب رحلة فيلق الاستكشاف بين عامي 1804 و1806 حسب تسلسلها، وسمِّ الأشخاص الذين جعلوها ممكنة، واسأل ماذا كانت تعني للأمم الأصلية على طول الطريق.","In 1804, President Jefferson sent a team called the Corps of Discovery to explore the huge new land west of the Mississippi River, all the way to the Pacific Ocean. What did they do first, next, and last — and who helped them along the way? Follow the trail and put the journey in order.":"في عام 1804، أرسل الرئيس جيفرسون فريقًا يُدعى فيلق الاستكشاف لاستكشاف الأرض الجديدة الشاسعة غرب نهر الميسيسيبي، حتى المحيط الهادئ. ماذا فعلوا أولًا، ثم ماذا، وماذا في النهاية — ومن ساعدهم على طول الطريق؟ اتبع المسار ورتّب الرحلة حسب تسلسلها.","Lewis & Clark Expedition":"رحلة لويس وكلارك الاستكشافية","St. Louis to the Pacific Ocean":"من سانت لويس إلى المحيط الهادئ","Compare your trail order with a partner. Did you put the moments in the same sequence? Where did you disagree?":"قارن ترتيب مسارك مع زميل لك. هل رتّبتما اللحظات بالتسلسل نفسه؟ في أي نقطة اختلفتما؟","Which moment do you think was the most important turning point of the journey? Why?":"ما اللحظة التي تعتقد أنها كانت أهم نقطة تحوّل في الرحلة؟ ولماذا؟","Tell the story of the expedition in your own words, in order. Use at least three moments from your trail and name at least two people or groups who made the journey possible.":"احكِ قصة الرحلة بأسلوبك الخاص، حسب تسلسلها. استخدم ثلاث لحظات على الأقل من مسارك، وسمِّ شخصين أو مجموعتين على الأقل جعلوا الرحلة ممكنة.","Explain what the Corps of Discovery set out to do, and whether they succeeded.":"اشرح ما الذي انطلق فيلق الاستكشاف لتحقيقه، وهل نجحوا في ذلك.","Connect the Louisiana Purchase to why Jefferson wanted this expedition.":"اربط بين صفقة شراء لويزيانا وسبب رغبة جيفرسون في هذه الرحلة.","Apply the idea of 'exploring the unknown' to an explorer or scientist today. What do they risk, and who helps them?":"طبّق فكرة \"استكشاف المجهول\" على مستكشف أو عالِم في وقتنا الحاضر. ما الذي يخاطرون به، ومن يساعدهم؟","Travel the Lewis & Clark Expedition — Expedition by Date (National Park Service)":"تتبّع رحلة لويس وكلارك الاستكشافية — الرحلة حسب التاريخ (هيئة الحدائق الوطنية)","A day-by-day timeline of the journey from the National Park Service.":"خط زمني يومًا بيوم للرحلة من هيئة الحدائق الوطنية.","What are three events in order from the timeline?":"ما هي ثلاثة أحداث بالترتيب من الخط الزمني؟","How long did the whole journey take?":"كم استغرقت الرحلة بأكملها؟","Jefferson's Secret Message Regarding the Lewis & Clark Expedition (Library of Congress)":"رسالة جيفرسون السرية بشأن رحلة لويس وكلارك الاستكشافية (مكتبة الكونغرس)","Jefferson's confidential January 1803 message to Congress asking for money to fund the expedition.":"رسالة جيفرسون السرية إلى الكونغرس في يناير 1803 يطلب فيها المال لتمويل الرحلة.","Why did Jefferson want to send the expedition west?":"لماذا أراد جيفرسون إرسال الرحلة نحو الغرب؟","What does a 'secret message' tell you about the plan?":"ماذا تخبرك \"الرسالة السرية\" عن الخطة؟","Expedition Timeline (Thomas Jefferson's Monticello)":"الخط الزمني للرحلة (مونتيسيلو توماس جيفرسون)","A timeline and background on the expedition's goals.":"خط زمني ومعلومات خلفية عن أهداف الرحلة.","What were the expedition's main goals?":"ما هي الأهداف الرئيسية للرحلة؟","Which goal do you think mattered most?":"أي هدف تعتقد أنه كان الأهم؟","1804 (May 14) — The Corps sets off up the Missouri River near St. Louis.":"1804 (14 مايو) — ينطلق الفيلق صعودًا في نهر ميزوري قرب سانت لويس.","1804–1805 (winter) — The Corps builds Fort Mandan; Sacagawea joins the group.":"1804–1805 (الشتاء) — يبني الفيلق حصن ماندان؛ وتنضم ساكاجاويا إلى المجموعة.","1805 (summer) — The Corps crosses the Rocky Mountains with Shoshone and Nez Perce help.":"1805 (الصيف) — يعبر الفيلق جبال روكي بمساعدة قبيلتي الشوشون والنيز بيرسيه.","1805 (November) — The Corps reaches the Pacific Ocean and builds Fort Clatsop.":"1805 (نوفمبر) — يصل الفيلق إلى المحيط الهادئ ويبني حصن كلاتسوب.","1806 (Sept 23) — The Corps returns safely to St. Louis.":"1806 (23 سبتمبر) — يعود الفيلق بأمان إلى سانت لويس.","Meriwether Lewis & William Clark — co-captains":"ميريويذر لويس ووليام كلارك — قائدان مشاركان","Sacagawea (Lemhi Shoshone) — interpreter who helped guide and trade":"ساكاجاويا (من قبيلة ليمهي شوشون) — مترجمة ساعدت في الإرشاد والتبادل التجاري","York — Clark's enslaved man, a full working member of the Corps":"يورك — الرجل المستعبَد لدى كلارك، عضو عامل كامل في الفيلق","Corps of Discovery — about 45 soldiers and explorers":"فيلق الاستكشاف — نحو 45 جنديًا ومستكشفًا","Mandan, Hidatsa, Shoshone & Nez Perce nations — hosts who gave food, directions, and horses":"أمم ماندان وهيداتسا وشوشون ونيز بيرسيه — مضيفون قدّموا الطعام والإرشادات والخيول","The journey mapped a huge new part of the country, recorded hundreds of plants, animals, and Native nations, and opened the West to more American travel and settlement.":"رسمت الرحلة خرائط لجزء جديد شاسع من البلاد، وسجّلت مئات النباتات والحيوانات والأمم الأصلية، وفتحت الغرب أمام مزيد من التنقّل والاستيطان الأمريكي.","How did the Native nations along the trail feel about the strangers crossing their homelands — and what happened to those nations afterward?":"كيف شعرت الأمم الأصلية على طول المسار تجاه الغرباء الذين عبروا أراضي أوطانهم — وماذا حدث لتلك الأمم بعد ذلك؟"},"zh":{"The Lewis & Clark Expedition":"刘易斯与克拉克远征","Put the Corps of Discovery's 1804–1806 journey in order, name the people who made it possible, and ask what it meant for the Native nations along the way.":"把探索队 1804–1806 年的旅程按顺序排好，说出让这次旅程得以成行的人，并思考它对沿途的原住民各族意味着什么。","In 1804, President Jefferson sent a team called the Corps of Discovery to explore the huge new land west of the Mississippi River, all the way to the Pacific Ocean. What did they do first, next, and last — and who helped them along the way? Follow the trail and put the journey in order.":"1804 年，杰斐逊总统派出一支叫作探索队的队伍，去勘察密西西比河以西那片辽阔的新土地，一直到太平洋。他们最先做了什么、接着做了什么、最后又做了什么——一路上又是谁帮助了他们？沿着路线走，把这段旅程按顺序排好。","Lewis & Clark Expedition":"刘易斯与克拉克远征","St. Louis to the Pacific Ocean":"从圣路易斯到太平洋","Compare your trail order with a partner. Did you put the moments in the same sequence? Where did you disagree?":"把你排的路线顺序和同伴比一比。你们把这些时刻排成同样的顺序了吗？你们在哪里有分歧？","Which moment do you think was the most important turning point of the journey? Why?":"你觉得哪个时刻是这段旅程中最重要的转折点？为什么？","Tell the story of the expedition in your own words, in order. Use at least three moments from your trail and name at least two people or groups who made the journey possible.":"用你自己的话，按顺序讲一讲这次远征的故事。至少用上你路线中的三个时刻，并说出至少两位让这次旅程得以成行的人物或群体。","Explain what the Corps of Discovery set out to do, and whether they succeeded.":"说明探索队出发时打算做什么，以及他们是否成功了。","Connect the Louisiana Purchase to why Jefferson wanted this expedition.":"把路易斯安那购地案和杰斐逊为什么想要这次远征联系起来。","Apply the idea of 'exploring the unknown' to an explorer or scientist today. What do they risk, and who helps them?":"把「探索未知」的想法用到今天的一位探险家或科学家身上。他们冒着什么风险，又是谁在帮助他们？","Travel the Lewis & Clark Expedition — Expedition by Date (National Park Service)":"跟随刘易斯与克拉克远征——按日期看行程（美国国家公园管理局）","A day-by-day timeline of the journey from the National Park Service.":"美国国家公园管理局提供的旅程逐日时间线。","What are three events in order from the timeline?":"从时间线中按顺序找出三个事件是哪些？","How long did the whole journey take?":"整段旅程一共花了多长时间？","Jefferson's Secret Message Regarding the Lewis & Clark Expedition (Library of Congress)":"杰斐逊有关刘易斯与克拉克远征的密函（美国国会图书馆）","Jefferson's confidential January 1803 message to Congress asking for money to fund the expedition.":"杰斐逊 1803 年 1 月写给国会的密函，请求拨款资助这次远征。","Why did Jefferson want to send the expedition west?":"杰斐逊为什么想把远征队派往西部？","What does a 'secret message' tell you about the plan?":"一封「密函」让你对这个计划了解到什么？","Expedition Timeline (Thomas Jefferson's Monticello)":"远征时间线（托马斯·杰斐逊的蒙蒂塞洛庄园）","A timeline and background on the expedition's goals.":"关于远征目标的时间线和背景介绍。","What were the expedition's main goals?":"这次远征的主要目标是什么？","Which goal do you think mattered most?":"你觉得哪个目标最重要？","1804 (May 14) — The Corps sets off up the Missouri River near St. Louis.":"1804 年（5 月 14 日）——探索队从圣路易斯附近出发，逆密苏里河而上。","1804–1805 (winter) — The Corps builds Fort Mandan; Sacagawea joins the group.":"1804–1805 年（冬季）——探索队修建曼丹堡；萨卡加维亚加入队伍。","1805 (summer) — The Corps crosses the Rocky Mountains with Shoshone and Nez Perce help.":"1805 年（夏季）——探索队在肖肖尼族和内兹佩尔塞族的帮助下翻越落基山脉。","1805 (November) — The Corps reaches the Pacific Ocean and builds Fort Clatsop.":"1805 年（11 月）——探索队抵达太平洋，并修建克拉特索普堡。","1806 (Sept 23) — The Corps returns safely to St. Louis.":"1806 年（9 月 23 日）——探索队平安返回圣路易斯。","Meriwether Lewis & William Clark — co-captains":"梅里韦瑟·刘易斯与威廉·克拉克——共同队长","Sacagawea (Lemhi Shoshone) — interpreter who helped guide and trade":"萨卡加维亚（莱姆希·肖肖尼族）——帮助带路和交易的翻译","York — Clark's enslaved man, a full working member of the Corps":"约克——克拉克的奴隶，探索队中一名尽职尽责的正式成员","Corps of Discovery — about 45 soldiers and explorers":"探索队——约 45 名士兵和探险者","Mandan, Hidatsa, Shoshone & Nez Perce nations — hosts who gave food, directions, and horses":"曼丹族、希达察族、肖肖尼族和内兹佩尔塞族——提供食物、路线指引和马匹的东道主","The journey mapped a huge new part of the country, recorded hundreds of plants, animals, and Native nations, and opened the West to more American travel and settlement.":"这段旅程为这个国家一大片新地区绘制了地图，记录了数百种植物、动物和原住民各族，并让更多美国人得以前往西部旅行和定居。","How did the Native nations along the trail feel about the strangers crossing their homelands — and what happened to those nations afterward?":"沿途的原住民各族对这些穿过他们家园的陌生人有什么感受——之后这些族群又遭遇了什么？"},"ur":{"The Lewis & Clark Expedition":"لیوس اور کلارک کی مہم","Put the Corps of Discovery's 1804–1806 journey in order, name the people who made it possible, and ask what it meant for the Native nations along the way.":"ڈسکوری کور کے 1804ء تا 1806ء سفر کو ترتیب سے لگائیں، اُن لوگوں کے نام بتائیں جنہوں نے اِسے ممکن بنایا، اور سوچیں کہ راستے میں بسنے والی مقامی قوموں کے لیے اِس کا کیا مطلب تھا۔","In 1804, President Jefferson sent a team called the Corps of Discovery to explore the huge new land west of the Mississippi River, all the way to the Pacific Ocean. What did they do first, next, and last — and who helped them along the way? Follow the trail and put the journey in order.":"1804ء میں صدر جیفرسن نے ڈسکوری کور نامی ایک ٹیم بھیجی تاکہ وہ دریائے مسیسیپی کے مغرب میں پھیلی ہوئی بڑی نئی زمین کو، بحرِ اوقیانوس تک، دریافت کرے۔ اُنہوں نے پہلے کیا کیا، پھر کیا، اور آخر میں کیا — اور راستے میں کن لوگوں نے اُن کی مدد کی؟ راستے کی پیروی کریں اور سفر کو ترتیب سے لگائیں۔","Lewis & Clark Expedition":"لیوس اور کلارک کی مہم","St. Louis to the Pacific Ocean":"سینٹ لوئس سے بحرِ اوقیانوس تک","Compare your trail order with a partner. Did you put the moments in the same sequence? Where did you disagree?":"اپنے راستے کی ترتیب کا موازنہ کسی ساتھی کے ساتھ کریں۔ کیا آپ دونوں نے واقعات کو ایک ہی ترتیب میں رکھا؟ آپ کہاں اختلاف رکھتے تھے؟","Which moment do you think was the most important turning point of the journey? Why?":"آپ کے خیال میں کون سا لمحہ سفر کا سب سے اہم موڑ تھا؟ کیوں؟","Tell the story of the expedition in your own words, in order. Use at least three moments from your trail and name at least two people or groups who made the journey possible.":"مہم کی کہانی اپنے الفاظ میں، ترتیب سے سنائیں۔ اپنے راستے میں سے کم از کم تین لمحے استعمال کریں اور کم از کم دو ایسے لوگوں یا گروہوں کے نام بتائیں جنہوں نے سفر کو ممکن بنایا۔","Explain what the Corps of Discovery set out to do, and whether they succeeded.":"بتائیں کہ ڈسکوری کور نے کیا کرنے کا ارادہ کیا تھا، اور کیا وہ کامیاب ہوئے۔","Connect the Louisiana Purchase to why Jefferson wanted this expedition.":"لوزیانا کی خریداری کو اِس بات سے جوڑیں کہ جیفرسن یہ مہم کیوں چاہتے تھے۔","Apply the idea of 'exploring the unknown' to an explorer or scientist today. What do they risk, and who helps them?":"'نامعلوم کو دریافت کرنے' کے خیال کو آج کے کسی مہم جو یا سائنسدان پر لاگو کریں۔ وہ کیا خطرہ مول لیتے ہیں، اور کون اُن کی مدد کرتا ہے؟","Travel the Lewis & Clark Expedition — Expedition by Date (National Park Service)":"لیوس اور کلارک کی مہم کا سفر کریں — تاریخ کے حساب سے مہم (نیشنل پارک سروس)","A day-by-day timeline of the journey from the National Park Service.":"نیشنل پارک سروس کی جانب سے سفر کی دن بہ دن ٹائم لائن۔","What are three events in order from the timeline?":"ٹائم لائن میں سے ترتیب کے مطابق تین واقعات کون سے ہیں؟","How long did the whole journey take?":"پورا سفر کتنا وقت لگا؟","Jefferson's Secret Message Regarding the Lewis & Clark Expedition (Library of Congress)":"لیوس اور کلارک کی مہم کے بارے میں جیفرسن کا خفیہ پیغام (لائبریری آف کانگریس)","Jefferson's confidential January 1803 message to Congress asking for money to fund the expedition.":"جنوری 1803ء میں جیفرسن کا کانگریس کے نام خفیہ پیغام جس میں مہم کے لیے رقم کی درخواست کی گئی۔","Why did Jefferson want to send the expedition west?":"جیفرسن مہم کو مغرب کی طرف کیوں بھیجنا چاہتے تھے؟","What does a 'secret message' tell you about the plan?":"ایک 'خفیہ پیغام' آپ کو منصوبے کے بارے میں کیا بتاتا ہے؟","Expedition Timeline (Thomas Jefferson's Monticello)":"مہم کی ٹائم لائن (تھامس جیفرسن کا مونٹیسیلو)","A timeline and background on the expedition's goals.":"مہم کے مقاصد کے بارے میں ایک ٹائم لائن اور پس منظر۔","What were the expedition's main goals?":"مہم کے بنیادی مقاصد کیا تھے؟","Which goal do you think mattered most?":"آپ کے خیال میں کون سا مقصد سب سے اہم تھا؟","1804 (May 14) — The Corps sets off up the Missouri River near St. Louis.":"1804ء (14 مئی) — کور سینٹ لوئس کے قریب دریائے مسوری کے اوپر کی جانب روانہ ہوتا ہے۔","1804–1805 (winter) — The Corps builds Fort Mandan; Sacagawea joins the group.":"1804ء–1805ء (سردیاں) — کور فورٹ منڈن تعمیر کرتا ہے؛ ساکا جاویا گروہ میں شامل ہوتی ہے۔","1805 (summer) — The Corps crosses the Rocky Mountains with Shoshone and Nez Perce help.":"1805ء (گرمیاں) — کور شوشونی اور نیز پرس قوموں کی مدد سے راکی پہاڑوں کو عبور کرتا ہے۔","1805 (November) — The Corps reaches the Pacific Ocean and builds Fort Clatsop.":"1805ء (نومبر) — کور بحرِ اوقیانوس تک پہنچتا ہے اور فورٹ کلاٹسوپ تعمیر کرتا ہے۔","1806 (Sept 23) — The Corps returns safely to St. Louis.":"1806ء (23 ستمبر) — کور بحفاظت سینٹ لوئس واپس آ جاتا ہے۔","Meriwether Lewis & William Clark — co-captains":"میری ویدر لیوس اور ولیم کلارک — مشترکہ کپتان","Sacagawea (Lemhi Shoshone) — interpreter who helped guide and trade":"ساکا جاویا (لیمھی شوشونی) — مترجم جس نے راہنمائی اور تجارت میں مدد کی","York — Clark's enslaved man, a full working member of the Corps":"یارک — کلارک کا غلام، جو کور کا مکمل کام کرنے والا رکن تھا","Corps of Discovery — about 45 soldiers and explorers":"ڈسکوری کور — تقریباً 45 سپاہی اور مہم جو","Mandan, Hidatsa, Shoshone & Nez Perce nations — hosts who gave food, directions, and horses":"منڈن، ہیڈاٹسا، شوشونی اور نیز پرس قومیں — میزبان جنہوں نے کھانا، راستے کی راہنمائی اور گھوڑے دیے","The journey mapped a huge new part of the country, recorded hundreds of plants, animals, and Native nations, and opened the West to more American travel and settlement.":"اِس سفر نے ملک کے ایک بہت بڑے نئے حصے کا نقشہ بنایا، سینکڑوں پودوں، جانوروں اور مقامی قوموں کو ریکارڈ کیا، اور مغرب کو مزید امریکی سفر اور آبادکاری کے لیے کھول دیا۔","How did the Native nations along the trail feel about the strangers crossing their homelands — and what happened to those nations afterward?":"راستے میں بسنے والی مقامی قوموں نے اپنے وطن سے گزرنے والے اجنبیوں کے بارے میں کیا محسوس کیا — اور بعد میں اُن قوموں کے ساتھ کیا ہوا؟"},"hi":{"The Lewis & Clark Expedition":"लुईस और क्लार्क अभियान","Put the Corps of Discovery's 1804–1806 journey in order, name the people who made it possible, and ask what it meant for the Native nations along the way.":"डिस्कवरी दल की 1804–1806 की यात्रा को क्रम में लगाएँ, उन लोगों के नाम बताएँ जिन्होंने इसे संभव बनाया, और सोचें कि रास्ते में बसने वाले मूल-निवासी राष्ट्रों के लिए इसका क्या मतलब था।","In 1804, President Jefferson sent a team called the Corps of Discovery to explore the huge new land west of the Mississippi River, all the way to the Pacific Ocean. What did they do first, next, and last — and who helped them along the way? Follow the trail and put the journey in order.":"1804 में, राष्ट्रपति जेफ़रसन ने डिस्कवरी दल नामक एक टीम भेजी ताकि वह मिसिसिपी नदी के पश्चिम की विशाल नई भूमि की, प्रशांत महासागर तक, खोज कर सके। उन्होंने पहले क्या किया, फिर क्या, और आख़िर में क्या — और रास्ते में किसने उनकी मदद की? रास्ते का अनुसरण करें और यात्रा को क्रम में लगाएँ।","Lewis & Clark Expedition":"लुईस और क्लार्क अभियान","St. Louis to the Pacific Ocean":"सेंट लुइस से प्रशांत महासागर तक","Compare your trail order with a partner. Did you put the moments in the same sequence? Where did you disagree?":"अपने रास्ते के क्रम की तुलना किसी साथी के साथ करें। क्या आप दोनों ने पलों को एक ही क्रम में रखा? आप कहाँ असहमत थे?","Which moment do you think was the most important turning point of the journey? Why?":"आपको क्या लगता है कि यात्रा का सबसे महत्वपूर्ण मोड़ कौन-सा पल था? क्यों?","Tell the story of the expedition in your own words, in order. Use at least three moments from your trail and name at least two people or groups who made the journey possible.":"अभियान की कहानी अपने शब्दों में, क्रम से सुनाएँ। अपने रास्ते के कम से कम तीन पलों का उपयोग करें और कम से कम दो ऐसे लोगों या समूहों के नाम बताएँ जिन्होंने यात्रा को संभव बनाया।","Explain what the Corps of Discovery set out to do, and whether they succeeded.":"बताएँ कि डिस्कवरी दल ने क्या करने का इरादा किया था, और क्या वे सफल हुए।","Connect the Louisiana Purchase to why Jefferson wanted this expedition.":"लुइज़ियाना ख़रीद को इस बात से जोड़ें कि जेफ़रसन यह अभियान क्यों चाहते थे।","Apply the idea of 'exploring the unknown' to an explorer or scientist today. What do they risk, and who helps them?":"'अनजान की खोज' के विचार को आज के किसी खोजकर्ता या वैज्ञानिक पर लागू करें। वे किस बात का जोखिम उठाते हैं, और कौन उनकी मदद करता है?","Travel the Lewis & Clark Expedition — Expedition by Date (National Park Service)":"लुईस और क्लार्क अभियान की यात्रा करें — तारीख़ के अनुसार अभियान (नेशनल पार्क सर्विस)","A day-by-day timeline of the journey from the National Park Service.":"नेशनल पार्क सर्विस की ओर से यात्रा की दिन-प्रतिदिन की समय-रेखा।","What are three events in order from the timeline?":"समय-रेखा में से क्रम में तीन घटनाएँ कौन-सी हैं?","How long did the whole journey take?":"पूरी यात्रा में कितना समय लगा?","Jefferson's Secret Message Regarding the Lewis & Clark Expedition (Library of Congress)":"लुईस और क्लार्क अभियान के बारे में जेफ़रसन का गुप्त संदेश (लाइब्रेरी ऑफ़ कांग्रेस)","Jefferson's confidential January 1803 message to Congress asking for money to fund the expedition.":"जनवरी 1803 में जेफ़रसन का कांग्रेस के नाम गोपनीय संदेश जिसमें अभियान के लिए धन माँगा गया।","Why did Jefferson want to send the expedition west?":"जेफ़रसन अभियान को पश्चिम की ओर क्यों भेजना चाहते थे?","What does a 'secret message' tell you about the plan?":"एक 'गुप्त संदेश' आपको योजना के बारे में क्या बताता है?","Expedition Timeline (Thomas Jefferson's Monticello)":"अभियान की समय-रेखा (थॉमस जेफ़रसन का मॉन्टिसेलो)","A timeline and background on the expedition's goals.":"अभियान के लक्ष्यों के बारे में एक समय-रेखा और पृष्ठभूमि।","What were the expedition's main goals?":"अभियान के मुख्य लक्ष्य क्या थे?","Which goal do you think mattered most?":"आपको क्या लगता है कि कौन-सा लक्ष्य सबसे महत्वपूर्ण था?","1804 (May 14) — The Corps sets off up the Missouri River near St. Louis.":"1804 (14 मई) — दल सेंट लुइस के पास मिसौरी नदी में ऊपर की ओर रवाना होता है।","1804–1805 (winter) — The Corps builds Fort Mandan; Sacagawea joins the group.":"1804–1805 (सर्दी) — दल फ़ोर्ट मैंडन बनाता है; सैकागावीआ समूह में शामिल होती है।","1805 (summer) — The Corps crosses the Rocky Mountains with Shoshone and Nez Perce help.":"1805 (गर्मी) — दल शोशोनी और नेज़ पर्स लोगों की मदद से रॉकी पर्वत पार करता है।","1805 (November) — The Corps reaches the Pacific Ocean and builds Fort Clatsop.":"1805 (नवंबर) — दल प्रशांत महासागर तक पहुँचता है और फ़ोर्ट क्लैटसॉप बनाता है।","1806 (Sept 23) — The Corps returns safely to St. Louis.":"1806 (23 सितंबर) — दल सुरक्षित रूप से सेंट लुइस लौट आता है।","Meriwether Lewis & William Clark — co-captains":"मेरिवेदर लुईस और विलियम क्लार्क — सह-कप्तान","Sacagawea (Lemhi Shoshone) — interpreter who helped guide and trade":"सैकागावीआ (लेम्ही शोशोनी) — दुभाषिया जिसने रास्ता दिखाने और व्यापार में मदद की","York — Clark's enslaved man, a full working member of the Corps":"यॉर्क — क्लार्क का ग़ुलाम बनाया गया व्यक्ति, दल का पूरी तरह काम करने वाला सदस्य","Corps of Discovery — about 45 soldiers and explorers":"डिस्कवरी दल — लगभग 45 सैनिक और खोजकर्ता","Mandan, Hidatsa, Shoshone & Nez Perce nations — hosts who gave food, directions, and horses":"मैंडन, हिडात्सा, शोशोनी और नेज़ पर्स राष्ट्र — मेज़बान जिन्होंने भोजन, रास्ता और घोड़े दिए","The journey mapped a huge new part of the country, recorded hundreds of plants, animals, and Native nations, and opened the West to more American travel and settlement.":"इस यात्रा ने देश के एक विशाल नए हिस्से का नक़्शा बनाया, सैकड़ों पौधों, जानवरों और मूल-निवासी राष्ट्रों को दर्ज किया, और पश्चिम को अधिक अमेरिकी यात्रा और बसाव के लिए खोल दिया।","How did the Native nations along the trail feel about the strangers crossing their homelands — and what happened to those nations afterward?":"रास्ते में बसने वाले मूल-निवासी राष्ट्रों ने अपनी मातृभूमि से गुज़रने वाले अजनबियों के बारे में कैसा महसूस किया — और बाद में उन राष्ट्रों के साथ क्या हुआ?"}},"road-to-civil-war":{"es":{"The Road to the Civil War":"El camino hacia la Guerra Civil","Follow the chain of conflicts over slavery's expansion from 1850 to 1861 and decide which link did the most to make war unavoidable.":"Sigue la cadena de conflictos sobre la expansión de la esclavitud desde 1850 hasta 1861 y decide qué eslabón contribuyó más a hacer inevitable la guerra.","The Civil War did not begin with a single event. Through the 1850s, a chain of conflicts over whether slavery could expand into the western territories pushed the nation toward war — each action producing a sharper reaction. Trace the chain from pressure to consequence, and decide which link mattered most.":"La Guerra Civil no comenzó con un solo acontecimiento. A lo largo de la década de 1850, una cadena de conflictos sobre si la esclavitud podía expandirse a los territorios del oeste empujó a la nación hacia la guerra, cada acción provocando una reacción más aguda. Traza la cadena desde la presión hasta la consecuencia y decide qué eslabón importó más.","Secession and Fort Sumter":"La secesión y Fort Sumter","The United States":"Los Estados Unidos","Compare your chains with a partner. Did you order the links the same way?":"Compara tus cadenas con las de un compañero. ¿Ordenaron los eslabones de la misma manera?","Did you choose the same 'most important link'? Defend your choice with evidence.":"¿Eligieron el mismo 'eslabón más importante'? Defiende tu elección con evidencia.","Which link in the chain did the most to make war unavoidable? Support your claim with evidence from at least two sources and two links.":"¿Qué eslabón de la cadena contribuyó más a hacer inevitable la guerra? Respalda tu afirmación con evidencia de al menos dos fuentes y dos eslabones.","Explain how one action in the chain produced a sharper reaction.":"Explica cómo una acción de la cadena provocó una reacción más aguda.","Connect the Kansas–Nebraska Act to the violence of 'Bleeding Kansas.'":"Relaciona la Ley Kansas–Nebraska con la violencia de 'Bleeding Kansas' (el Kansas sangrante).","Apply the idea of an escalating chain of conflict to another dispute in history or the world today.":"Aplica la idea de una cadena de conflicto que se intensifica a otra disputa de la historia o del mundo actual.","Dred Scott v. Sandford (1857) — National Archives":"Dred Scott contra Sandford (1857) — Archivos Nacionales","The Supreme Court judgment that denied Black citizenship and struck down the Missouri Compromise.":"El fallo de la Corte Suprema que negó la ciudadanía a las personas negras y anuló el Compromiso de Misuri.","What did the Court decide about citizenship and about Congress's power?":"¿Qué decidió la Corte sobre la ciudadanía y sobre el poder del Congreso?","How might Northerners and Southerners react differently to this ruling?":"¿Cómo podrían reaccionar de manera diferente los norteños y los sureños ante este fallo?","Bleeding Kansas — National Park Service":"Bleeding Kansas (el Kansas sangrante) — Servicio de Parques Nacionales","How popular sovereignty turned Kansas into a battleground over slavery.":"Cómo la soberanía popular convirtió a Kansas en un campo de batalla por la esclavitud.","Why did violence break out in Kansas?":"¿Por qué estalló la violencia en Kansas?","How did this deepen the conflict between North and South?":"¿Cómo profundizó esto el conflicto entre el Norte y el Sur?","Trigger Events of the Civil War — American Battlefield Trust":"Acontecimientos desencadenantes de la Guerra Civil — American Battlefield Trust","The escalating chain of events from the Fugitive Slave Act to Fort Sumter.":"La cadena de acontecimientos en aumento desde la Ley de Esclavos Fugitivos hasta Fort Sumter.","Which events form the chain toward war?":"¿Qué acontecimientos forman la cadena que conduce a la guerra?","Which one seems to be the point of no return?":"¿Cuál parece ser el punto sin retorno?","Disputes over whether slavery may expand into western territories won from Mexico (1848–1850).":"Disputas sobre si la esclavitud puede expandirse a los territorios del oeste ganados a México (1848–1850).","Compromise of 1850 and its Fugitive Slave Act (Sept. 1850) — a deal that also forced free states to return escaped people.":"El Compromiso de 1850 y su Ley de Esclavos Fugitivos (septiembre de 1850): un acuerdo que también obligó a los estados libres a devolver a las personas que habían escapado.","Kansas–Nebraska Act (May 1854) reopens the question by 'popular sovereignty,' leading to 'Bleeding Kansas' violence (1854–1859).":"La Ley Kansas–Nebraska (mayo de 1854) reabre la cuestión mediante la 'soberanía popular', lo que conduce a la violencia de 'Bleeding Kansas' (el Kansas sangrante) (1854–1859).","Dred Scott decision (March 1857) denies Black citizenship and any federal power to bar slavery; John Brown's Harpers Ferry raid (Oct. 1859) hardens both sides.":"La decisión Dred Scott (marzo de 1857) niega la ciudadanía a las personas negras y cualquier poder federal para prohibir la esclavitud; el asalto de John Brown a Harpers Ferry (octubre de 1859) endurece a ambos bandos.","Lincoln's election (Nov. 1860) leads Deep South states to secede (Dec. 1860–Feb. 1861); Confederates fire on Fort Sumter (April 12–14, 1861).":"La elección de Lincoln (noviembre de 1860) lleva a los estados del Sur Profundo a separarse (diciembre de 1860 – febrero de 1861); los confederados disparan contra Fort Sumter (12–14 de abril de 1861).","Outbreak of the Civil War (1861–1865); the Upper South secedes after Sumter; the war becomes one that ends slavery.":"El estallido de la Guerra Civil (1861–1865); el Alto Sur se separa después de Sumter; la guerra se convierte en una que pone fin a la esclavitud.","What if the Compromise of 1850 had not included the harsh Fugitive Slave Act — would sectional anger have cooled instead of spreading North?":"¿Qué habría pasado si el Compromiso de 1850 no hubiera incluido la dura Ley de Esclavos Fugitivos? ¿Se habría enfriado la ira entre las regiones en lugar de extenderse hacia el Norte?","Stephen A. Douglas — authored the Kansas–Nebraska Act and popular sovereignty":"Stephen A. Douglas — autor de la Ley Kansas–Nebraska y de la soberanía popular","Chief Justice Roger B. Taney — wrote the Dred Scott majority opinion":"El presidente de la Corte Suprema Roger B. Taney — redactó la opinión mayoritaria en el caso Dred Scott","John Brown — led the Harpers Ferry raid":"John Brown — dirigió el asalto a Harpers Ferry","Abraham Lincoln — whose election triggered secession":"Abraham Lincoln — cuya elección desencadenó la secesión","Which single link did the most to make war unavoidable — the Fugitive Slave Act, the Kansas–Nebraska Act, Dred Scott, Harpers Ferry, or Lincoln's election? Choose one, and use evidence from at least two other links to defend it.":"¿Qué eslabón por sí solo contribuyó más a hacer inevitable la guerra: la Ley de Esclavos Fugitivos, la Ley Kansas–Nebraska, el caso Dred Scott, Harpers Ferry o la elección de Lincoln? Elige uno y usa evidencia de al menos otros dos eslabones para defenderlo."},"vi":{"The Road to the Civil War":"Con đường dẫn đến Nội chiến","Follow the chain of conflicts over slavery's expansion from 1850 to 1861 and decide which link did the most to make war unavoidable.":"Hãy theo dõi chuỗi các xung đột về việc mở rộng chế độ nô lệ từ năm 1850 đến năm 1861 và quyết định mắt xích nào đã góp phần nhiều nhất khiến chiến tranh trở nên không thể tránh khỏi.","The Civil War did not begin with a single event. Through the 1850s, a chain of conflicts over whether slavery could expand into the western territories pushed the nation toward war — each action producing a sharper reaction. Trace the chain from pressure to consequence, and decide which link mattered most.":"Nội chiến không bắt đầu bằng một sự kiện đơn lẻ. Trong suốt thập niên 1850, một chuỗi các xung đột về việc liệu chế độ nô lệ có thể mở rộng vào các vùng lãnh thổ phía tây hay không đã đẩy quốc gia đến chiến tranh — mỗi hành động lại tạo ra một phản ứng gay gắt hơn. Hãy lần theo chuỗi từ áp lực đến hậu quả, và quyết định mắt xích nào quan trọng nhất.","Secession and Fort Sumter":"Sự ly khai và Đồn Sumter","The United States":"Hoa Kỳ","Compare your chains with a partner. Did you order the links the same way?":"Hãy so sánh chuỗi của em với một bạn cùng lớp. Các em có sắp xếp các mắt xích theo cùng một cách không?","Did you choose the same 'most important link'? Defend your choice with evidence.":"Các em có chọn cùng một 'mắt xích quan trọng nhất' không? Hãy bảo vệ lựa chọn của em bằng bằng chứng.","Which link in the chain did the most to make war unavoidable? Support your claim with evidence from at least two sources and two links.":"Mắt xích nào trong chuỗi đã góp phần nhiều nhất khiến chiến tranh trở nên không thể tránh khỏi? Hãy chứng minh lập luận của em bằng bằng chứng từ ít nhất hai nguồn và hai mắt xích.","Explain how one action in the chain produced a sharper reaction.":"Hãy giải thích cách một hành động trong chuỗi đã tạo ra một phản ứng gay gắt hơn.","Connect the Kansas–Nebraska Act to the violence of 'Bleeding Kansas.'":"Hãy liên hệ Đạo luật Kansas–Nebraska với bạo lực của 'Bleeding Kansas' (Kansas đẫm máu).","Apply the idea of an escalating chain of conflict to another dispute in history or the world today.":"Hãy vận dụng ý tưởng về một chuỗi xung đột leo thang vào một tranh chấp khác trong lịch sử hoặc trên thế giới ngày nay.","Dred Scott v. Sandford (1857) — National Archives":"Dred Scott kiện Sandford (1857) — Cục Lưu trữ Quốc gia","The Supreme Court judgment that denied Black citizenship and struck down the Missouri Compromise.":"Phán quyết của Tòa án Tối cao phủ nhận quyền công dân của người da đen và bãi bỏ Thỏa hiệp Missouri.","What did the Court decide about citizenship and about Congress's power?":"Tòa án đã quyết định điều gì về quyền công dân và về quyền lực của Quốc hội?","How might Northerners and Southerners react differently to this ruling?":"Người miền Bắc và người miền Nam có thể phản ứng khác nhau như thế nào trước phán quyết này?","Bleeding Kansas — National Park Service":"Bleeding Kansas (Kansas đẫm máu) — Cục Công viên Quốc gia","How popular sovereignty turned Kansas into a battleground over slavery.":"Cách chủ quyền của dân chúng (popular sovereignty) đã biến Kansas thành một chiến trường về vấn đề chế độ nô lệ.","Why did violence break out in Kansas?":"Tại sao bạo lực bùng phát ở Kansas?","How did this deepen the conflict between North and South?":"Điều này đã làm sâu sắc thêm xung đột giữa miền Bắc và miền Nam như thế nào?","Trigger Events of the Civil War — American Battlefield Trust":"Những sự kiện châm ngòi Nội chiến — American Battlefield Trust","The escalating chain of events from the Fugitive Slave Act to Fort Sumter.":"Chuỗi sự kiện leo thang từ Đạo luật Nô lệ Bỏ trốn đến Đồn Sumter.","Which events form the chain toward war?":"Những sự kiện nào tạo thành chuỗi dẫn đến chiến tranh?","Which one seems to be the point of no return?":"Sự kiện nào có vẻ là điểm không thể quay đầu?","Disputes over whether slavery may expand into western territories won from Mexico (1848–1850).":"Những tranh chấp về việc liệu chế độ nô lệ có thể mở rộng vào các vùng lãnh thổ phía tây giành được từ Mexico hay không (1848–1850).","Compromise of 1850 and its Fugitive Slave Act (Sept. 1850) — a deal that also forced free states to return escaped people.":"Thỏa hiệp năm 1850 và Đạo luật Nô lệ Bỏ trốn kèm theo (tháng 9 năm 1850) — một thỏa thuận cũng buộc các bang tự do phải trả lại những người đã bỏ trốn.","Kansas–Nebraska Act (May 1854) reopens the question by 'popular sovereignty,' leading to 'Bleeding Kansas' violence (1854–1859).":"Đạo luật Kansas–Nebraska (tháng 5 năm 1854) khơi lại vấn đề bằng 'chủ quyền của dân chúng', dẫn đến bạo lực 'Bleeding Kansas' (Kansas đẫm máu) (1854–1859).","Dred Scott decision (March 1857) denies Black citizenship and any federal power to bar slavery; John Brown's Harpers Ferry raid (Oct. 1859) hardens both sides.":"Phán quyết Dred Scott (tháng 3 năm 1857) phủ nhận quyền công dân của người da đen và bất kỳ quyền lực liên bang nào nhằm cấm chế độ nô lệ; cuộc đột kích của John Brown vào Harpers Ferry (tháng 10 năm 1859) khiến cả hai phe thêm cứng rắn.","Lincoln's election (Nov. 1860) leads Deep South states to secede (Dec. 1860–Feb. 1861); Confederates fire on Fort Sumter (April 12–14, 1861).":"Cuộc bầu cử Lincoln (tháng 11 năm 1860) khiến các bang miền Nam Sâu (Deep South) ly khai (tháng 12 năm 1860 – tháng 2 năm 1861); quân Liên minh miền Nam nổ súng vào Đồn Sumter (12–14 tháng 4 năm 1861).","Outbreak of the Civil War (1861–1865); the Upper South secedes after Sumter; the war becomes one that ends slavery.":"Nội chiến bùng nổ (1861–1865); miền Nam Trên (Upper South) ly khai sau vụ Sumter; cuộc chiến trở thành một cuộc chiến chấm dứt chế độ nô lệ.","What if the Compromise of 1850 had not included the harsh Fugitive Slave Act — would sectional anger have cooled instead of spreading North?":"Điều gì sẽ xảy ra nếu Thỏa hiệp năm 1850 không bao gồm Đạo luật Nô lệ Bỏ trốn hà khắc — liệu cơn giận giữa các vùng có nguôi đi thay vì lan ra miền Bắc không?","Stephen A. Douglas — authored the Kansas–Nebraska Act and popular sovereignty":"Stephen A. Douglas — người soạn thảo Đạo luật Kansas–Nebraska và chủ quyền của dân chúng","Chief Justice Roger B. Taney — wrote the Dred Scott majority opinion":"Chánh án Roger B. Taney — người viết ý kiến đa số trong vụ Dred Scott","John Brown — led the Harpers Ferry raid":"John Brown — người dẫn đầu cuộc đột kích Harpers Ferry","Abraham Lincoln — whose election triggered secession":"Abraham Lincoln — người mà cuộc bầu cử của ông đã châm ngòi cho sự ly khai","Which single link did the most to make war unavoidable — the Fugitive Slave Act, the Kansas–Nebraska Act, Dred Scott, Harpers Ferry, or Lincoln's election? Choose one, and use evidence from at least two other links to defend it.":"Mắt xích đơn lẻ nào đã góp phần nhiều nhất khiến chiến tranh trở nên không thể tránh khỏi — Đạo luật Nô lệ Bỏ trốn, Đạo luật Kansas–Nebraska, vụ Dred Scott, Harpers Ferry, hay cuộc bầu cử Lincoln? Hãy chọn một và dùng bằng chứng từ ít nhất hai mắt xích khác để bảo vệ lựa chọn đó."},"ar":{"The Road to the Civil War":"الطريق إلى الحرب الأهلية","Follow the chain of conflicts over slavery's expansion from 1850 to 1861 and decide which link did the most to make war unavoidable.":"تتبّع سلسلة الصراعات حول توسّع نظام العبودية من عام 1850 إلى عام 1861، وقرّر أي حلقة أسهمت أكثر من غيرها في جعل الحرب أمرًا لا مفرّ منه.","The Civil War did not begin with a single event. Through the 1850s, a chain of conflicts over whether slavery could expand into the western territories pushed the nation toward war — each action producing a sharper reaction. Trace the chain from pressure to consequence, and decide which link mattered most.":"لم تبدأ الحرب الأهلية بحدث واحد. فخلال خمسينيات القرن التاسع عشر، دفعت سلسلة من الصراعات حول ما إذا كان بإمكان نظام العبودية أن يتوسّع إلى الأقاليم الغربية بالأمة نحو الحرب — إذ أنتج كل فعلٍ ردَّ فعلٍ أشدّ حدّة. تتبّع السلسلة من الضغط إلى النتيجة، وقرّر أي حلقة كانت الأهمّ.","Secession and Fort Sumter":"الانفصال وحصن سمتر (Fort Sumter)","The United States":"الولايات المتحدة","Compare your chains with a partner. Did you order the links the same way?":"قارن سلسلتك مع زميلٍ لك. هل رتّبتما الحلقات بالطريقة نفسها؟","Did you choose the same 'most important link'? Defend your choice with evidence.":"هل اخترتما 'الحلقة الأهمّ' نفسها؟ ادعم اختيارك بالأدلة.","Which link in the chain did the most to make war unavoidable? Support your claim with evidence from at least two sources and two links.":"أيّ حلقة في السلسلة أسهمت أكثر من غيرها في جعل الحرب أمرًا لا مفرّ منه؟ ادعم دعواك بأدلّة من مصدرين اثنين على الأقل وحلقتين اثنتين.","Explain how one action in the chain produced a sharper reaction.":"اشرح كيف أنتج فعلٌ واحد في السلسلة ردَّ فعلٍ أشدّ حدّة.","Connect the Kansas–Nebraska Act to the violence of 'Bleeding Kansas.'":"اربط قانون كانساس–نبراسكا (Kansas–Nebraska Act) بأعمال العنف في 'كانساس النازفة' (Bleeding Kansas).","Apply the idea of an escalating chain of conflict to another dispute in history or the world today.":"طبّق فكرة سلسلة الصراع المتصاعدة على نزاعٍ آخر في التاريخ أو في العالم اليوم.","Dred Scott v. Sandford (1857) — National Archives":"قضية دريد سكوت ضد ساندفورد (Dred Scott v. Sandford) (1857) — الأرشيف الوطني","The Supreme Court judgment that denied Black citizenship and struck down the Missouri Compromise.":"حكم المحكمة العليا الذي أنكر المواطنة على السود وألغى تسوية ميزوري (Missouri Compromise).","What did the Court decide about citizenship and about Congress's power?":"بماذا قضت المحكمة بشأن المواطنة وبشأن سلطة الكونغرس؟","How might Northerners and Southerners react differently to this ruling?":"كيف قد يختلف ردّ فعل أهل الشمال عن ردّ فعل أهل الجنوب تجاه هذا الحكم؟","Bleeding Kansas — National Park Service":"كانساس النازفة (Bleeding Kansas) — هيئة المتنزهات الوطنية","How popular sovereignty turned Kansas into a battleground over slavery.":"كيف حوّلت سيادة الشعب (popular sovereignty) كانساس إلى ساحة معركة حول نظام العبودية.","Why did violence break out in Kansas?":"لماذا اندلع العنف في كانساس؟","How did this deepen the conflict between North and South?":"كيف عمّق هذا الصراع بين الشمال والجنوب؟","Trigger Events of the Civil War — American Battlefield Trust":"الأحداث التي أشعلت الحرب الأهلية — American Battlefield Trust","The escalating chain of events from the Fugitive Slave Act to Fort Sumter.":"سلسلة الأحداث المتصاعدة من قانون العبيد الهاربين (Fugitive Slave Act) إلى حصن سمتر (Fort Sumter).","Which events form the chain toward war?":"ما الأحداث التي تُشكّل السلسلة المؤدية إلى الحرب؟","Which one seems to be the point of no return?":"أيّها يبدو أنه نقطة اللاعودة؟","Disputes over whether slavery may expand into western territories won from Mexico (1848–1850).":"نزاعات حول ما إذا كان بإمكان نظام العبودية أن يتوسّع إلى الأقاليم الغربية التي انتُزعت من المكسيك (1848–1850).","Compromise of 1850 and its Fugitive Slave Act (Sept. 1850) — a deal that also forced free states to return escaped people.":"تسوية عام 1850 وما تضمّنته من قانون العبيد الهاربين (Fugitive Slave Act) (سبتمبر 1850) — وهي صفقة أجبرت أيضًا الولايات الحرّة على إعادة الأشخاص الفارّين.","Kansas–Nebraska Act (May 1854) reopens the question by 'popular sovereignty,' leading to 'Bleeding Kansas' violence (1854–1859).":"قانون كانساس–نبراسكا (Kansas–Nebraska Act) (مايو 1854) يعيد فتح المسألة عبر 'سيادة الشعب'، مما يؤدّي إلى عنف 'كانساس النازفة' (Bleeding Kansas) (1854–1859).","Dred Scott decision (March 1857) denies Black citizenship and any federal power to bar slavery; John Brown's Harpers Ferry raid (Oct. 1859) hardens both sides.":"حكم دريد سكوت (Dred Scott) (مارس 1857) يُنكر المواطنة على السود وأي سلطة فيدرالية لحظر نظام العبودية؛ وغارة جون براون (John Brown) على هاربرز فيري (Harpers Ferry) (أكتوبر 1859) تزيد تصلّب الطرفين.","Lincoln's election (Nov. 1860) leads Deep South states to secede (Dec. 1860–Feb. 1861); Confederates fire on Fort Sumter (April 12–14, 1861).":"انتخاب لينكولن (Lincoln) (نوفمبر 1860) يدفع ولايات الجنوب العميق (Deep South) إلى الانفصال (ديسمبر 1860 – فبراير 1861)؛ والكونفدراليون يطلقون النار على حصن سمتر (Fort Sumter) (12–14 أبريل 1861).","Outbreak of the Civil War (1861–1865); the Upper South secedes after Sumter; the war becomes one that ends slavery.":"اندلاع الحرب الأهلية (1861–1865)؛ الجنوب الأعلى (Upper South) ينفصل بعد سمتر (Sumter)؛ وتتحوّل الحرب إلى حربٍ تُنهي نظام العبودية.","What if the Compromise of 1850 had not included the harsh Fugitive Slave Act — would sectional anger have cooled instead of spreading North?":"ماذا لو لم تتضمّن تسوية عام 1850 قانون العبيد الهاربين (Fugitive Slave Act) القاسي — هل كان الغضب بين الأقاليم سيهدأ بدلًا من أن ينتشر نحو الشمال؟","Stephen A. Douglas — authored the Kansas–Nebraska Act and popular sovereignty":"ستيفن أ. دوغلاس (Stephen A. Douglas) — صاحب قانون كانساس–نبراسكا (Kansas–Nebraska Act) وفكرة سيادة الشعب","Chief Justice Roger B. Taney — wrote the Dred Scott majority opinion":"رئيس المحكمة العليا روجر ب. تاني (Roger B. Taney) — كتب رأي الأغلبية في قضية دريد سكوت (Dred Scott)","John Brown — led the Harpers Ferry raid":"جون براون (John Brown) — قاد غارة هاربرز فيري (Harpers Ferry)","Abraham Lincoln — whose election triggered secession":"أبراهام لينكولن (Abraham Lincoln) — الذي أشعل انتخابه شرارة الانفصال","Which single link did the most to make war unavoidable — the Fugitive Slave Act, the Kansas–Nebraska Act, Dred Scott, Harpers Ferry, or Lincoln's election? Choose one, and use evidence from at least two other links to defend it.":"أيّ حلقة واحدة أسهمت أكثر من غيرها في جعل الحرب أمرًا لا مفرّ منه — قانون العبيد الهاربين (Fugitive Slave Act)، أم قانون كانساس–نبراسكا (Kansas–Nebraska Act)، أم قضية دريد سكوت (Dred Scott)، أم هاربرز فيري (Harpers Ferry)، أم انتخاب لينكولن (Lincoln)؟ اختر واحدة، واستخدم أدلّة من حلقتين أخريين على الأقل للدفاع عنها."},"zh":{"The Road to the Civil War":"通往内战之路","Follow the chain of conflicts over slavery's expansion from 1850 to 1861 and decide which link did the most to make war unavoidable.":"追踪1850年至1861年间围绕奴隶制扩张的一系列冲突，并判断哪一环节对使战争变得无法避免起了最大作用。","The Civil War did not begin with a single event. Through the 1850s, a chain of conflicts over whether slavery could expand into the western territories pushed the nation toward war — each action producing a sharper reaction. Trace the chain from pressure to consequence, and decide which link mattered most.":"内战并非始于单一事件。整个1850年代，围绕奴隶制能否扩张到西部领地的一连串冲突把这个国家推向了战争——每一次行动都引发更为激烈的反应。请追溯这条从压力到后果的链条，并判断哪一环节最为关键。","Secession and Fort Sumter":"脱离联邦与萨姆特堡（Fort Sumter）","The United States":"美国","Compare your chains with a partner. Did you order the links the same way?":"与同伴比较你们的链条。你们排列各环节的顺序一样吗？","Did you choose the same 'most important link'? Defend your choice with evidence.":"你们选择的\"最重要的环节\"是否相同？请用证据为你的选择辩护。","Which link in the chain did the most to make war unavoidable? Support your claim with evidence from at least two sources and two links.":"链条中哪一环节对使战争变得无法避免起了最大作用？请用至少两个来源和两个环节的证据来支持你的主张。","Explain how one action in the chain produced a sharper reaction.":"请解释链条中的某一行动如何引发了更为激烈的反应。","Connect the Kansas–Nebraska Act to the violence of 'Bleeding Kansas.'":"将《堪萨斯—内布拉斯加法案》（Kansas–Nebraska Act）与\"血溅堪萨斯\"（Bleeding Kansas）的暴力联系起来。","Apply the idea of an escalating chain of conflict to another dispute in history or the world today.":"将\"冲突不断升级的链条\"这一思路应用到历史上或当今世界的另一场争端上。","Dred Scott v. Sandford (1857) — National Archives":"德雷德·斯科特诉桑福德案（Dred Scott v. Sandford，1857年）——美国国家档案馆","The Supreme Court judgment that denied Black citizenship and struck down the Missouri Compromise.":"最高法院的这项判决否定了黑人的公民身份，并推翻了《密苏里妥协案》。","What did the Court decide about citizenship and about Congress's power?":"法院就公民身份以及国会的权力作出了什么裁定？","How might Northerners and Southerners react differently to this ruling?":"北方人和南方人对这项裁决的反应可能有何不同？","Bleeding Kansas — National Park Service":"血溅堪萨斯（Bleeding Kansas）——美国国家公园管理局","How popular sovereignty turned Kansas into a battleground over slavery.":"\"人民主权\"（popular sovereignty）如何使堪萨斯变成了一个围绕奴隶制的战场。","Why did violence break out in Kansas?":"堪萨斯为什么会爆发暴力？","How did this deepen the conflict between North and South?":"这如何加深了南北方之间的冲突？","Trigger Events of the Civil War — American Battlefield Trust":"引发内战的导火索事件——American Battlefield Trust","The escalating chain of events from the Fugitive Slave Act to Fort Sumter.":"从《逃亡奴隶法》（Fugitive Slave Act）到萨姆特堡（Fort Sumter）不断升级的一系列事件。","Which events form the chain toward war?":"哪些事件构成了通向战争的链条？","Which one seems to be the point of no return?":"哪一件似乎是无法回头的转折点？","Disputes over whether slavery may expand into western territories won from Mexico (1848–1850).":"围绕奴隶制能否扩张到从墨西哥赢得的西部领地的争端（1848–1850年）。","Compromise of 1850 and its Fugitive Slave Act (Sept. 1850) — a deal that also forced free states to return escaped people.":"《1850年妥协案》及其中的《逃亡奴隶法》（1850年9月）——这项协议还迫使自由州将逃出的人送回。","Kansas–Nebraska Act (May 1854) reopens the question by 'popular sovereignty,' leading to 'Bleeding Kansas' violence (1854–1859).":"《堪萨斯—内布拉斯加法案》（Kansas–Nebraska Act，1854年5月）以\"人民主权\"重新引发这一问题，导致\"血溅堪萨斯\"（Bleeding Kansas）暴力（1854–1859年）。","Dred Scott decision (March 1857) denies Black citizenship and any federal power to bar slavery; John Brown's Harpers Ferry raid (Oct. 1859) hardens both sides.":"德雷德·斯科特案判决（Dred Scott，1857年3月）否定了黑人的公民身份以及联邦禁止奴隶制的任何权力；约翰·布朗（John Brown）对哈珀斯费里（Harpers Ferry）的袭击（1859年10月）使双方立场更加强硬。","Lincoln's election (Nov. 1860) leads Deep South states to secede (Dec. 1860–Feb. 1861); Confederates fire on Fort Sumter (April 12–14, 1861).":"林肯（Lincoln）当选（1860年11月）促使南方腹地（Deep South）各州脱离联邦（1860年12月–1861年2月）；南方邦联军炮击萨姆特堡（Fort Sumter，1861年4月12–14日）。","Outbreak of the Civil War (1861–1865); the Upper South secedes after Sumter; the war becomes one that ends slavery.":"内战爆发（1861–1865年）；上南方（Upper South）在萨姆特堡事件后脱离联邦；这场战争最终成为一场结束奴隶制的战争。","What if the Compromise of 1850 had not included the harsh Fugitive Slave Act — would sectional anger have cooled instead of spreading North?":"假如《1850年妥协案》没有包含严厉的《逃亡奴隶法》——地区间的愤怒会平息，而不是向北方蔓延吗？","Stephen A. Douglas — authored the Kansas–Nebraska Act and popular sovereignty":"斯蒂芬·A·道格拉斯（Stephen A. Douglas）——《堪萨斯—内布拉斯加法案》及\"人民主权\"的提出者","Chief Justice Roger B. Taney — wrote the Dred Scott majority opinion":"首席大法官罗杰·B·坦尼（Roger B. Taney）——撰写了德雷德·斯科特案（Dred Scott）的多数意见","John Brown — led the Harpers Ferry raid":"约翰·布朗（John Brown）——领导了哈珀斯费里（Harpers Ferry）袭击","Abraham Lincoln — whose election triggered secession":"亚伯拉罕·林肯（Abraham Lincoln）——他的当选引发了脱离联邦","Which single link did the most to make war unavoidable — the Fugitive Slave Act, the Kansas–Nebraska Act, Dred Scott, Harpers Ferry, or Lincoln's election? Choose one, and use evidence from at least two other links to defend it.":"哪一个单独的环节对使战争变得无法避免起了最大作用——《逃亡奴隶法》、《堪萨斯—内布拉斯加法案》、德雷德·斯科特案、哈珀斯费里，还是林肯当选？选择一个，并用至少另外两个环节的证据为它辩护。"},"ur":{"The Road to the Civil War":"خانہ جنگی کی طرف راستہ","Follow the chain of conflicts over slavery's expansion from 1850 to 1861 and decide which link did the most to make war unavoidable.":"1850 سے 1861 تک غلامی کے پھیلاؤ پر ہونے والے تنازعات کی زنجیر کا سراغ لگائیں اور فیصلہ کریں کہ کس کڑی نے جنگ کو ناگزیر بنانے میں سب سے زیادہ کردار ادا کیا۔","The Civil War did not begin with a single event. Through the 1850s, a chain of conflicts over whether slavery could expand into the western territories pushed the nation toward war — each action producing a sharper reaction. Trace the chain from pressure to consequence, and decide which link mattered most.":"خانہ جنگی کسی ایک واقعے سے شروع نہیں ہوئی۔ 1850 کی دہائی کے دوران، اس بارے میں تنازعات کی ایک زنجیر کہ آیا غلامی مغربی علاقوں تک پھیل سکتی ہے، قوم کو جنگ کی طرف دھکیلتی رہی — ہر عمل ایک زیادہ شدید ردعمل پیدا کرتا رہا۔ دباؤ سے نتیجے تک اس زنجیر کا سراغ لگائیں اور فیصلہ کریں کہ کون سی کڑی سب سے زیادہ اہم تھی۔","Secession and Fort Sumter":"علیحدگی اور فورٹ سمٹر (Fort Sumter)","The United States":"ریاستہائے متحدہ امریکہ","Compare your chains with a partner. Did you order the links the same way?":"اپنی زنجیر کا موازنہ کسی ساتھی کے ساتھ کریں۔ کیا آپ دونوں نے کڑیوں کو ایک ہی ترتیب میں رکھا؟","Did you choose the same 'most important link'? Defend your choice with evidence.":"کیا آپ دونوں نے وہی 'سب سے اہم کڑی' چنی؟ اپنے انتخاب کا دفاع شواہد سے کریں۔","Which link in the chain did the most to make war unavoidable? Support your claim with evidence from at least two sources and two links.":"زنجیر کی کون سی کڑی نے جنگ کو ناگزیر بنانے میں سب سے زیادہ کردار ادا کیا؟ اپنے دعوے کی تائید کم از کم دو ذرائع اور دو کڑیوں کے شواہد سے کریں۔","Explain how one action in the chain produced a sharper reaction.":"وضاحت کریں کہ زنجیر کے کسی ایک عمل نے کیسے زیادہ شدید ردعمل پیدا کیا۔","Connect the Kansas–Nebraska Act to the violence of 'Bleeding Kansas.'":"کینساس–نبراسکا ایکٹ (Kansas–Nebraska Act) کو 'بلیڈنگ کینساس' (Bleeding Kansas) کے تشدد سے جوڑیں۔","Apply the idea of an escalating chain of conflict to another dispute in history or the world today.":"بڑھتے ہوئے تنازعے کی زنجیر کے تصور کو تاریخ کے کسی اور تنازعے یا آج کی دنیا کے کسی تنازعے پر لاگو کریں۔","Dred Scott v. Sandford (1857) — National Archives":"ڈریڈ اسکاٹ بمقابلہ سینڈفورڈ (Dred Scott v. Sandford) (1857) — نیشنل آرکائیوز","The Supreme Court judgment that denied Black citizenship and struck down the Missouri Compromise.":"سپریم کورٹ کا وہ فیصلہ جس نے سیاہ فام لوگوں کی شہریت سے انکار کیا اور مسوری سمجھوتے (Missouri Compromise) کو کالعدم قرار دیا۔","What did the Court decide about citizenship and about Congress's power?":"عدالت نے شہریت اور کانگریس کے اختیار کے بارے میں کیا فیصلہ کیا؟","How might Northerners and Southerners react differently to this ruling?":"اس فیصلے پر شمالی اور جنوبی لوگ مختلف انداز میں کیسے ردعمل ظاہر کر سکتے ہیں؟","Bleeding Kansas — National Park Service":"بلیڈنگ کینساس (Bleeding Kansas) — نیشنل پارک سروس","How popular sovereignty turned Kansas into a battleground over slavery.":"عوامی خودمختاری (popular sovereignty) نے کیسے کینساس کو غلامی پر ایک میدانِ جنگ بنا دیا۔","Why did violence break out in Kansas?":"کینساس میں تشدد کیوں پھوٹ پڑا؟","How did this deepen the conflict between North and South?":"اس نے شمال اور جنوب کے درمیان تنازعے کو کیسے گہرا کیا؟","Trigger Events of the Civil War — American Battlefield Trust":"خانہ جنگی کو بھڑکانے والے واقعات — American Battlefield Trust","The escalating chain of events from the Fugitive Slave Act to Fort Sumter.":"مفرور غلاموں کے قانون (Fugitive Slave Act) سے فورٹ سمٹر (Fort Sumter) تک بڑھتے ہوئے واقعات کی زنجیر۔","Which events form the chain toward war?":"کون سے واقعات جنگ کی طرف لے جانے والی زنجیر بناتے ہیں؟","Which one seems to be the point of no return?":"کون سا واقعہ ایسا لگتا ہے جس کے بعد واپسی ممکن نہ رہی؟","Disputes over whether slavery may expand into western territories won from Mexico (1848–1850).":"اس بارے میں تنازعات کہ آیا غلامی میکسیکو سے جیتے گئے مغربی علاقوں تک پھیل سکتی ہے (1848–1850)۔","Compromise of 1850 and its Fugitive Slave Act (Sept. 1850) — a deal that also forced free states to return escaped people.":"1850 کا سمجھوتہ اور اس کا مفرور غلاموں کا قانون (Fugitive Slave Act) (ستمبر 1850) — ایک ایسا معاہدہ جس نے آزاد ریاستوں کو بھی فرار ہونے والے افراد کو واپس کرنے پر مجبور کیا۔","Kansas–Nebraska Act (May 1854) reopens the question by 'popular sovereignty,' leading to 'Bleeding Kansas' violence (1854–1859).":"کینساس–نبراسکا ایکٹ (Kansas–Nebraska Act) (مئی 1854) 'عوامی خودمختاری' کے ذریعے اس سوال کو دوبارہ کھول دیتا ہے، جو 'بلیڈنگ کینساس' (Bleeding Kansas) کے تشدد (1854–1859) کا سبب بنتا ہے۔","Dred Scott decision (March 1857) denies Black citizenship and any federal power to bar slavery; John Brown's Harpers Ferry raid (Oct. 1859) hardens both sides.":"ڈریڈ اسکاٹ فیصلہ (Dred Scott) (مارچ 1857) سیاہ فام لوگوں کی شہریت اور غلامی پر پابندی لگانے کے کسی بھی وفاقی اختیار سے انکار کرتا ہے؛ جان براؤن (John Brown) کا ہارپرز فیری (Harpers Ferry) پر حملہ (اکتوبر 1859) دونوں فریقوں کو مزید سخت کر دیتا ہے۔","Lincoln's election (Nov. 1860) leads Deep South states to secede (Dec. 1860–Feb. 1861); Confederates fire on Fort Sumter (April 12–14, 1861).":"لنکن (Lincoln) کا انتخاب (نومبر 1860) گہرے جنوب (Deep South) کی ریاستوں کو علیحدگی پر لے جاتا ہے (دسمبر 1860 – فروری 1861)؛ کنفیڈریٹ فورٹ سمٹر (Fort Sumter) پر گولہ باری کرتے ہیں (12–14 اپریل 1861)۔","Outbreak of the Civil War (1861–1865); the Upper South secedes after Sumter; the war becomes one that ends slavery.":"خانہ جنگی کا آغاز (1861–1865)؛ بالائی جنوب (Upper South) سمٹر کے بعد علیحدگی اختیار کر لیتا ہے؛ یہ جنگ ایک ایسی جنگ بن جاتی ہے جو غلامی کو ختم کر دیتی ہے۔","What if the Compromise of 1850 had not included the harsh Fugitive Slave Act — would sectional anger have cooled instead of spreading North?":"اگر 1850 کے سمجھوتے میں سخت مفرور غلاموں کا قانون (Fugitive Slave Act) شامل نہ ہوتا — تو کیا علاقائی غصہ شمال میں پھیلنے کے بجائے ٹھنڈا پڑ جاتا؟","Stephen A. Douglas — authored the Kansas–Nebraska Act and popular sovereignty":"اسٹیفن اے ڈگلس (Stephen A. Douglas) — کینساس–نبراسکا ایکٹ (Kansas–Nebraska Act) اور عوامی خودمختاری کے خالق","Chief Justice Roger B. Taney — wrote the Dred Scott majority opinion":"چیف جسٹس راجر بی ٹینی (Roger B. Taney) — نے ڈریڈ اسکاٹ (Dred Scott) کیس میں اکثریتی رائے لکھی","John Brown — led the Harpers Ferry raid":"جان براؤن (John Brown) — نے ہارپرز فیری (Harpers Ferry) پر حملے کی قیادت کی","Abraham Lincoln — whose election triggered secession":"ابراہم لنکن (Abraham Lincoln) — جس کے انتخاب نے علیحدگی کو بھڑکایا","Which single link did the most to make war unavoidable — the Fugitive Slave Act, the Kansas–Nebraska Act, Dred Scott, Harpers Ferry, or Lincoln's election? Choose one, and use evidence from at least two other links to defend it.":"کون سی ایک کڑی نے جنگ کو ناگزیر بنانے میں سب سے زیادہ کردار ادا کیا — مفرور غلاموں کا قانون (Fugitive Slave Act)، کینساس–نبراسکا ایکٹ (Kansas–Nebraska Act)، ڈریڈ اسکاٹ (Dred Scott)، ہارپرز فیری (Harpers Ferry)، یا لنکن (Lincoln) کا انتخاب؟ ایک کا انتخاب کریں اور اس کے دفاع کے لیے کم از کم دو دیگر کڑیوں کے شواہد استعمال کریں۔"},"hi":{"The Road to the Civil War":"गृहयुद्ध की ओर राह","Follow the chain of conflicts over slavery's expansion from 1850 to 1861 and decide which link did the most to make war unavoidable.":"1850 से 1861 तक दासता के विस्तार को लेकर हुए संघर्षों की श्रृंखला का अनुसरण करें और तय करें कि किस कड़ी ने युद्ध को अनिवार्य बनाने में सबसे अधिक योगदान दिया।","The Civil War did not begin with a single event. Through the 1850s, a chain of conflicts over whether slavery could expand into the western territories pushed the nation toward war — each action producing a sharper reaction. Trace the chain from pressure to consequence, and decide which link mattered most.":"गृहयुद्ध किसी एक घटना से नहीं शुरू हुआ। 1850 के दशक भर में, इस बात को लेकर संघर्षों की एक श्रृंखला कि क्या दासता पश्चिमी क्षेत्रों में फैल सकती है, राष्ट्र को युद्ध की ओर धकेलती रही — हर कार्रवाई और भी तीखी प्रतिक्रिया को जन्म देती रही। दबाव से परिणाम तक इस श्रृंखला का अनुसरण करें और तय करें कि कौन-सी कड़ी सबसे अधिक महत्वपूर्ण रही।","Secession and Fort Sumter":"पृथक्करण और फोर्ट सम्टर (Fort Sumter)","The United States":"संयुक्त राज्य अमेरिका","Compare your chains with a partner. Did you order the links the same way?":"अपनी श्रृंखला की तुलना किसी साथी से करें। क्या आप दोनों ने कड़ियों को एक ही तरह से क्रमबद्ध किया?","Did you choose the same 'most important link'? Defend your choice with evidence.":"क्या आप दोनों ने वही 'सबसे महत्वपूर्ण कड़ी' चुनी? अपने चयन का बचाव साक्ष्य के साथ करें।","Which link in the chain did the most to make war unavoidable? Support your claim with evidence from at least two sources and two links.":"श्रृंखला की किस कड़ी ने युद्ध को अनिवार्य बनाने में सबसे अधिक योगदान दिया? अपने दावे का समर्थन कम से कम दो स्रोतों और दो कड़ियों के साक्ष्य से करें।","Explain how one action in the chain produced a sharper reaction.":"समझाएँ कि श्रृंखला की किसी एक कार्रवाई ने कैसे और तीखी प्रतिक्रिया को जन्म दिया।","Connect the Kansas–Nebraska Act to the violence of 'Bleeding Kansas.'":"कैनसस–नेब्रास्का अधिनियम (Kansas–Nebraska Act) को 'ब्लीडिंग कैनसस' (Bleeding Kansas) की हिंसा से जोड़ें।","Apply the idea of an escalating chain of conflict to another dispute in history or the world today.":"बढ़ते संघर्ष की श्रृंखला के विचार को इतिहास के किसी अन्य विवाद या आज की दुनिया पर लागू करें।","Dred Scott v. Sandford (1857) — National Archives":"ड्रेड स्कॉट बनाम सैंडफोर्ड (Dred Scott v. Sandford) (1857) — राष्ट्रीय अभिलेखागार","The Supreme Court judgment that denied Black citizenship and struck down the Missouri Compromise.":"सर्वोच्च न्यायालय का वह निर्णय जिसने अश्वेत लोगों की नागरिकता को अस्वीकार किया और मिसौरी समझौते (Missouri Compromise) को रद्द कर दिया।","What did the Court decide about citizenship and about Congress's power?":"न्यायालय ने नागरिकता और कांग्रेस की शक्ति के बारे में क्या निर्णय लिया?","How might Northerners and Southerners react differently to this ruling?":"इस फैसले पर उत्तरी और दक्षिणी लोग किस तरह अलग-अलग प्रतिक्रिया दे सकते हैं?","Bleeding Kansas — National Park Service":"ब्लीडिंग कैनसस (Bleeding Kansas) — राष्ट्रीय उद्यान सेवा","How popular sovereignty turned Kansas into a battleground over slavery.":"जन संप्रभुता (popular sovereignty) ने कैसे कैनसस को दासता को लेकर एक युद्धभूमि में बदल दिया।","Why did violence break out in Kansas?":"कैनसस में हिंसा क्यों भड़की?","How did this deepen the conflict between North and South?":"इसने उत्तर और दक्षिण के बीच संघर्ष को कैसे गहरा किया?","Trigger Events of the Civil War — American Battlefield Trust":"गृहयुद्ध को भड़काने वाली घटनाएँ — American Battlefield Trust","The escalating chain of events from the Fugitive Slave Act to Fort Sumter.":"भगोड़ा दास अधिनियम (Fugitive Slave Act) से फोर्ट सम्टर (Fort Sumter) तक बढ़ती हुई घटनाओं की श्रृंखला।","Which events form the chain toward war?":"कौन-सी घटनाएँ युद्ध की ओर ले जाने वाली श्रृंखला बनाती हैं?","Which one seems to be the point of no return?":"कौन-सी घटना वापसी के असंभव बिंदु जैसी प्रतीत होती है?","Disputes over whether slavery may expand into western territories won from Mexico (1848–1850).":"इस बात को लेकर विवाद कि क्या दासता मेक्सिको से जीते गए पश्चिमी क्षेत्रों में फैल सकती है (1848–1850)।","Compromise of 1850 and its Fugitive Slave Act (Sept. 1850) — a deal that also forced free states to return escaped people.":"1850 का समझौता और उसका भगोड़ा दास अधिनियम (Fugitive Slave Act) (सितंबर 1850) — एक ऐसा सौदा जिसने स्वतंत्र राज्यों को भी भागे हुए लोगों को वापस करने के लिए बाध्य किया।","Kansas–Nebraska Act (May 1854) reopens the question by 'popular sovereignty,' leading to 'Bleeding Kansas' violence (1854–1859).":"कैनसस–नेब्रास्का अधिनियम (Kansas–Nebraska Act) (मई 1854) 'जन संप्रभुता' के ज़रिए इस प्रश्न को फिर से खोल देता है, जिससे 'ब्लीडिंग कैनसस' (Bleeding Kansas) की हिंसा (1854–1859) होती है।","Dred Scott decision (March 1857) denies Black citizenship and any federal power to bar slavery; John Brown's Harpers Ferry raid (Oct. 1859) hardens both sides.":"ड्रेड स्कॉट निर्णय (Dred Scott) (मार्च 1857) अश्वेत लोगों की नागरिकता और दासता पर रोक लगाने की किसी भी संघीय शक्ति को नकार देता है; जॉन ब्राउन (John Brown) का हार्पर्स फेरी (Harpers Ferry) पर हमला (अक्टूबर 1859) दोनों पक्षों को और कठोर बना देता है।","Lincoln's election (Nov. 1860) leads Deep South states to secede (Dec. 1860–Feb. 1861); Confederates fire on Fort Sumter (April 12–14, 1861).":"लिंकन (Lincoln) का चुनाव (नवंबर 1860) गहरे दक्षिण (Deep South) के राज्यों को अलग होने की ओर ले जाता है (दिसंबर 1860 – फरवरी 1861); कॉन्फेडरेट फोर्ट सम्टर (Fort Sumter) पर गोलीबारी करते हैं (12–14 अप्रैल 1861)।","Outbreak of the Civil War (1861–1865); the Upper South secedes after Sumter; the war becomes one that ends slavery.":"गृहयुद्ध का प्रकोप (1861–1865); सम्टर के बाद ऊपरी दक्षिण (Upper South) अलग हो जाता है; यह युद्ध एक ऐसा युद्ध बन जाता है जो दासता को समाप्त कर देता है।","What if the Compromise of 1850 had not included the harsh Fugitive Slave Act — would sectional anger have cooled instead of spreading North?":"यदि 1850 के समझौते में कठोर भगोड़ा दास अधिनियम (Fugitive Slave Act) शामिल न होता — तो क्या क्षेत्रीय गुस्सा उत्तर की ओर फैलने के बजाय ठंडा पड़ जाता?","Stephen A. Douglas — authored the Kansas–Nebraska Act and popular sovereignty":"स्टीफन ए. डगलस (Stephen A. Douglas) — कैनसस–नेब्रास्का अधिनियम (Kansas–Nebraska Act) और जन संप्रभुता के रचयिता","Chief Justice Roger B. Taney — wrote the Dred Scott majority opinion":"मुख्य न्यायाधीश रोजर बी. टेनी (Roger B. Taney) — ने ड्रेड स्कॉट (Dred Scott) मामले में बहुमत की राय लिखी","John Brown — led the Harpers Ferry raid":"जॉन ब्राउन (John Brown) — ने हार्पर्स फेरी (Harpers Ferry) पर हमले का नेतृत्व किया","Abraham Lincoln — whose election triggered secession":"अब्राहम लिंकन (Abraham Lincoln) — जिनके चुनाव ने पृथक्करण को भड़का दिया","Which single link did the most to make war unavoidable — the Fugitive Slave Act, the Kansas–Nebraska Act, Dred Scott, Harpers Ferry, or Lincoln's election? Choose one, and use evidence from at least two other links to defend it.":"कौन-सी एक कड़ी ने युद्ध को अनिवार्य बनाने में सबसे अधिक योगदान दिया — भगोड़ा दास अधिनियम (Fugitive Slave Act), कैनसस–नेब्रास्का अधिनियम (Kansas–Nebraska Act), ड्रेड स्कॉट (Dred Scott), हार्पर्स फेरी (Harpers Ferry), या लिंकन (Lincoln) का चुनाव? एक चुनें, और उसके बचाव के लिए कम से कम दो अन्य कड़ियों के साक्ष्य का उपयोग करें।"}},"transcontinental-railroad":{"es":{"The First Transcontinental Railroad":"El primer ferrocarril transcontinental","Trace the ripples out from the 1869 golden spike: what caused the railroad, what happened right afterward, and what changed for years to come — for whom.":"Sigue las ondas que salen del clavo de oro de 1869: qué causó el ferrocarril, qué pasó justo después y qué cambió durante los años siguientes, y para quién.","On May 10, 1869, two railroads met at Promontory Summit, Utah, and a golden spike joined the coasts by rail for the first time. A trip that once took months now took about a week. But every big change sends out ripples. What caused the railroad, what happened right afterward, and what changed later — and who was helped or hurt?":"El 10 de mayo de 1869, dos ferrocarriles se unieron en Promontory Summit, Utah, y un clavo de oro conectó por primera vez las dos costas por tren. Un viaje que antes tardaba meses ahora tardaba cerca de una semana. Pero todo gran cambio envía ondas. ¿Qué causó el ferrocarril, qué pasó justo después y qué cambió más tarde, y a quién ayudó o perjudicó?","The Golden Spike — the railroad joins the coasts":"El clavo de oro: el ferrocarril une las costas","Promontory Summit, Utah":"Promontory Summit, Utah","Compare your ripples with a partner. Which effects did you both list? Which did only one of you find?":"Compara tus ondas con un compañero. ¿Qué efectos anotaron los dos? ¿Cuáles encontró solo uno de ustedes?","Did you put any effect in a different ring (immediate vs. later) than your partner? Talk about why.":"¿Pusiste algún efecto en un anillo distinto (inmediato o posterior) que tu compañero? Hablen sobre por qué.","Choose the one result of the railroad you think mattered most. Use evidence from your ripples to explain who it helped and who it hurt.":"Elige el resultado del ferrocarril que crees que importó más. Usa pruebas de tus ondas para explicar a quién ayudó y a quién perjudicó.","Explain what the transcontinental railroad was and why it was built.":"Explica qué fue el ferrocarril transcontinental y por qué se construyó.","Connect one cause of the railroad to one long-term change it created.":"Conecta una causa del ferrocarril con un cambio a largo plazo que produjo.","Apply the idea of a big new technology sending out ripples to something today, like the internet. Name one good ripple and one hard ripple.":"Aplica la idea de que una gran tecnología nueva envía ondas a algo de hoy, como el internet. Nombra una onda buena y una onda difícil.","Pacific Railway Act (1862) — National Archives":"Ley del Ferrocarril del Pacífico (1862) — Archivos Nacionales","The 1862 law, signed by Lincoln, that funded the railroad with federal land and loans.":"La ley de 1862, firmada por Lincoln, que financió el ferrocarril con tierras y préstamos federales.","What did the government give the railroad companies?":"¿Qué les dio el gobierno a las compañías ferroviarias?","Why would the government help pay for a railroad?":"¿Por qué ayudaría el gobierno a pagar un ferrocarril?","The Archeology of Chinese Laborers Who Connected the Country (National Park Service)":"La arqueología de los trabajadores chinos que conectaron el país (Servicio de Parques Nacionales)","How over 12,000 Chinese immigrant laborers built the Central Pacific line.":"Cómo más de 12,000 trabajadores inmigrantes chinos construyeron la línea Central Pacific.","Who did much of the hardest building work?":"¿Quiénes hicieron gran parte del trabajo de construcción más duro?","Why might their story have been left out for so long?":"¿Por qué es posible que su historia se haya dejado de lado durante tanto tiempo?","Transcontinental Railroad — Railroads (Library of Congress)":"Ferrocarril transcontinental — Ferrocarriles (Biblioteca del Congreso)","Background and sources on how the two lines met at Promontory Summit.":"Antecedentes y fuentes sobre cómo se unieron las dos líneas en Promontory Summit.","Where and when did the two lines meet?":"¿Dónde y cuándo se unieron las dos líneas?","What changed about travel afterward?":"¿Qué cambió en los viajes después de eso?","Congress passed the Pacific Railway Act (1862) to help pay for the tracks.":"El Congreso aprobó la Ley del Ferrocarril del Pacífico (1862) para ayudar a pagar las vías.","People wanted a fast, safe way to connect the East and West coasts.":"La gente quería una forma rápida y segura de conectar las costas Este y Oeste.","Gold, land, and the chance to settle the West pulled people westward.":"El oro, la tierra y la oportunidad de asentarse en el Oeste atrajeron a la gente hacia el oeste.","Trade and mail needed to move quickly across the whole country.":"El comercio y el correo necesitaban moverse rápidamente por todo el país.","The golden spike joined the two railroads into one line.":"El clavo de oro unió los dos ferrocarriles en una sola línea.","Coast-to-coast travel dropped from months to about a week.":"El viaje de costa a costa se redujo de meses a cerca de una semana.","Goods, mail, and news moved much faster across the country.":"Las mercancías, el correo y las noticias se movían mucho más rápido por todo el país.","New towns and stops grew up along the tracks.":"Nuevos pueblos y paradas surgieron a lo largo de las vías.","Many more settlers moved west, and Western towns and farms grew.":"Muchos más colonos se mudaron al oeste, y los pueblos y granjas del Oeste crecieron.","Native nations lost land and hunting grounds, and the bison were nearly wiped out.":"Las naciones indígenas perdieron tierras y zonas de caza, y los bisontes casi fueron exterminados.","Chinese and Irish immigrant workers shaped the country but faced unfair treatment and low pay.":"Los trabajadores inmigrantes chinos e irlandeses dieron forma al país, pero sufrieron un trato injusto y salarios bajos.","The railroad tied the nation into one big trade network and sped up its growth.":"El ferrocarril unió a la nación en una gran red comercial y aceleró su crecimiento.","The railroad companies — Central Pacific and Union Pacific":"Las compañías ferroviarias: Central Pacific y Union Pacific","Immigrant laborers — Chinese (Central Pacific) and Irish (Union Pacific)":"Trabajadores inmigrantes: chinos (Central Pacific) e irlandeses (Union Pacific)","Native nations of the Plains and West":"Las naciones indígenas de las Llanuras y el Oeste","Settlers, farmers, and traders moving into the West":"Colonos, agricultores y comerciantes que se mudaban al Oeste","Look at all the ripples. Which result of the railroad do you think mattered most — and who did it help or hurt? Give one reason from the map.":"Observa todas las ondas. ¿Qué resultado del ferrocarril crees que importó más, y a quién ayudó o perjudicó? Da una razón a partir del mapa."},"vi":{"The First Transcontinental Railroad":"Tuyến đường sắt xuyên lục địa đầu tiên","Trace the ripples out from the 1869 golden spike: what caused the railroad, what happened right afterward, and what changed for years to come — for whom.":"Hãy lần theo những gợn sóng lan ra từ chiếc đinh vàng năm 1869: điều gì đã tạo ra tuyến đường sắt, điều gì xảy ra ngay sau đó, và điều gì đã thay đổi trong nhiều năm về sau — và với ai.","On May 10, 1869, two railroads met at Promontory Summit, Utah, and a golden spike joined the coasts by rail for the first time. A trip that once took months now took about a week. But every big change sends out ripples. What caused the railroad, what happened right afterward, and what changed later — and who was helped or hurt?":"Vào ngày 10 tháng 5 năm 1869, hai tuyến đường sắt gặp nhau tại Promontory Summit, Utah, và một chiếc đinh vàng lần đầu tiên nối liền hai bờ biển bằng đường sắt. Một chuyến đi từng mất nhiều tháng nay chỉ còn khoảng một tuần. Nhưng mọi thay đổi lớn đều lan ra những gợn sóng. Điều gì đã tạo ra tuyến đường sắt, điều gì xảy ra ngay sau đó, và điều gì đã thay đổi về sau — và ai được lợi hay bị thiệt?","The Golden Spike — the railroad joins the coasts":"Chiếc đinh vàng — đường sắt nối liền hai bờ biển","Promontory Summit, Utah":"Promontory Summit, Utah","Compare your ripples with a partner. Which effects did you both list? Which did only one of you find?":"Hãy so sánh những gợn sóng của em với một bạn. Cả hai em cùng liệt kê những tác động nào? Tác động nào chỉ một trong hai em tìm ra?","Did you put any effect in a different ring (immediate vs. later) than your partner? Talk about why.":"Em có xếp tác động nào vào vòng khác (ngay lập tức so với về sau) so với bạn của em không? Hãy trao đổi lý do vì sao.","Choose the one result of the railroad you think mattered most. Use evidence from your ripples to explain who it helped and who it hurt.":"Hãy chọn một kết quả của tuyến đường sắt mà em cho là quan trọng nhất. Dùng bằng chứng từ những gợn sóng của em để giải thích nó giúp ai và làm hại ai.","Explain what the transcontinental railroad was and why it was built.":"Hãy giải thích tuyến đường sắt xuyên lục địa là gì và vì sao nó được xây dựng.","Connect one cause of the railroad to one long-term change it created.":"Hãy nối một nguyên nhân của tuyến đường sắt với một thay đổi lâu dài mà nó tạo ra.","Apply the idea of a big new technology sending out ripples to something today, like the internet. Name one good ripple and one hard ripple.":"Hãy áp dụng ý tưởng về một công nghệ mới lớn lan ra những gợn sóng vào một thứ ngày nay, như internet. Hãy nêu tên một gợn sóng tốt và một gợn sóng khó khăn.","Pacific Railway Act (1862) — National Archives":"Đạo luật Đường sắt Thái Bình Dương (1862) — Cục Lưu trữ Quốc gia","The 1862 law, signed by Lincoln, that funded the railroad with federal land and loans.":"Đạo luật năm 1862, do Lincoln ký, đã cấp vốn cho tuyến đường sắt bằng đất đai và các khoản vay của liên bang.","What did the government give the railroad companies?":"Chính phủ đã cấp cho các công ty đường sắt những gì?","Why would the government help pay for a railroad?":"Vì sao chính phủ lại giúp chi trả cho một tuyến đường sắt?","The Archeology of Chinese Laborers Who Connected the Country (National Park Service)":"Khảo cổ học về những người lao động Trung Quốc đã nối liền đất nước (Cục Công viên Quốc gia)","How over 12,000 Chinese immigrant laborers built the Central Pacific line.":"Cách hơn 12.000 người lao động nhập cư Trung Quốc đã xây dựng tuyến Central Pacific.","Who did much of the hardest building work?":"Ai đã làm phần lớn công việc xây dựng khó khăn nhất?","Why might their story have been left out for so long?":"Vì sao câu chuyện của họ có thể đã bị bỏ quên trong thời gian dài như vậy?","Transcontinental Railroad — Railroads (Library of Congress)":"Đường sắt xuyên lục địa — Đường sắt (Thư viện Quốc hội)","Background and sources on how the two lines met at Promontory Summit.":"Bối cảnh và các nguồn tư liệu về việc hai tuyến đường gặp nhau tại Promontory Summit.","Where and when did the two lines meet?":"Hai tuyến đường gặp nhau ở đâu và khi nào?","What changed about travel afterward?":"Sau đó việc đi lại đã thay đổi như thế nào?","Congress passed the Pacific Railway Act (1862) to help pay for the tracks.":"Quốc hội đã thông qua Đạo luật Đường sắt Thái Bình Dương (1862) để giúp chi trả cho đường ray.","People wanted a fast, safe way to connect the East and West coasts.":"Mọi người muốn có một cách nhanh chóng và an toàn để nối liền bờ Đông và bờ Tây.","Gold, land, and the chance to settle the West pulled people westward.":"Vàng, đất đai và cơ hội định cư ở miền Tây đã lôi cuốn mọi người đi về phía tây.","Trade and mail needed to move quickly across the whole country.":"Việc buôn bán và thư từ cần được vận chuyển nhanh chóng khắp cả nước.","The golden spike joined the two railroads into one line.":"Chiếc đinh vàng đã nối hai tuyến đường sắt thành một tuyến duy nhất.","Coast-to-coast travel dropped from months to about a week.":"Việc đi lại từ bờ biển này sang bờ biển kia giảm từ nhiều tháng xuống còn khoảng một tuần.","Goods, mail, and news moved much faster across the country.":"Hàng hóa, thư từ và tin tức di chuyển nhanh hơn nhiều trên khắp đất nước.","New towns and stops grew up along the tracks.":"Những thị trấn và trạm dừng mới mọc lên dọc theo đường ray.","Many more settlers moved west, and Western towns and farms grew.":"Nhiều người định cư hơn chuyển về miền Tây, và các thị trấn cùng nông trại ở miền Tây phát triển.","Native nations lost land and hunting grounds, and the bison were nearly wiped out.":"Các dân tộc bản địa mất đất đai và vùng săn bắn, và loài bò rừng bison gần như bị tận diệt.","Chinese and Irish immigrant workers shaped the country but faced unfair treatment and low pay.":"Những người lao động nhập cư Trung Quốc và Ireland đã góp phần định hình đất nước nhưng phải chịu sự đối xử bất công và tiền lương thấp.","The railroad tied the nation into one big trade network and sped up its growth.":"Tuyến đường sắt đã gắn kết cả quốc gia thành một mạng lưới thương mại lớn và thúc đẩy sự phát triển của nó.","The railroad companies — Central Pacific and Union Pacific":"Các công ty đường sắt — Central Pacific và Union Pacific","Immigrant laborers — Chinese (Central Pacific) and Irish (Union Pacific)":"Người lao động nhập cư — người Trung Quốc (Central Pacific) và người Ireland (Union Pacific)","Native nations of the Plains and West":"Các dân tộc bản địa ở vùng Đồng bằng và miền Tây","Settlers, farmers, and traders moving into the West":"Những người định cư, nông dân và thương nhân chuyển đến miền Tây","Look at all the ripples. Which result of the railroad do you think mattered most — and who did it help or hurt? Give one reason from the map.":"Hãy nhìn tất cả những gợn sóng. Em cho rằng kết quả nào của tuyến đường sắt là quan trọng nhất — và nó giúp ai hay làm hại ai? Hãy nêu một lý do từ bản đồ."},"ar":{"The First Transcontinental Railroad":"أول سكة حديد عابرة للقارة","Trace the ripples out from the 1869 golden spike: what caused the railroad, what happened right afterward, and what changed for years to come — for whom.":"تتبّع الموجات المنتشرة من المسمار الذهبي عام 1869: ما الذي أدى إلى بناء السكة الحديدية، وما الذي حدث بعدها مباشرة، وما الذي تغيّر على مدى السنوات التالية — ولمن.","On May 10, 1869, two railroads met at Promontory Summit, Utah, and a golden spike joined the coasts by rail for the first time. A trip that once took months now took about a week. But every big change sends out ripples. What caused the railroad, what happened right afterward, and what changed later — and who was helped or hurt?":"في 10 مايو 1869، التقت سكتان حديديتان عند برومونتوري سِمِت في يوتا، وربط مسمار ذهبي الساحلين بالسكة الحديدية لأول مرة. رحلة كانت تستغرق أشهراً صارت تستغرق نحو أسبوع. لكن كل تغيير كبير يُطلق موجات. ما الذي أدى إلى بناء السكة الحديدية، وما الذي حدث بعدها مباشرة، وما الذي تغيّر لاحقاً — ومن الذي استفاد أو تضرّر؟","The Golden Spike — the railroad joins the coasts":"المسمار الذهبي — السكة الحديدية تربط الساحلين","Promontory Summit, Utah":"برومونتوري سِمِت، يوتا","Compare your ripples with a partner. Which effects did you both list? Which did only one of you find?":"قارن موجاتك مع زميل. ما التأثيرات التي ذكرتماها معاً؟ وما التأثير الذي وجده أحدكما فقط؟","Did you put any effect in a different ring (immediate vs. later) than your partner? Talk about why.":"هل وضعت أي تأثير في حلقة مختلفة (فوري مقابل لاحق) عن زميلك؟ تحدّثا عن السبب.","Choose the one result of the railroad you think mattered most. Use evidence from your ripples to explain who it helped and who it hurt.":"اختر نتيجة واحدة للسكة الحديدية تعتقد أنها الأهم. استخدم أدلة من موجاتك لتوضّح من الذي استفاد ومن الذي تضرّر.","Explain what the transcontinental railroad was and why it was built.":"اشرح ما هي السكة الحديدية العابرة للقارة ولماذا بُنيت.","Connect one cause of the railroad to one long-term change it created.":"اربط سبباً واحداً لبناء السكة الحديدية بتغيير واحد طويل الأمد أحدثته.","Apply the idea of a big new technology sending out ripples to something today, like the internet. Name one good ripple and one hard ripple.":"طبّق فكرة أن تقنية جديدة كبيرة تُطلق موجات على شيء في وقتنا الحاضر، مثل الإنترنت. اذكر موجة إيجابية واحدة وموجة صعبة واحدة.","Pacific Railway Act (1862) — National Archives":"قانون سكة حديد الباسيفيك (1862) — الأرشيف الوطني","The 1862 law, signed by Lincoln, that funded the railroad with federal land and loans.":"قانون عام 1862، الذي وقّعه لينكولن، ومَوّل السكة الحديدية بأراضٍ وقروض فيدرالية.","What did the government give the railroad companies?":"ماذا أعطت الحكومة لشركات السكك الحديدية؟","Why would the government help pay for a railroad?":"لماذا قد تساعد الحكومة في دفع تكاليف سكة حديدية؟","The Archeology of Chinese Laborers Who Connected the Country (National Park Service)":"علم آثار العمّال الصينيين الذين ربطوا البلاد (هيئة الحدائق الوطنية)","How over 12,000 Chinese immigrant laborers built the Central Pacific line.":"كيف بنى أكثر من 12,000 عامل مهاجر صيني خط سنترال باسيفيك.","Who did much of the hardest building work?":"من الذي قام بمعظم أصعب أعمال البناء؟","Why might their story have been left out for so long?":"لماذا قد تكون قصتهم قد أُهملت لمدة طويلة كهذه؟","Transcontinental Railroad — Railroads (Library of Congress)":"السكة الحديدية العابرة للقارة — السكك الحديدية (مكتبة الكونغرس)","Background and sources on how the two lines met at Promontory Summit.":"خلفية ومصادر حول كيفية التقاء الخطين عند برومونتوري سِمِت.","Where and when did the two lines meet?":"أين ومتى التقى الخطان؟","What changed about travel afterward?":"ما الذي تغيّر في السفر بعد ذلك؟","Congress passed the Pacific Railway Act (1862) to help pay for the tracks.":"أقرّ الكونغرس قانون سكة حديد الباسيفيك (1862) للمساعدة في دفع تكاليف القضبان.","People wanted a fast, safe way to connect the East and West coasts.":"أراد الناس وسيلة سريعة وآمنة لربط الساحلين الشرقي والغربي.","Gold, land, and the chance to settle the West pulled people westward.":"الذهب والأرض وفرصة الاستقرار في الغرب جذبت الناس نحو الغرب.","Trade and mail needed to move quickly across the whole country.":"كانت التجارة والبريد بحاجة إلى التنقّل بسرعة عبر البلاد كلها.","The golden spike joined the two railroads into one line.":"ربط المسمار الذهبي السكتين الحديديتين في خط واحد.","Coast-to-coast travel dropped from months to about a week.":"انخفض السفر من ساحل إلى ساحل من أشهر إلى نحو أسبوع.","Goods, mail, and news moved much faster across the country.":"انتقلت البضائع والبريد والأخبار بسرعة أكبر بكثير عبر البلاد.","New towns and stops grew up along the tracks.":"نشأت بلدات ومحطات جديدة على طول القضبان.","Many more settlers moved west, and Western towns and farms grew.":"انتقل مستوطنون كثيرون إلى الغرب، ونمت بلدات ومزارع الغرب.","Native nations lost land and hunting grounds, and the bison were nearly wiped out.":"فقدت الأمم الأصلية أراضيها ومناطق صيدها، وكادت الجواميس (البيسون) أن تُباد بالكامل.","Chinese and Irish immigrant workers shaped the country but faced unfair treatment and low pay.":"شكّل العمّال المهاجرون الصينيون والأيرلنديون البلاد لكنهم واجهوا معاملة جائرة وأجوراً منخفضة.","The railroad tied the nation into one big trade network and sped up its growth.":"ربطت السكة الحديدية الأمة في شبكة تجارية كبيرة واحدة وسرّعت نموها.","The railroad companies — Central Pacific and Union Pacific":"شركتا السكك الحديدية — سنترال باسيفيك ويونيون باسيفيك","Immigrant laborers — Chinese (Central Pacific) and Irish (Union Pacific)":"العمّال المهاجرون — الصينيون (سنترال باسيفيك) والأيرلنديون (يونيون باسيفيك)","Native nations of the Plains and West":"الأمم الأصلية في السهول والغرب","Settlers, farmers, and traders moving into the West":"المستوطنون والمزارعون والتجار المنتقلون إلى الغرب","Look at all the ripples. Which result of the railroad do you think mattered most — and who did it help or hurt? Give one reason from the map.":"انظر إلى جميع الموجات. أي نتيجة للسكة الحديدية تعتقد أنها الأهم — ومن الذي ساعدته أو أضرّت به؟ اذكر سبباً واحداً من الخريطة."},"zh":{"The First Transcontinental Railroad":"第一条横贯大陆铁路","Trace the ripples out from the 1869 golden spike: what caused the railroad, what happened right afterward, and what changed for years to come — for whom.":"追溯从1869年金道钉扩散出去的涟漪：是什么带来了这条铁路，紧接着发生了什么，以及在之后许多年里发生了什么变化——又是为了谁。","On May 10, 1869, two railroads met at Promontory Summit, Utah, and a golden spike joined the coasts by rail for the first time. A trip that once took months now took about a week. But every big change sends out ripples. What caused the railroad, what happened right afterward, and what changed later — and who was helped or hurt?":"1869年5月10日，两条铁路在犹他州的普罗蒙特里峰会合，一枚金道钉第一次用铁路把东西两岸连接起来。一趟曾经需要几个月的旅程，如今只需大约一周。但每一个巨大的变化都会激起涟漪。是什么带来了这条铁路，紧接着发生了什么，之后又发生了什么变化——谁得到了帮助，谁受到了伤害？","The Golden Spike — the railroad joins the coasts":"金道钉——铁路连接东西两岸","Promontory Summit, Utah":"犹他州普罗蒙特里峰","Compare your ripples with a partner. Which effects did you both list? Which did only one of you find?":"和同伴比一比你们的涟漪。哪些影响你们两人都列出来了？哪些只有你们其中一人找到了？","Did you put any effect in a different ring (immediate vs. later) than your partner? Talk about why.":"有没有哪个影响，你放进的圈层（立刻发生还是后来发生）和同伴不一样？说说为什么。","Choose the one result of the railroad you think mattered most. Use evidence from your ripples to explain who it helped and who it hurt.":"选出你认为最重要的一个铁路带来的结果。用你涟漪图里的证据来说明它帮助了谁、伤害了谁。","Explain what the transcontinental railroad was and why it was built.":"解释横贯大陆铁路是什么，以及为什么要修建它。","Connect one cause of the railroad to one long-term change it created.":"把铁路的一个起因和它带来的一个长期变化联系起来。","Apply the idea of a big new technology sending out ripples to something today, like the internet. Name one good ripple and one hard ripple.":"把一项重大新技术激起涟漪的想法用到今天的某样东西上，比如互联网。说出一个好的涟漪和一个艰难的涟漪。","Pacific Railway Act (1862) — National Archives":"《太平洋铁路法案》（1862年）——国家档案馆","The 1862 law, signed by Lincoln, that funded the railroad with federal land and loans.":"1862年由林肯签署的法律，用联邦土地和贷款为铁路提供资金。","What did the government give the railroad companies?":"政府给了铁路公司什么？","Why would the government help pay for a railroad?":"政府为什么要帮忙出钱修铁路？","The Archeology of Chinese Laborers Who Connected the Country (National Park Service)":"连接全国的华工考古（国家公园管理局）","How over 12,000 Chinese immigrant laborers built the Central Pacific line.":"一万两千多名华人移民劳工是如何修建中央太平洋铁路线的。","Who did much of the hardest building work?":"大部分最艰苦的修建工作是谁做的？","Why might their story have been left out for so long?":"为什么他们的故事可能被遗漏了这么久？","Transcontinental Railroad — Railroads (Library of Congress)":"横贯大陆铁路——铁路（国会图书馆）","Background and sources on how the two lines met at Promontory Summit.":"关于两条线路如何在普罗蒙特里峰会合的背景资料和来源。","Where and when did the two lines meet?":"两条线路在何时何地会合？","What changed about travel afterward?":"此后出行发生了什么变化？","Congress passed the Pacific Railway Act (1862) to help pay for the tracks.":"国会通过了《太平洋铁路法案》（1862年），以帮助支付修建铁轨的费用。","People wanted a fast, safe way to connect the East and West coasts.":"人们想要一种快速、安全的方式来连接东西两岸。","Gold, land, and the chance to settle the West pulled people westward.":"黄金、土地以及在西部定居的机会把人们吸引向西部。","Trade and mail needed to move quickly across the whole country.":"贸易和邮件需要在全国范围内快速传送。","The golden spike joined the two railroads into one line.":"金道钉把两条铁路连成了一条线。","Coast-to-coast travel dropped from months to about a week.":"从一岸到另一岸的旅行时间从几个月缩短到大约一周。","Goods, mail, and news moved much faster across the country.":"货物、邮件和消息在全国的传送快得多了。","New towns and stops grew up along the tracks.":"沿着铁轨兴起了新的城镇和站点。","Many more settlers moved west, and Western towns and farms grew.":"更多的定居者迁往西部，西部的城镇和农场随之壮大。","Native nations lost land and hunting grounds, and the bison were nearly wiped out.":"原住民族失去了土地和狩猎场，野牛几乎被赶尽杀绝。","Chinese and Irish immigrant workers shaped the country but faced unfair treatment and low pay.":"华人和爱尔兰移民工人塑造了这个国家，却遭受不公平的对待和低薪。","The railroad tied the nation into one big trade network and sped up its growth.":"铁路把整个国家连成一个大的贸易网络，并加快了它的发展。","The railroad companies — Central Pacific and Union Pacific":"铁路公司——中央太平洋公司和联合太平洋公司","Immigrant laborers — Chinese (Central Pacific) and Irish (Union Pacific)":"移民劳工——华人（中央太平洋公司）和爱尔兰人（联合太平洋公司）","Native nations of the Plains and West":"大平原和西部的原住民族","Settlers, farmers, and traders moving into the West":"迁入西部的定居者、农民和商人","Look at all the ripples. Which result of the railroad do you think mattered most — and who did it help or hurt? Give one reason from the map.":"看看所有的涟漪。你认为铁路带来的哪个结果最重要——它帮助了谁、伤害了谁？从图中给出一个理由。"},"ur":{"The First Transcontinental Railroad":"پہلی بین البراعظمی ریل گاڑی","Trace the ripples out from the 1869 golden spike: what caused the railroad, what happened right afterward, and what changed for years to come — for whom.":"1869 کے سنہری کیل سے پھیلنے والی لہروں کا سراغ لگائیں: ریلوے کس چیز نے بنائی، فوراً بعد کیا ہوا، اور آنے والے برسوں میں کیا بدلا — اور کس کے لیے۔","On May 10, 1869, two railroads met at Promontory Summit, Utah, and a golden spike joined the coasts by rail for the first time. A trip that once took months now took about a week. But every big change sends out ripples. What caused the railroad, what happened right afterward, and what changed later — and who was helped or hurt?":"10 مئی 1869 کو دو ریلوے لائنیں یوٹا کے پرومونٹری سمٹ پر ملیں، اور ایک سنہری کیل نے پہلی بار دونوں ساحلوں کو ریل کے ذریعے جوڑ دیا۔ جو سفر پہلے مہینوں میں طے ہوتا تھا اب تقریباً ایک ہفتے میں ہونے لگا۔ لیکن ہر بڑی تبدیلی لہریں پھیلاتی ہے۔ ریلوے کس چیز نے بنائی، فوراً بعد کیا ہوا، اور بعد میں کیا بدلا — اور کس کو فائدہ ہوا یا نقصان؟","The Golden Spike — the railroad joins the coasts":"سنہری کیل — ریلوے دونوں ساحلوں کو جوڑتی ہے","Promontory Summit, Utah":"پرومونٹری سمٹ، یوٹا","Compare your ripples with a partner. Which effects did you both list? Which did only one of you find?":"اپنی لہروں کا موازنہ کسی ساتھی کے ساتھ کریں۔ کون سے اثرات آپ دونوں نے لکھے؟ کون سا صرف آپ میں سے ایک نے پایا؟","Did you put any effect in a different ring (immediate vs. later) than your partner? Talk about why.":"کیا آپ نے کوئی اثر اپنے ساتھی سے مختلف دائرے (فوری بمقابلہ بعد میں) میں رکھا؟ اس کی وجہ پر بات کریں۔","Choose the one result of the railroad you think mattered most. Use evidence from your ripples to explain who it helped and who it hurt.":"ریلوے کا وہ ایک نتیجہ چنیں جو آپ کے خیال میں سب سے اہم تھا۔ اپنی لہروں سے شواہد استعمال کر کے بتائیں کہ اس نے کس کو فائدہ اور کس کو نقصان پہنچایا۔","Explain what the transcontinental railroad was and why it was built.":"بتائیں کہ بین البراعظمی ریلوے کیا تھی اور اسے کیوں بنایا گیا۔","Connect one cause of the railroad to one long-term change it created.":"ریلوے کے ایک سبب کو اس سے پیدا ہونے والی ایک طویل المدت تبدیلی سے جوڑیں۔","Apply the idea of a big new technology sending out ripples to something today, like the internet. Name one good ripple and one hard ripple.":"کسی بڑی نئی ٹیکنالوجی کے لہریں پھیلانے کے خیال کو آج کی کسی چیز پر لاگو کریں، جیسے انٹرنیٹ۔ ایک اچھی لہر اور ایک مشکل لہر کا نام بتائیں۔","Pacific Railway Act (1862) — National Archives":"پیسیفک ریلوے ایکٹ (1862) — نیشنل آرکائیوز","The 1862 law, signed by Lincoln, that funded the railroad with federal land and loans.":"1862 کا قانون، جس پر لنکن نے دستخط کیے، جس نے وفاقی زمین اور قرضوں سے ریلوے کو مالی مدد دی۔","What did the government give the railroad companies?":"حکومت نے ریلوے کمپنیوں کو کیا دیا؟","Why would the government help pay for a railroad?":"حکومت ریلوے کے لیے پیسے دینے میں مدد کیوں کرے گی؟","The Archeology of Chinese Laborers Who Connected the Country (National Park Service)":"ان چینی مزدوروں کی آثار قدیمہ جنہوں نے ملک کو جوڑا (نیشنل پارک سروس)","How over 12,000 Chinese immigrant laborers built the Central Pacific line.":"کس طرح 12,000 سے زیادہ چینی تارکینِ وطن مزدوروں نے سینٹرل پیسیفک لائن بنائی۔","Who did much of the hardest building work?":"سب سے مشکل تعمیراتی کام کا زیادہ تر حصہ کس نے کیا؟","Why might their story have been left out for so long?":"ان کی کہانی اتنے لمبے عرصے تک کیوں چھوڑ دی گئی ہوگی؟","Transcontinental Railroad — Railroads (Library of Congress)":"بین البراعظمی ریلوے — ریلویز (لائبریری آف کانگریس)","Background and sources on how the two lines met at Promontory Summit.":"اس بارے میں پس منظر اور ذرائع کہ دونوں لائنیں پرومونٹری سمٹ پر کیسے ملیں۔","Where and when did the two lines meet?":"دونوں لائنیں کہاں اور کب ملیں؟","What changed about travel afterward?":"اس کے بعد سفر میں کیا تبدیلی آئی؟","Congress passed the Pacific Railway Act (1862) to help pay for the tracks.":"کانگریس نے پٹریوں کے اخراجات میں مدد کے لیے پیسیفک ریلوے ایکٹ (1862) منظور کیا۔","People wanted a fast, safe way to connect the East and West coasts.":"لوگ مشرقی اور مغربی ساحلوں کو جوڑنے کے لیے ایک تیز اور محفوظ راستہ چاہتے تھے۔","Gold, land, and the chance to settle the West pulled people westward.":"سونا، زمین اور مغرب میں آباد ہونے کا موقع لوگوں کو مغرب کی طرف کھینچ لے گیا۔","Trade and mail needed to move quickly across the whole country.":"تجارت اور ڈاک کو پورے ملک میں تیزی سے پہنچنے کی ضرورت تھی۔","The golden spike joined the two railroads into one line.":"سنہری کیل نے دونوں ریلوے کو ایک لائن میں جوڑ دیا۔","Coast-to-coast travel dropped from months to about a week.":"ایک ساحل سے دوسرے ساحل تک کا سفر مہینوں سے کم ہو کر تقریباً ایک ہفتے پر آ گیا۔","Goods, mail, and news moved much faster across the country.":"سامان، ڈاک اور خبریں پورے ملک میں کہیں زیادہ تیزی سے پہنچنے لگیں۔","New towns and stops grew up along the tracks.":"پٹریوں کے ساتھ ساتھ نئے قصبے اور اسٹاپ بن گئے۔","Many more settlers moved west, and Western towns and farms grew.":"بہت زیادہ آباد کار مغرب کی طرف منتقل ہوئے، اور مغربی قصبے اور کھیت بڑھتے گئے۔","Native nations lost land and hunting grounds, and the bison were nearly wiped out.":"مقامی اقوام نے اپنی زمین اور شکار گاہیں کھو دیں، اور بائسن تقریباً ختم ہو گئے۔","Chinese and Irish immigrant workers shaped the country but faced unfair treatment and low pay.":"چینی اور آئرش تارکینِ وطن مزدوروں نے ملک کو تشکیل دیا لیکن انہیں ناانصافی اور کم اجرت کا سامنا کرنا پڑا۔","The railroad tied the nation into one big trade network and sped up its growth.":"ریلوے نے قوم کو ایک بڑے تجارتی نیٹ ورک میں باندھ دیا اور اس کی ترقی کو تیز کر دیا۔","The railroad companies — Central Pacific and Union Pacific":"ریلوے کمپنیاں — سینٹرل پیسیفک اور یونین پیسیفک","Immigrant laborers — Chinese (Central Pacific) and Irish (Union Pacific)":"تارکینِ وطن مزدور — چینی (سینٹرل پیسیفک) اور آئرش (یونین پیسیفک)","Native nations of the Plains and West":"میدانی علاقوں اور مغرب کی مقامی اقوام","Settlers, farmers, and traders moving into the West":"مغرب کی طرف جانے والے آباد کار، کسان اور تاجر","Look at all the ripples. Which result of the railroad do you think mattered most — and who did it help or hurt? Give one reason from the map.":"تمام لہروں کو دیکھیں۔ آپ کے خیال میں ریلوے کا کون سا نتیجہ سب سے اہم تھا — اور اس نے کس کو فائدہ یا نقصان پہنچایا؟ نقشے سے ایک وجہ بتائیں۔"},"hi":{"The First Transcontinental Railroad":"पहली अंतरमहाद्वीपीय रेलवे","Trace the ripples out from the 1869 golden spike: what caused the railroad, what happened right afterward, and what changed for years to come — for whom.":"1869 के सुनहरे कील से फैलती लहरों का पता लगाएँ: रेलवे किस कारण बनी, उसके ठीक बाद क्या हुआ, और आने वाले सालों में क्या बदला — और किसके लिए।","On May 10, 1869, two railroads met at Promontory Summit, Utah, and a golden spike joined the coasts by rail for the first time. A trip that once took months now took about a week. But every big change sends out ripples. What caused the railroad, what happened right afterward, and what changed later — and who was helped or hurt?":"10 मई 1869 को दो रेलमार्ग यूटा के प्रोमोंटरी समिट पर मिले, और एक सुनहरी कील ने पहली बार दोनों तटों को रेल से जोड़ दिया। जो यात्रा कभी महीनों लेती थी, अब लगभग एक सप्ताह में हो जाती थी। लेकिन हर बड़ा बदलाव लहरें फैलाता है। रेलवे किस कारण बनी, उसके ठीक बाद क्या हुआ, और बाद में क्या बदला — और किसे मदद मिली या किसे नुकसान हुआ?","The Golden Spike — the railroad joins the coasts":"सुनहरी कील — रेलवे दोनों तटों को जोड़ती है","Promontory Summit, Utah":"प्रोमोंटरी समिट, यूटा","Compare your ripples with a partner. Which effects did you both list? Which did only one of you find?":"अपनी लहरों की तुलना किसी साथी से करें। कौन-से प्रभाव आप दोनों ने लिखे? कौन-सा केवल आप में से एक ने खोजा?","Did you put any effect in a different ring (immediate vs. later) than your partner? Talk about why.":"क्या आपने कोई प्रभाव अपने साथी से अलग घेरे (तुरंत बनाम बाद में) में रखा? इसके कारण पर बात करें।","Choose the one result of the railroad you think mattered most. Use evidence from your ripples to explain who it helped and who it hurt.":"रेलवे का वह एक परिणाम चुनें जो आपके विचार में सबसे महत्वपूर्ण था। अपनी लहरों से साक्ष्य का उपयोग करके समझाएँ कि इसने किसे मदद पहुँचाई और किसे नुकसान।","Explain what the transcontinental railroad was and why it was built.":"समझाएँ कि अंतरमहाद्वीपीय रेलवे क्या थी और इसे क्यों बनाया गया।","Connect one cause of the railroad to one long-term change it created.":"रेलवे के एक कारण को उससे बने एक दीर्घकालिक बदलाव से जोड़ें।","Apply the idea of a big new technology sending out ripples to something today, like the internet. Name one good ripple and one hard ripple.":"किसी बड़ी नई तकनीक के लहरें फैलाने के विचार को आज की किसी चीज़ पर लागू करें, जैसे इंटरनेट। एक अच्छी लहर और एक कठिन लहर का नाम बताएँ।","Pacific Railway Act (1862) — National Archives":"पैसिफिक रेलवे अधिनियम (1862) — राष्ट्रीय अभिलेखागार","The 1862 law, signed by Lincoln, that funded the railroad with federal land and loans.":"1862 का कानून, जिस पर लिंकन ने हस्ताक्षर किए, जिसने संघीय भूमि और ऋणों से रेलवे को धन दिया।","What did the government give the railroad companies?":"सरकार ने रेलवे कंपनियों को क्या दिया?","Why would the government help pay for a railroad?":"सरकार रेलवे के लिए पैसे देने में मदद क्यों करेगी?","The Archeology of Chinese Laborers Who Connected the Country (National Park Service)":"देश को जोड़ने वाले चीनी मज़दूरों का पुरातत्व (राष्ट्रीय उद्यान सेवा)","How over 12,000 Chinese immigrant laborers built the Central Pacific line.":"कैसे 12,000 से अधिक चीनी प्रवासी मज़दूरों ने सेंट्रल पैसिफिक लाइन बनाई।","Who did much of the hardest building work?":"सबसे कठिन निर्माण कार्य का अधिकांश हिस्सा किसने किया?","Why might their story have been left out for so long?":"उनकी कहानी इतने लंबे समय तक क्यों छूट गई होगी?","Transcontinental Railroad — Railroads (Library of Congress)":"अंतरमहाद्वीपीय रेलवे — रेलवे (कांग्रेस पुस्तकालय)","Background and sources on how the two lines met at Promontory Summit.":"दोनों लाइनें प्रोमोंटरी समिट पर कैसे मिलीं, इस बारे में पृष्ठभूमि और स्रोत।","Where and when did the two lines meet?":"दोनों लाइनें कहाँ और कब मिलीं?","What changed about travel afterward?":"उसके बाद यात्रा में क्या बदला?","Congress passed the Pacific Railway Act (1862) to help pay for the tracks.":"कांग्रेस ने पटरियों के खर्च में मदद के लिए पैसिफिक रेलवे अधिनियम (1862) पारित किया।","People wanted a fast, safe way to connect the East and West coasts.":"लोग पूर्वी और पश्चिमी तटों को जोड़ने के लिए एक तेज़ और सुरक्षित तरीका चाहते थे।","Gold, land, and the chance to settle the West pulled people westward.":"सोना, ज़मीन और पश्चिम में बसने का अवसर लोगों को पश्चिम की ओर खींच लाया।","Trade and mail needed to move quickly across the whole country.":"व्यापार और डाक को पूरे देश में तेज़ी से पहुँचने की ज़रूरत थी।","The golden spike joined the two railroads into one line.":"सुनहरी कील ने दोनों रेलमार्गों को एक ही लाइन में जोड़ दिया।","Coast-to-coast travel dropped from months to about a week.":"एक तट से दूसरे तट तक की यात्रा महीनों से घटकर लगभग एक सप्ताह रह गई।","Goods, mail, and news moved much faster across the country.":"माल, डाक और समाचार पूरे देश में कहीं तेज़ी से पहुँचने लगे।","New towns and stops grew up along the tracks.":"पटरियों के साथ-साथ नए कस्बे और पड़ाव विकसित हुए।","Many more settlers moved west, and Western towns and farms grew.":"बहुत अधिक बसने वाले लोग पश्चिम की ओर गए, और पश्चिमी कस्बे और खेत बढ़े।","Native nations lost land and hunting grounds, and the bison were nearly wiped out.":"मूल राष्ट्रों ने अपनी ज़मीन और शिकार-भूमि खो दी, और बाइसन लगभग समाप्त हो गए।","Chinese and Irish immigrant workers shaped the country but faced unfair treatment and low pay.":"चीनी और आयरिश प्रवासी मज़दूरों ने देश को आकार दिया, पर उन्हें अन्यायपूर्ण व्यवहार और कम मज़दूरी झेलनी पड़ी।","The railroad tied the nation into one big trade network and sped up its growth.":"रेलवे ने देश को एक बड़े व्यापार नेटवर्क में बाँध दिया और इसकी वृद्धि को तेज़ किया।","The railroad companies — Central Pacific and Union Pacific":"रेलवे कंपनियाँ — सेंट्रल पैसिफिक और यूनियन पैसिफिक","Immigrant laborers — Chinese (Central Pacific) and Irish (Union Pacific)":"प्रवासी मज़दूर — चीनी (सेंट्रल पैसिफिक) और आयरिश (यूनियन पैसिफिक)","Native nations of the Plains and West":"मैदानों और पश्चिम के मूल राष्ट्र","Settlers, farmers, and traders moving into the West":"पश्चिम की ओर जाने वाले बसने वाले, किसान और व्यापारी","Look at all the ripples. Which result of the railroad do you think mattered most — and who did it help or hurt? Give one reason from the map.":"सभी लहरों को देखें। आपके विचार में रेलवे का कौन-सा परिणाम सबसे महत्वपूर्ण था — और इसने किसे मदद पहुँचाई या नुकसान? नक्शे से एक कारण बताएँ।"}}};
